'' ================================================================================================
''
''   File....... flash_fs.spin2
''   Purpose.... This object is the full flash file system driver for the P2 it manages all but the
''               first 512KB of the flash chip (where the boot image is stored) it provides a
''               standard (ANSI C like) file system interface to the flash chip
''   Author..... Chip Gracey
''   Contributions...... Jon McPhalen, Stephen M Moraco
''               -- see below for terms of use
''   E-mail..... stephen@ironsheep.biz
''   Started.... AUG 2023
''   Updated.... 25 NOV 2026
''
'' ================================================================================================
''
'' Reporting errors
'' ----------------
'' Every call sets error() for the calling cog, on every path it can take: SUCCESS, or the reason
'' the call failed. Each cog has its own error(), so a call made by another cog never changes what
'' your cog reads. The only calls that leave error() as it was are error(), string_for_error(),
'' null() and mounted().
''
'' A method whose valid results are never negative also returns the negative code in place of its
'' result. The @returns of each method names the return style it uses:
''   status         returns SUCCESS (0) or a negative code
''   value-or-code  returns a result that is never negative (a handle, size, position or byte), or
''                  the negative code in its place
''   count          returns the number of bytes transferred; when that is fewer than asked, error()
''                  holds why (0 bytes transferred returns 0)
''   count-or-code  returns the number of bytes transferred, or the negative code when none were
''   boolean        returns TRUE or FALSE; when FALSE is a failure and not an answer, error() holds
''                  why
''   value          returns a value that has no code: rd_long() returns 0 when it fails, so check
''                  error()
''   values         returns several results, none of them a code unless the method says so:
''                  serial_number() returns 0, 0 when it fails, so check error()
''
'' A handle that is in range but not open gives E_BAD_HANDLE from every method that takes a handle.
'' E_FILE_MODE means only a handle that is open in a mode the method does not serve.
''
'' A call that erases or programs the flash gives E_FLASH_TIMEOUT when the chip does not finish
'' in time. The filesystem is then unmounted and every handle is freed without a commit; each
'' later call gives E_NOT_MOUNTED until mount() or format() is called. Nothing on the flash is
'' undone: the next mount() recovers the flash as it would after a power loss.
''
'' mount(), format() and can_mount() check the configuration first, before they take the lock or
'' touch the flash: E_NO_HANDLE when MAX_FILES_OPEN is below 1, E_BAD_HANDLE when HANDLE_BASE
'' is not 0 or 1.
''
'' E_FILE_WRITING (-5), E_FILE_READING (-6) and E_SHORT_TRANSER (-16) are reserved: the driver never
'' returns them. Their values are kept so the numbering of the other codes does not change.
''
'' Constants
'' ---------
'' YES is 1, not TRUE (TRUE is -1, as ON is); NO is 0, as FALSE and OFF are.
''
'' Configuring the driver
'' ----------------------
'' A program overrides these constants on its OBJ line, for example:  OBJ fs : "flash_fs" |
'' MAX_FILES_OPEN = 4 The compiler checks none of the values.
'' -- MAX_FILES_OPEN: the number of files that can be open at one time, and so the number of
''    handles. The default is 2; any value of 1 or more is valid. Each handle takes 4264 bytes of
''    hub RAM.
'' -- HANDLE_BASE: the value of the first handle open() and open_circular() return, 0 or 1 (the
''    default is 0). The handles are HANDLE_BASE .. HANDLE_BASE + MAX_FILES_OPEN - 1, and every
''    method that takes a handle takes one of these.
'' -- FIRST_BLOCK and LAST_BLOCK: the first and last 4KB block of the flash the file system uses.
''    The defaults, $080 and $FFF, leave the first 512KB for the boot image. LAST_BLOCK -
''    FIRST_BLOCK + 1 can be no more than 4096 blocks.
'' -- Not constants to override: a file name is at most 127 characters, and the driver serves at
''    most 8 cogs at once.
''
'' Known limits
'' ------------
' -- A power loss part-way through moving a block leaves two blocks with one ID. mount() resolves that
'    pair by keeping the newer. It assumes no ID is held by more than two blocks.
'' -- A bit error in stored data can be carried silently into a new copy when the driver moves data
''    to wear-level the flash.
' -- When a block is moved to wear-level the flash, its data is copied with a new CRC computed over the
'    copy. The CRC of the block being moved is not checked first, so a bit error in it is copied.
'' -- Every call that reaches the flash takes over pins 58 to 61, the flash chip's pins, and does
''    not check whether another user of those pins (such as an SD card) holds them.
'' -- The driver is certified at a 320 MHz system clock, the clock every regression run uses. The
''    SPI timing has been verified up to 350 MHz.
''
'' Version history: see CHANGELOG.md
'' -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------


CON { version }

  LIB_VERSION = 210                                     ' 2.1.0

  ' ON is TRUE (-1) and OFF is 0; NO is FALSE (0) and YES is 1, not TRUE
  #true,  ON, OFF
  #false, NO, YES

  ' file open mode equivalents (the values match the %"r+", %"w+" value encodings!)
  ' for extended-mode use these constants when the %"..." syntax is not supported by your compiler
  FILEMODE_READ = $72                                   ' "r"
  FILEMODE_WRITE = $77                                  ' "w"
  FILEMODE_APPEND = $61                                 ' "a"
  FILEMODE_READ_EXTENDED = $2B72                        ' "r+"
  FILEMODE_WRITE_EXTENDED = $2B77                       ' "w+"

CON { fixed io pins }

  PGM_RX   = 63  { I }                                  ' programming / debug
  PGM_TX   = 62  { O }

  SF_CS    = 61  { O }                                  ' flash chip select
  SF_SCLK  = 60  { O }                                  ' flash clock
  SF_MOSI  = 59  { O }                                  ' flash data in
  SF_MISO  = 58  { I }                                  ' flash data out

  LED2     = 57  { O }                                  ' Eval and Edge LEDs
  LED1     = 56  { O }


CON { PUBLIC driver constants }

  ' Return Codes

  OKAY             = 0                                  ' No error / Success
  SUCCESS          = OKAY                               ' No error / Success

' SK_* ENUM values (parameter to seek() method)
' SK_FILE_START: seek using position from start of file
' SK_CURRENT_POSN: seek where position is relative to current seek location in file
  #0, SK_Unknown, SK_FILE_START, SK_CURRENT_POSN

  E_BAD_HANDLE     = -1                                         ' Error: Handle in invalid
  E_NO_HANDLE      = -2                                         ' Error: Out of available handles
  E_FILE_NOT_FOUND = -3                                         ' Error: File not present
  E_DRIVE_FULL     = -4                                         ' Error: Out of space on flash chip
  E_FILE_WRITING   = -5                                         ' Error: File is open for writing (reserved: the driver never returns it)
  E_FILE_READING   = -6                                         ' Error: File is open for reading (reserved: the driver never returns it)
  E_FILE_OPEN      = -7                                         ' Error: File is open
  E_FILE_EXISTS    = -8                                         ' Error: the File exists
  E_END_OF_FILE    = -9                                         ' Error: no more data available, at end of file
  E_FILE_MODE      = -10                                        ' Error: file not opened in desired mode
  E_FILE_SEEK      = -11                                        ' Error: Attempted seek past either end of file
  E_BAD_BLOCKS_REMOVED = -12                                    ' Error: Block bit failure detetected, bad blocks removed
  E_NO_LOCK_AVAIL  = -13                                        ' Error: Unable to obtain a LOCK for driver use
  E_TRUNCATED_STRING = -14                                      ' Error: Buffer full, before reaching string terminator
  E_INCOMPLETE_STRING = -15                                     ' Error: End of file reached before string terminator
  E_SHORT_TRANSER = -16                                         ' Error: Too few bytes read or written (reserved: the driver never returns it)
  E_NOT_MOUNTED = -17                                           ' Error: Filesystem NOT mounted (not yet accessible)
  E_BAD_FILE_LENGTH = -18                                       ' Error: File length given is negative or zero
  E_BAD_SEEK_ARG = -19                                          ' Error: Invalid seek argument
  E_BAD_FILENAME = -20                                          ' Error: Filename is a null pointer, empty or longer than 127 characters
  E_FLASH_TIMEOUT = -21                                         ' Error: Flash chip did not finish an erase or program in time, filesystem unmounted

  BYTES_IN_HEAD_BLOCK = 3956                                    ' first block in file contains 3956 bytes, 140 bytes overhead
  WORDS_IN_HEAD_BLOCK = BYTES_IN_HEAD_BLOCK/2
  LONGS_IN_HEAD_BLOCK = BYTES_IN_HEAD_BLOCK/4

  BYTES_IN_BODY_BLOCK = 4088                                    ' all other blocks in file contain 4088 bytes, 8 bytes overhead
  WORD_IN_BODY_BLOCK = BYTES_IN_BODY_BLOCK/2
  LONGS_IN_BODY_BLOCK = BYTES_IN_BODY_BLOCK/4

CON { PRIVATE driver constants }

  ' optionally customizable
  '
  ' A program overrides one of these constants in its OBJ line, for example: OBJ fs : "flash_fs" | MAX_FILES_OPEN = 4
  ' The compiler checks none of the values: mount(), format() and can_mount() check MAX_FILES_OPEN and HANDLE_BASE when
  ' they run, and each fails before it takes the lock or touches the flash when either is invalid.
  '
  ' MAX_FILES_OPEN - the number of files that can be open at one time, and so the number of handles
  '   default 2; valid values are 1 or more
  '   below 1, mount(), format() and can_mount() report E_NO_HANDLE
  '   each handle takes 4264 bytes of hub RAM: the growth of the driver's DAT for one more handle, from the
  '   pnut-ts v1.55.12 listing (pnut-ts -l) of the driver compiled with MAX_FILES_OPEN 2 and 3
  '
  ' HANDLE_BASE - the value of the first handle open() and open_circular() return: 0 or 1
  '   the handles are HANDLE_BASE .. HANDLE_BASE + MAX_FILES_OPEN - 1, and every method that takes a handle takes one of these
  '   a program that counts handles from 1 overrides it: OBJ fs : "flash_fs" | HANDLE_BASE = 1
  '   any other value makes mount(), format() and can_mount() report E_BAD_HANDLE
  '
  ' FIRST_BLOCK and LAST_BLOCK - the first and last block of the flash this file system uses
  '   a block ID is a 12-bit field in the block header (ThisID, bits 19..8, and NextID, bits 31..20), and the ID-to-block
  '   table holds 12-bit entries, so BLOCKS (LAST_BLOCK - FIRST_BLOCK + 1) can be no more than 4096
  '
  ' Limits that are not constants to override:
  '   a file name is at most 127 characters, and FILENAME_SIZE holds it with its zero terminator
  '   the driver serves at most 8 cogs at once: errorCode and fsCogCts hold one entry for each cog

  FIRST_BLOCK      = $080                                       ' Physical address of first block in this flash file system
  LAST_BLOCK       = $FFF                                       ' Physical address of last block in this flash file system
  MAX_FILES_OPEN   = 2                                          ' Maximum number of files that can be open at one time
  HANDLE_BASE      = 0                                          ' Value of the first handle: 0 or 1

  ' NOT customizable! below here
  BLOCKS          = LAST_BLOCK - FIRST_BLOCK+1                 ' Number of blocks in flash allocated to this file system

  BLOCK_SIZE       = $1000                                      ' Size in bytes: 4KB block (4096 bytes)
  BLOCK_SIZE_EXP   = encod BLOCK_SIZE

  ADDR_HEAD_FN_CRC  = $004                                      ' Offset in head block of filename CRC
  ADDR_HEAD_SONAME  = $008                                      ' Offset in head block of first filename byte
  ADDR_HEAD_DATA    = $088                                      ' Offset in head block of first data byte
  ADDR_BODY_DATA    = $004                                      ' Offset in body block of first data byte
  ADDR_DATA_END     = BLOCK_SIZE - 4                            ' Offset in any block of its CRC: the data area ends just before it
  ' The largest data offset a trim gives a head block that has a next block: the trim makes the block before the
  ' data block the head when the data starts at or before ADDR_HEAD_DATA in the data block, so the offset skips the
  ' head's whole data area and up to ADDR_HEAD_DATA - ADDR_BODY_DATA bytes of the next block
  MAX_HEAD_DATA_OFFSET = BYTES_IN_HEAD_BLOCK + ADDR_HEAD_DATA - ADDR_BODY_DATA

  FILENAME_SIZE    = $088-$008                                  ' File name string length: 127 characters plus 0 terminator
  FILENAME_SIZE_EXP   = encod FILENAME_SIZE

  ID_TO_BLOCKS_SZ  = (BLOCKS * 12 + 15) / 16                    ' 12-bit fields in WORD array (rounded to full WORD)
  FLAGS_SIZE       = (BLOCKS * 1 + 7) / 8                       ' 1-bit fields in BYTE array (rounded to full BYTE)
  STATES_SIZE      = (BLOCKS * 2 + 7) / 8                       ' 2-bit fields in BYTE array (rounded to full BYTE)


  B_FREE           = %00                                        ' Block is not in use (free)
  B_TEMP           = %01                                        ' Block is being put to use
  B_HEAD           = %10                                        ' Block is head of a file (contains filename)
  B_BODY           = %11                                        ' BLock is body of file (any blocks after head)

  H_READ           = %0001                                       ' Existing file is being read
  H_WRITE          = %0010                                       ' New file is being written
  H_FORK           = %0100                                       ' Existing file is being written and forked at some block (rewrite/append)
  H_MODIFY         = %1000                                       ' Existing file is being modified

  H_APPEND = H_WRITE | H_FORK                                    ' New file is being written or existing is being rewritten
  H_READWRITE = H_WRITE | H_MODIFY                               ' New file is being written or existing is being rewritten

  H_READ_WRITE     = H_READ | H_WRITE                           ' (Any) File is open for reading and/or writing
  H_READ_ONLY      = H_READ                                     ' Existing File is open for reading only

  NEXT_BLOCK_SPARE = 1                                          ' free blocks a written block that has a next block leaves for it
  ONE_FREE_BLOCK   = 1                                          ' free blocks an allocation takes, and an open for writing or a rename needs at least
  RANDOM_PICK_TRIES = 64                                        ' random tries an allocation makes for a block that is not B_TEMP before it scans every block
  MIN_FILES_OPEN = 1                                            ' fewest handles a driver that can open a file has
  MIN_HANDLE_BASE = 0                                           ' lowest value HANDLE_BASE may take
  MAX_HANDLE_BASE = 1                                           ' highest value HANDLE_BASE may take

  ID_FLAGS_PER_BYTE = 8                                         ' block IDs whose valid flags one byte of IDValids holds
  ID_FLAGS_ALL_USED = $FF                                       ' a byte of IDValids whose block IDs are all in use

  NO_CACHED_BLOCK  = BLOCKS                                     ' the seek cache of a handle that holds no block: block IDs run 0..BLOCKS-1
  NO_STOP_BLOCK    = BLOCKS                                     ' the stop block of a chain walk that stops at no block: block IDs run 0..BLOCKS-1

  ' the upper-case spellings of the extended open modes, packed as %"R+" and %"W+" pack
  FILEMODE_READ_EXTENDED_UC = $2B52                             ' "R+", the same mode as FILEMODE_READ_EXTENDED
  FILEMODE_WRITE_EXTENDED_UC = $2B57                            ' "W+", the same mode as FILEMODE_WRITE_EXTENDED

  NOT_ENABLED      = -1                                         ' this feature is NOT enabled (e.g., seeking)
  NOT_VALID        = -30                                        ' this value is not initialized

  ' The states of the election that decides which cog creates the driver's lock (fsElection):
  '  ELECT_NONE       - no cog is creating the lock; while fsLock is -1 a caller may enter the election
  '  ELECT_ALLOCATING - the cog that won the election is asking the hub for a lock
  '  ELECT_FAILED     - the winning cog found no free hub lock; the next caller resets the state and elects again
  #0, ELECT_NONE, ELECT_ALLOCATING, ELECT_FAILED

  ELECT_ENTRIES    = 8                                          ' entries of the election, one for each cog
  ELECT_UNSET      = POSX                                       ' the entry of a cog that is not in the election
  ELECT_WAIT_MS    = 10                                         ' time a cog waits, after it enters, for other cogs to enter

  ' The longest a flash wait lets the chip stay busy before it reports a timeout. The W25Q128JV datasheet
  ' (DOCs/W25Q128JV-210823.pdf, AC Electrical Characteristics, page 65) gives Sector Erase Time (4KB) tSE as
  ' 45 ms typical and 400 ms maximum, and Page Program Time tPP as 0.4 ms typical and 3 ms maximum, so a
  ' working chip always finishes well inside this bound. In system clock ticks it is below 2^31 at any
  ' clock the P2 runs at (350_000_000 ticks at 350 MHz), so the signed elapsed-tick compare holds.
  FLASH_TIMEOUT_MS = 1000                                       ' bound on one flash erase or program wait, in milliseconds
  MS_PER_SECOND    = 1000                                       ' clkfreq / MS_PER_SECOND is the system clock ticks in one millisecond

  ' The values of the flash fault countdown (fsFaultCountdown) with a meaning of their own:
  '  FAULT_OFF       - no fault is injected: every flash wait polls the chip
  '  FAULT_THIS_WAIT - the flash wait that finds this value reports a timeout without polling the chip
  FAULT_OFF        = 0
  FAULT_THIS_WAIT  = 1

DAT { pre-initialized: driver state tracking tables }

'-------+-----+---------+-------+---------------+-------+-----------------------+
errorCode     LONG      0[8]                                                    'most recent error code
fsLock        LONG      -1                                                      'flash lock semaphore for driver use, kept for the life of the run once created
fsElection    LONG      ELECT_NONE                                              'state of the election that creates fsLock: ELECT_NONE, ELECT_ALLOCATING or ELECT_FAILED
fsFreeHndlCt  LONG      MAX_FILES_OPEN
fsCogCts      LONG      ELECT_UNSET[ELECT_ENTRIES]                              'cog counts: one for each cog that is attempting to start the filesystem
showRTdebug   LONG      false
fsMounted     LONG      false                                                   ' T/F where T means the filesystem is mounted
fsDeviceFault LONG      false                                                   ' T/F where T means a flash wait timed out or a block program was refused; every block program is refused until it is cleared
fsFlashWaitMs LONG      FLASH_TIMEOUT_MS                                        'the longest one flash wait lets the chip stay busy, in milliseconds
fsFaultCountdown LONG   FAULT_OFF                                               'FAULT_OFF in normal operation; else counts flash waits down to the one that reports a timeout

' physically: 3/4 of a word (12 bits) for every valid block ID, 12 bits per ID
' logically: a "BLOCKS"-sized array of 12-bit variables, 1 for ea. block ID - indexed by block ID
' contains block_address in ea. 12 bit field
IDToBlocks    WORD      0[ID_TO_BLOCKS_SZ]                                      'ID-to-block translation table
IDToBlock     LONG      0                                                       '(field pointer to 12-bit variables)

' physically: 1 byte for every 8 valid block IDs, 1 bit per block ID
' logically: a "BLOCKS"-sized array of single bit variables, 1 for ea. block ID - indexed by block ID
' contains [0,1] in ea. 1 bit field, where 1 means ID is valid
IDValids      BYTE      0[FLAGS_SIZE]                                           'ID-valid flags
IDValid       LONG      0                                                       '(field pointer to 1-bit variables)

' physically: 1 byte for every 4 valid block IDs, 2 bits per block ID
' logically: a "BLOCKS"-sized array of 2-bit variables, 1 for ea. block ID - indexed by block ID
' contains a Block-State value in ea. 2 bit field [B_FREE, B_TEMP, B_HEAD, B_BODY]
BlockStates   BYTE      0[STATES_SIZE]                                          'block states
BlockState    LONG      0                                                       '(field pointer to 2-bit variables)

' handle-related variables and buffers
'   handle is index into each of the arrays below

hStatus         BYTE    0[MAX_FILES_OPEN]                                       'handle: open mode bits, a combination of H_READ, H_WRITE, H_FORK and H_MODIFY
hHeadBlockID    WORD    NOT_VALID[MAX_FILES_OPEN]                               'handle: first blockID of file chain
hChainBlockID   WORD    0[MAX_FILES_OPEN]                                       'handle: first blockID of commit chain
hChainBlockAddr WORD    0[MAX_FILES_OPEN]                                       'handle: first block_address of commit chain
hChainLifeCycle BYTE    0[MAX_FILES_OPEN]                                       'handle: first block lifecycle (cycle value for replacement first block of chain)
hModified       BYTE    0[MAX_FILES_OPEN]                                       'handle: current block is modified
hEndPtr         WORD    0[MAX_FILES_OPEN]                                       'handle: pointer to next byte in block
hSeekPtr        LONG    NOT_ENABLED[MAX_FILES_OPEN]                             'handle: seek endptr within file
hSeekFileOffset LONG    0[MAX_FILES_OPEN]                                       'handle: seek offset within entire file
hCircularLength LONG    0[MAX_FILES_OPEN]                                       'handle: circular buffer length in byt
hHeadPending    BYTE    0[MAX_FILES_OPEN]                                       'handle: TRUE while the head block of a "w+" file is not yet active on the flash
hTrimPending    BYTE    0[MAX_FILES_OPEN]                                       'handle: TRUE while a committed circular file is over its limit because its trim found no free block
hWindowStart    LONG    0[MAX_FILES_OPEN]                                       'handle: file offset of the first byte of an old-format circular read, 0 for every other handle; seek positions count from it
hReplacedID     LONG    NOT_VALID[MAX_FILES_OPEN]                             'handle: head block ID of the existing file this handle replaces at close, or NOT_VALID
' the seek cache: a block of the file the last locate of the handle found (a seek, or a size that counts the handle's
' bytes), so the next one walks the chain on from it, and the format of the file's head block. It names the block by
' ID, which a block keeps when it moves, and it is emptied whenever the chain can lose a block or change its head
' (open, close, flush commit, mount)
hCacheBlockID   WORD    NO_CACHED_BLOCK[MAX_FILES_OPEN]                         'handle: ID of the block the last locate found, or NO_CACHED_BLOCK when the cache is empty
hCacheStart     LONG    0[MAX_FILES_OPEN]                                       'handle: file offset of the first data byte position of that block (negative for a head block with a data offset)
hCacheOldFmt    BYTE    0[MAX_FILES_OPEN]                                       'handle: TRUE when the file's head block is old format (CRC32 filename CRC, no data offset); valid while the cache holds a block
hFilename       BYTE    0[MAX_FILES_OPEN * FILENAME_SIZE]                       'handle: FILENAME_SIZE byte buffer for filename
hBlockBuff      BYTE    0[MAX_FILES_OPEN * BLOCK_SIZE]                          'handle: 4KB buffer for file data

tmpBlockBuffer  BYTE     0[BLOCK_SIZE]                                          'buffer used for copying blocks

' FALSE in normal operation. While TRUE, the next create_file() skips its free-ID and free-block checks;
' create_file() clears it on entry, so it covers one call. Only a regression-test method sets it.
fsSkipCreateChecks LONG  false

' NOT_ENABLED in normal operation. Otherwise a block address that next_block_address() takes, in place of a
' random pick, whenever that block is not B_TEMP; the name is cleared when the block is moved to a free block.
' Only a regression-test method sets it.
fsTargetBlock   LONG    NOT_ENABLED

VAR ' ---- per-instance state ----

  ' count of block programs refused for a block address outside 0..BLOCKS-1; per object instance (VAR, not DAT)
  ' so it lies outside the DAT tables above, and it is incremented only when a program is refused
  LONG fsRefusedBlocks


CON ' --- Public Methods ---

PUB null()

'' This is not an application
'' -- (invoke format() or mount() to use the flash file system)
'' -- does not change error()

PUB version() : result | status

'' Returns flash file system library version as integer
'' -- e.g., version 120 is 1.2.0 (major, minor, bugfix)
'' -- sets error() to SUCCESS
''
'' @returns result - return style value: the library version, as an integer

' Local Variables:
' @local status - SUCCESS, which version() leaves in error()

  status := SUCCESS
  result := LIB_VERSION
  LONG[@errorCode][cogid()] := status                                           'every path leaves its status in error() for this cog

{$flexspin
VAR
   long m_sn_hi, m_sn_lo        ' temporary storage for serial number read
}

PUB serial_number() : sn_hi, sn_lo | status

'' Returns 64-bit unique id of flash chip
''
'' @returns sn_hi - return style values: high 32 bits of 64-bit unique id of flash chip (0 when
'' .. error return)
'' @returns sn_lo - low 32 bits of 64-bit unique id of flash chip (0 when error return)
'' (sets error() to SUCCESS, or to E_NOT_MOUNTED and returns 0,0 if filesystem has not been mounted)

' Local Variables:
' @local status - SUCCESS, or the reason no id was read

  sn_hi := sn_lo := 0                                                           'the id returned when the filesystem is not mounted
  ifnot fsMounted
    status := E_NOT_MOUNTED
  else

    repeat while locktry(fsLock) == 0                                           ' lock for exlusive use

    ifnot fsMounted                                                             'unmount() may have run while this cog waited for the lock
      status := E_NOT_MOUNTED
    else
      status := SUCCESS

      flash_command($4B, 1)
      flash_send($00, 4)
{$flexspin
#ifdef __FLEXSPIN__
      ' flexspin does not like using HUB variables (@) in inline assembly
      ' so do the read into a class member in HUB, then copy to the local
      ' variables in registers
      flash_receive(@m_sn_hi, 8)
      sn_hi := m_sn_hi
      sn_lo := m_sn_lo
#else
}
      flash_receive(@sn_hi, 8)
{$flexspin #endif}

      ' UID values are stored Big Endian
      ' -- swap ends to correct LE reads from flash

      org
                movbyts     sn_hi, #%%0123
                movbyts     sn_lo, #%%0123
      end

    status := release_lock(status)                                              ' release the lock, we're done with it

  LONG[@errorCode][cogid()] := status                                           'every path leaves its status in error() for this cog

PUB format() : status | block_address, cycleBits

'' Format the file system blocks and (re)mount it
'' -- while format() runs, a call from another cog finds either E_NOT_MOUNTED or the formatted
''    filesystem fully mounted
' -- the lock is held from before the first block is cancelled until the filesystem is mounted again
'' -- every file that is open is abandoned: every handle is freed, and the data a handle holds that
''    was not written to the flash is lost
''
'' @returns status - return style status: 0 (SUCCESS) if successful,
'' .. E_BAD_BLOCKS_REMOVED if BAD blocks were found and fixed,
'' .. E_NO_LOCK_AVAIL if all 16 LOCKs are in use,
'' .. E_FLASH_TIMEOUT if the flash chip did not finish an erase or program in time: the filesystem
''    is left unmounted and is not mounted again, and the next mount() or format() starts over,
'' .. E_NO_HANDLE if MAX_FILES_OPEN is below 1, E_BAD_HANDLE if HANDLE_BASE is not 0 or 1: no
''    block is changed

' Local Variables:
' @local block_address - the block offset within the file system
' @local cycleBits - lifeCycle bit-pattern found in block

  'debug("* format()")
    status := configuration_status()                                            ' SUCCESS, or the reason the driver cannot run as configured
    if status == SUCCESS and fsLock == -1                                       ' no cog has created the lock yet
        status := setup_semaphore()                                             ' E_NO_LOCK_AVAIL if no hub lock was free

    if status == SUCCESS
        'debug("- have lock, trying...")
        repeat while locktry(fsLock) == 0                                       ' lock for exlusive use

        fsMounted := false                                                     ' every call that takes the lock until the mount below finds the filesystem not mounted
        bytefill(@hStatus, 0, MAX_FILES_OPEN)                                   ' every handle is freed, any open handle is abandoned
        fsFreeHndlCt := MAX_FILES_OPEN

        status := clear_device_fault()                                          ' wait out any erase or program a failed flash wait left running

        'debug("- formatting...")
        if status == SUCCESS
            repeat BLOCKS with block_address                                    'cancel all active blocks
                flash_read_block_addr(block_address, @cycleBits, $000, $000)
                'if block_address // 128 == 0
                '  debug(" -- block ", uhex_word_(block_address),", cycle...", ubin_byte(cycleBits))
                if lookdown(cycleBits.[7..5] : %011, %101, %110)
                    'debug(" -- clearing...")
                    flash_cancel_block(block_address)
                    if fsDeviceFault                                            ' the flash failed: no further block is cancelled
                        quit

            'debug("- formatting done")
            if fsDeviceFault                                                    ' a failed cancel leaves the filesystem unmounted
                status := E_FLASH_TIMEOUT
            else
                status := mount_no_lock()                                       '(re)mount flash while still holding the lock

        status := release_lock(status)                                          ' release the lock, we're done with it
        'debug("- lock released")

    LONG[@errorCode][cogid()] := status                                         'every path leaves its status in error() for this cog


PUB mount() : status

'' Mount the filesystem so it is ready to use
' -- the mount scans all blocks and initializes the internal tables and buffers
'' -- the first mount() of the run creates the driver's lock, which is then kept until reset or
''    power-off
'' -- mounted() becomes TRUE only once the mount has finished
'' -- a filesystem that is already mounted is left as it is: its files stay open and the call
''    returns SUCCESS
'' -- a mount of an unmounted filesystem frees every handle
'' -- damage a power loss or a flash error left is repaired: damaged data is removed, a file that
''    used it is removed, and E_BAD_BLOCKS_REMOVED is returned
' -- a bad block is cancelled: a block whose CRC does not match, one whose block IDs, end pointer or data
'    offset are out of range, or one that no file reaches. A file whose chain runs through a block that was
'    cancelled, or names a block that cannot exist, is removed
''
'' @returns status - return style status: E_BAD_BLOCKS_REMOVED if BAD blocks were found and
'' .. fixed,
'' .. E_NO_LOCK_AVAIL if all 16 LOCKs are in use,
'' .. E_FLASH_TIMEOUT if the flash chip did not finish an erase or program in time (the filesystem
''    stays unmounted),
'' .. E_NO_HANDLE if MAX_FILES_OPEN is below 1, E_BAD_HANDLE if HANDLE_BASE is not 0 or 1 (nothing
''    is mounted),
'' .. otherwise 0 for success

    status := configuration_status()                                            ' SUCCESS, or the reason the driver cannot run as configured
    if status == SUCCESS and not fsMounted                                      ' don't mount if already mounted
        if fsLock == -1                                                         ' no cog has created the lock yet
            status := setup_semaphore()                                         ' E_NO_LOCK_AVAIL if no hub lock was free

        if status == SUCCESS
            'debug("* mount()")
            repeat while locktry(fsLock) == 0                                   ' lock for exlusive use

            ifnot fsMounted                                                     ' another cog may have mounted while this one waited for the lock
                status := clear_device_fault()                                  ' wait out any erase or program a failed flash wait left running
                if status == SUCCESS
                    status := mount_no_lock()

            status := release_lock(status)                                      ' release the lock, we're done with it
            'debug("- lock released")

    LONG[@errorCode][cogid()] := status                                         'every path leaves its status in error() for this cog


PUB can_mount() : bool | status, block_address, signature, BYTE blockTypeBits, dupeIdCount, fileCount, badBlockCount, bad_count, dupe_count

'' Check entire flash - to see if it would mount without modifying any blocks
''
'' -- a filesystem that is already mounted would not be changed, so the answer is True
'' -- the answer is False and error() holds E_BAD_BLOCKS_REMOVED when mount() would remove damaged
''    data
'' -- the answer is False and error() holds SUCCESS when mount() would only tidy up a move that a
''    power loss interrupted; that mount reports SUCCESS
' -- a bad block is a block a mount would cancel: one whose CRC does not match, one whose block IDs, end pointer
'    or data offset are out of range, or one that no file reaches (a dead block)
' -- a duplicate block ID alone gives False with error() SUCCESS: a mount would resolve it, keeping the newer
'    block and cancelling the older
'' -- the answer is True and error() holds SUCCESS when a mount would change nothing
'' -- the answer is False, and no check is made, when the check could not be made: error() holds
''    E_NO_LOCK_AVAIL when no lock could be created, E_FLASH_TIMEOUT when the flash chip stayed
''    busy past the bound of a flash wait, E_NO_HANDLE when MAX_FILES_OPEN is below 1, or
''    E_BAD_HANDLE when HANDLE_BASE is not 0 or 1
''
'' @returns bool - return style boolean: True/False where True means mount() would change nothing:
'' .. False when mount() would change something, or when the check could not be made

' Local Variables:
' @local status - SUCCESS, E_BAD_BLOCKS_REMOVED when a mount would cancel a block, or the reason the check was not made
' @local block_address - the block offset within the file system
' @local signature - temporary block state bits
' @local blockTypeBits - temporary block type bits
' @local dupeIdCount - count of duplicate ID blocks found
' @local fileCount - count of files found
' @local badBlockCount - count of bad blocks found
' @local bad_count - count of bad blocks found
' @local dupe_count - count of duplicate ID blocks found at one block

    status := configuration_status()                                            ' SUCCESS, or the reason the driver cannot run as configured
    bool := status == SUCCESS                                                   ' a mounted filesystem would not be changed by a mount; a driver that cannot run as configured makes no check
    if status == SUCCESS and not fsMounted
        bool := FALSE                                                           ' with no lock the check cannot be made
        if fsLock == -1                                                         ' no cog has created the lock yet
            status := setup_semaphore()                                         ' E_NO_LOCK_AVAIL if no hub lock was free

        if status == SUCCESS
            'debug("- have lock, trying...")
            repeat while locktry(fsLock) == 0                                   ' lock for exlusive use

            ifnot fsMounted                                                     ' a chip still busy with an erase or program ignores reads: wait for it
                status := flash_wait()

            if status <> SUCCESS                                                ' the chip was still busy at the bound: no check is made
                bool := FALSE
            elseifnot fsMounted                                                 ' another cog may have mounted while this one waited for the lock
                'debug("* mntCk: can_mount()?")
                badBlockCount := dupeIdCount := fileCount := 0

                'debug("- mounting...")
                bytefill(@hStatus, 0, MAX_FILES_OPEN)                           'clear handles

                wordfill(@IDToBlocks, 0, ID_TO_BLOCKS_SZ)                       'clear ID-to-block translation table
                bytefill(@IDValids, 0, FLAGS_SIZE)                              'clear ID flags
                bytefill(@BlockStates, 0, STATES_SIZE)                          'clear block states to B_FREE

                IDToBlock  := ^@IDToBlocks.[11..0]                              'set field pointers
                IDValid    := ^@IDValids.[0]
                BlockState := ^@BlockStates.[1..0]

                'debug("mntCk: - fixing power-out leftovers...")
                repeat BLOCKS with block_address                                'check each block and fix any duplicate IDs
                    bad_count, dupe_count := check_block_read_only(block_address)
                    badBlockCount += bad_count
                    dupeIdCount += dupe_count

                'debug("mntCk: - locating files...")
                repeat BLOCKS with block_address                                'trace head blocks and cancel any broken files
                    if field[BlockState][block_address] == B_TEMP               'is this a valid block?
                        flash_read_block_addr(block_address, @blockTypeBits, $000, $000) 'yes, read first byte of block
                        ifnot blockTypeBits.[1]                                 'is this a head block?
                            'debug("mnt: - head block ", uhex_word(block_address))
                            ifnot trace_file_set_flags(block_address, true)     'yes, trace file, set block states to B_HEAD/B_BODY
                                trace_file_set_flags(block_address, false)      'if error, retrace file, return block states to B_TEMP
                            else
                                fileCount++

                'debug("mntCk: - clearing dead blocks...")
                repeat BLOCKS with block_address                                'cancel sTEMP blocks that didn't become sHEAD/sBODY blocks
                    if field[BlockState][block_address] == B_TEMP               'is this an B_TEMP block?
                        flash_read_block_addr(block_address, @signature, $000, $003) 'if so, read first long of block to get ID
                        field[IDValid][signature.[19..8]]~                      '..cancel ID flag (bit := 0): the first pass made only a block whose ID is in range B_TEMP
                        field[BlockState][block_address] := B_FREE              '..return block state to B_FREE
                        badBlockCount++                                         '..would cancel block to inhibit future CRC checks
                        'debug(" -- found dead block...")

                'debug("mntCk: - mount test done")
                bool := badBlockCount == 0 and dupeIdCount == 0                 'a duplicate ID is resolved by cancelling a block, so a mount would change one
                if badBlockCount > 0
                    status := E_BAD_BLOCKS_REMOVED                              'mount() reports a cancelled bad block, and not a cancelled duplicate
                'debug("mntCk: - ", udec(badBlockCount, dupeIdCount, fileCount))

            else
                bool := TRUE                                                    'another cog mounted while this one waited: a mount would change nothing

            status := release_lock(status)                                      ' release the lock, we're done with it
            'debug("- lock released")

    LONG[@errorCode][cogid()] := status                                         'every path leaves its status in error() for this cog


PUB mounted() : bool

'' Returns the mounted status of the filesystem
' -- (saves us from having to find creative ways to get an error code telling us this)
'' -- does not change error()
''
'' @returns bool - return style boolean: True/False where True means the filesystem has already been
'' .. successfully mounted

  bool := fsMounted


PUB unmount() : status | handle, tmpStatus

'' Prepare for shutdown / power-off by closing any open files
'' -- (no further access allowed until a subsequent mount())
'' -- every file open for writing is committed before its handle is freed
'' -- the first close that fails is the status returned, and every handle is still closed: a file
''    that could not be committed for lack of a free block is closed without the data it had not
''    written
'' -- the driver's lock is kept for the next mount(); a call another cog makes meanwhile returns
''    E_NOT_MOUNTED
''
'' @returns status - return style status: 0 (SUCCESS) if successful,
'' .. E_NOT_MOUNTED if filesystem had not been mounted,
'' .. E_DRIVE_FULL if a file could not be committed, trimmed or rewritten for lack of a free block,
'' .. E_FLASH_TIMEOUT if the flash chip did not finish a write in time: the commits stop at that
''    file, every handle is freed, the data of every file not yet committed is lost, and the next
''    mount() recovers the flash as it would after a power loss

' Local Variables:
' @local handle - temporary handle to use when closing files
' @local tmpStatus - what closing one handle returned

  ifnot fsMounted
    status := E_NOT_MOUNTED
  else
    repeat while locktry(fsLock) == 0                                           ' lock for exlusive use

    ifnot fsMounted                                                             'another cog's unmount() ran while this cog waited for the lock
      status := E_NOT_MOUNTED
    else
      status := SUCCESS

      'debug("* unmount()")
      repeat MAX_FILES_OPEN with handle                                         ' for each handle
        if hStatus[handle]                                                      ' if handle is open...
          tmpStatus := close_no_lock(handle, TRUE)                              ' ..commit it while its mode is still set
          if tmpStatus < 0 and status == SUCCESS
            status := tmpStatus                                                 ' the first failure of a close is kept, every handle is still closed
          if fsDeviceFault                                                      ' ..the flash failed: no further file is committed
            quit
          hStatus[handle]~                                                      ' ..then free it
          hCircularLength[handle] := 0                                          'clear prior length

      if fsDeviceFault == FALSE                                                 ' after a flash failure the release below unmounts
        fsFreeHndlCt := MAX_FILES_OPEN
        fsMounted := false                                                      ' clear "mounted" indication

    status := release_lock(status)                                              ' release the lock, it is kept for the next mount()

  LONG[@errorCode][cogid()] := status                                           'every path leaves its status in error() for this cog



PUB error() : status

'' Returns the error code from most recent operation the calling cog made
'' -- every filesystem call sets error() for the calling cog, on every path it can take: SUCCESS, or
''    the reason it failed; each cog has its own error()
'' -- error(), string_for_error(), null() and mounted() leave it as it was, so reading it never
''    loses a code
''
'' @returns status - return style value: latest error code (SUCCESS, for no error)

  status := LONG[@errorCode][cogid()]


PUB open(p_filename, mode) : handle | status, bFileExists, signature

'' Open file in mode; return handle (HANDLE_BASE..HANDLE_BASE+MAX_FILES_OPEN-1) if successful
''
'' A file with no contents does not exist: the flash keeps no empty file and no empty name, where C
'' would leave a zero-length file. An existing file that a "w" or "w+" open replaces is left
'' untouched until the handle is closed. Closed with no write, a "w" or "w+" open of an existing
'' file DELETES it: close() still returns SUCCESS and error() is SUCCESS, so use exists() to
'' confirm. This and the other differences from C are in the "Differences from ANSI C" table of
'' README.md.
''
'' @param p_filename - address of a zstring containing the filename
'' @param mode - the mode in which to open the file, what each does with a file that exists or not:
'' -- mode "r", "R" reads. The file must exist (E_FILE_NOT_FOUND). Closing changes nothing.
'' -- mode "w", "W" writes. A new file holds what was written when closed, or no file is left if
''    nothing was written. An existing file is replaced by what was written when closed, or deleted
''    if nothing was written.
'' -- mode "a", "A" appends. A new file is made as "w" makes it. An existing file holds its old
''    contents plus what was appended when closed, and is unchanged if nothing was appended.
'' -- mode "r+", "R+" reads, seeks and modifies within an existing file, and extends it at its end
''    with no gap. The file must exist (E_FILE_NOT_FOUND). It is modified in place, and
''    unchanged if nothing was written.
'' -- mode "w+", "W+" is "w" with reading, seeking and rewriting within the new file: an existing
''    file is replaced by what was written when closed, or deleted if nothing was written.
'' -- any other mode, such as "a+", is E_FILE_MODE
'' @returns handle - return style value-or-code: handle to open file if successful,
'' .. E_NOT_MOUNTED if filesystem has not been mounted,
'' .. E_BAD_FILENAME if the filename is a null pointer, empty or longer than 127 characters,
'' .. E_NO_HANDLE if no handle is available,
'' .. E_FILE_MODE if mode letter(s) is/are invalid,
'' .. E_DRIVE_FULL if the flash has no room for a new file (any mode but "r"),
' (that is: no free block, or no free block ID for the head of a new file)
'' .. E_FILE_OPEN if file is already open,
'' .. E_FILE_NOT_FOUND if file does not exist (read mode, "r" or "r+")

' Local Variables:
' @local status - SUCCESS, or the reason no handle is returned
' @local bFileExists - TRUE when a file of this name exists
' @local signature - the first long of the head block of the file of this name, or 0 when there is none

{
    ANSI C file info
    REF: https://www.tutorialspoint.com/cprogramming/c_file_io.htm
    REF: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/C_file_input/output
        "r"  (read-only) Open a file for reading.  The file must exist.
        "w"  (write-only) Create an empty file for writing.  If a file with the same name already exists,
             its contents are discarded and the file is treated as a new empty file.
        "a"  (write-only) Append to a file.  Writing operations append data at the end of the file.
             The file is created if it does not exist.
        "r+" (read-write) Open a file for update both reading and writing.  The file must exist.
        "w+" (read-write) Create an empty file for both reading and writing.  If a file with the same name
             already exists its contents are discarded and the file is treated as a new empty file.
        "a+" (read-write) Opens a text file for both reading and writing. It creates the file if it does not exist.
             The reading will start from the beginning but writing can only be appended.
}

  status := SUCCESS                                                             'stays SUCCESS until a check fails

  ifnot fsMounted
    status := E_NOT_MOUNTED
  elseifnot valid_filename(p_filename)
    status := E_BAD_FILENAME
  elseif fsFreeHndlCt == 0
    status := E_NO_HANDLE
  else
    ' mode-specific checks
    case mode
      "r", "R":
      "a", "A", "w", "W", FILEMODE_READ_EXTENDED, FILEMODE_READ_EXTENDED_UC, FILEMODE_WRITE_EXTENDED, FILEMODE_WRITE_EXTENDED_UC:
        ifnot has_free_blocks(ONE_FREE_BLOCK)                                   'if no free block exists, abort with error
          status := E_DRIVE_FULL
      other: status := E_FILE_MODE

  if status == SUCCESS                                                          'every check that needs no lock passed
    'debug("open() ENTRY get sem #", udec_(fsLock))
    repeat while locktry(fsLock) == 0                                           ' lock for exlusive use

    ' every check made before the lock is made again: another cog may have changed the filesystem meanwhile
    ifnot fsMounted                                                             'unmount() may have run while this cog waited for the lock
      status := E_NOT_MOUNTED
    else
      ' look the file up once: the open below uses this head signature, and nothing changes the flash before it
      signature := get_file_head_signature(p_filename)
      bFileExists := signature <> 0

      ' do checks that require the lock
      if lookdown(mode : "a", "A", "w", "W", FILEMODE_READ_EXTENDED, FILEMODE_READ_EXTENDED_UC, FILEMODE_WRITE_EXTENDED, FILEMODE_WRITE_EXTENDED_UC) and not has_free_blocks(ONE_FREE_BLOCK)
        status := E_DRIVE_FULL                                                  'no free block exists, abort with error
      elseif lookdown(mode : "r", "R", FILEMODE_READ_EXTENDED, FILEMODE_READ_EXTENDED_UC) and not bFileExists
        'debug("open() filename=[", zstr_(p_filename), "]")
        status := E_FILE_NOT_FOUND                                              'the file to read does not exist, abort with error

    if status == SUCCESS and is_file_open(p_filename, H_READ_WRITE)             'if file is already open, abort
      status := E_FILE_OPEN

    elseif status == SUCCESS and fsFreeHndlCt == 0                              'yep, check this again since we have the lock
      status := E_NO_HANDLE

    if status <> SUCCESS
      status := release_lock(status)                                            ' aborting, release the lock
      'debug("open(", sdec_(status), ") ABORT freed sem #", udec_(fsLock))
    else
      ' the following calls release the lock
      case mode
        "r", "R"  : handle := finish_open_read(p_filename, 0, signature)        ' read
        "w", "W"  : handle := finish_open_write(p_filename, 0, signature)       ' replace
        "a", "A"  :
          if bFileExists
              handle := finish_open_append(p_filename, 0, signature)            ' append
          else
              handle := finish_open_write(p_filename, 0, signature)             ' create new
        FILEMODE_READ_EXTENDED, FILEMODE_READ_EXTENDED_UC:
          handle := finish_open_readwrite(p_filename, FALSE, signature)         ' read/write/modify the existing file
        FILEMODE_WRITE_EXTENDED, FILEMODE_WRITE_EXTENDED_UC:
          handle := finish_open_readwrite(p_filename, TRUE, signature)          ' read/write/modify a new file, which replaces any existing file at close
      if handle < 0
        status := handle                                                        'the reason the open could not finish
      else
        handle += HANDLE_BASE                                                   'the caller's handle counts from HANDLE_BASE

  if status < 0
    handle := status                                                            'a failed open returns its code in place of a handle

  'debug("open(", sdec_(handle), ") EXIT freed sem #", udec_(fsLock))
  LONG[@errorCode][cogid()] := status                                           'every path leaves its status in error() for this cog


PUB open_circular(p_filename, mode, max_file_length) : handle | status, bFileExists, signature

'' Open circular file of max_file_length in mode; return handle
'' (HANDLE_BASE..HANDLE_BASE+MAX_FILES_OPEN-1) if successful
'' -- a circular file keeps its newest max_file_length bytes: when it is committed by close() or
''    flush(), the oldest bytes beyond the limit are removed from its start
'' -- as with open(), a file with no contents does not exist, so a new file closed with nothing
''    written is not left; see the "Differences from ANSI C" table of README.md
''
'' @param p_filename - address of a zstring containing the filename
'' @param mode - the mode in which to open the file (no other mode is valid, and "w" is
'' .. E_FILE_MODE):
'' -- mode "a", "A" to append to the end of an existing circular file (file created if doesn't
''    exist). Closed with nothing appended, an existing file is unchanged
'' -- mode "r", "R" to read from an existing circular file (the file must exist)
'' @param max_file_length - constrain the file to this length (in bytes, 1 or more)
'' @returns handle - return style value-or-code: handle to open file if successful,
'' .. E_NOT_MOUNTED if filesystem has not been mounted,
'' .. E_BAD_FILENAME if the filename is a null pointer, empty or longer than 127 characters,
'' .. E_NO_HANDLE if no handle is available,
'' .. E_BAD_FILE_LENGTH if file length is negative or zero,
'' .. E_FILE_MODE if mode letter(s) is/are invalid,
'' .. E_FILE_NOT_FOUND if file does not exist (read mode),
'' .. E_DRIVE_FULL if flash filesystem is full (write/append mode),
'' .. E_FILE_OPEN if file is already open

' Local Variables:
' @local status - SUCCESS, or the reason no handle is returned
' @local bFileExists - TRUE when a file of this name exists
' @local signature - the first long of the head block of the file of this name, or 0 when there is none

  status := SUCCESS                                                             'stays SUCCESS until a check fails

  ifnot fsMounted
    status := E_NOT_MOUNTED
  elseifnot valid_filename(p_filename)
    status := E_BAD_FILENAME
  elseif fsFreeHndlCt == 0
    status := E_NO_HANDLE
  elseif max_file_length < 1
    status := E_BAD_FILE_LENGTH
  else
    ' do we have a legal mode?
    case mode
      "r", "R":
      "a", "A":
      other: status := E_FILE_MODE

  if status == SUCCESS                                                          'every check that needs no lock passed
    ' acquire lock
    repeat while locktry(fsLock) == 0                                           ' lock for exlusive use

    ' every check made before the lock is made again: another cog may have changed the filesystem meanwhile
    ifnot fsMounted                                                             'unmount() may have run while this cog waited for the lock
      status := E_NOT_MOUNTED
    else
      ' look the file up once: the open below uses this head signature, and nothing changes the flash before it
      signature := get_file_head_signature(p_filename)
      bFileExists := signature <> 0

      ' do checks that require the lock
      case mode
        "r", "R":
          ifnot bFileExists                                                     'if the file to read does not exist, abort with error
            status := E_FILE_NOT_FOUND
        "a", "A":
          ifnot has_free_blocks(ONE_FREE_BLOCK)                                 'if no free block exists, abort with error
            status := E_DRIVE_FULL

    if status == SUCCESS and is_file_open(p_filename, H_READ_WRITE)             'if file is already open, abort
      status := E_FILE_OPEN

    elseif status == SUCCESS and fsFreeHndlCt == 0                              'yep, check this again since we have the lock
      status := E_NO_HANDLE

    if status <> SUCCESS
      status := release_lock(status)                                            ' aborting, release the lock
    else
      ' the following calls release the lock
      case mode
        "a", "A":
          if bFileExists
            handle := finish_open_append(p_filename, max_file_length, signature) ' append CIRC
          else
            handle := finish_open_write(p_filename, max_file_length, signature) ' write CIRC
        "r", "R": handle := finish_open_read(p_filename, max_file_length, signature) ' read CIRC
      if handle < 0
        status := handle                                                        'the reason the open could not finish
      else
        handle += HANDLE_BASE                                                   'the caller's handle counts from HANDLE_BASE

  if status < 0
    handle := status                                                            'a failed open returns its code in place of a handle

  LONG[@errorCode][cogid()] := status                                           'every path leaves its status in error() for this cog


PUB flush(handle) : status | fileOffset, seekStatus

'' Logically, "close", then "reopen file in same mode" (but you don't lose the file handle)
'' -- (forces any pending writes to be completed)
'' -- a handle with nothing written since it was opened or last flushed has nothing to flush and
''    is left as it is
'' -- a "w+" file is committed, replacing any existing file of the same name, and stays open at
''    the same position
'' -- a "w" or "a" file that cannot be committed for lack of a free block stays open as it was, its
''    unwritten bytes kept, so a later flush() or close() commits it once a block is free
'' -- a circular file that is committed over its limit, because its trim found no free block, stays
''    whole and the status is E_DRIVE_FULL: close() trims it once a block is free
'' @param handle - a handle to an open file
'' @returns status - return style status: 0 (SUCCESS) if successful,
'' .. E_NOT_MOUNTED if filesystem has not been mounted,
'' .. E_FILE_MODE if the handle is open for reading only,
'' .. E_BAD_HANDLE if the handle is not an open handle,
'' .. E_DRIVE_FULL if the file could not be committed, trimmed or rewritten for lack of a free block
''    (it stays open),
'' .. E_FLASH_TIMEOUT if the flash chip did not finish a write in time: the filesystem is unmounted
''    and every handle freed, and the next mount() recovers the flash as it would after a power
''    loss

' Local Variables:
' @local fileOffset - the position in a "w+" file, kept across its commit
' @local seekStatus - what the return to that position reported

  handle := handle_index(handle)                                                'from here on handle is the index in the handle tables
  ifnot fsMounted
    status := E_NOT_MOUNTED
  elseif handle < 0 or handle > MAX_FILES_OPEN - 1
    status := E_BAD_HANDLE
  else
    repeat while locktry(fsLock) == 0                                           ' lock for exlusive use

    status := SUCCESS                                                           'new operation

    ifnot fsMounted                                                             'unmount() may have run while this cog waited for the lock
      status := E_NOT_MOUNTED
    else
      ' Flush write buffer, completes any write operation, but leaves file open
      'debug("* flush() ", udec(handle))

      case hStatus[handle]

        0:                                                                      'handle is not open?
          status := E_BAD_HANDLE                                                'nothing to flush, nothing to change

        H_WRITE, H_APPEND:                                                      'write/rewrite/append mode?
          if hModified[handle]                                                  'only when something was written since the last commit
            status := close_no_lock(handle, FALSE)                              'commit the file, keeping the handle
            if hModified[handle] == FALSE and fsDeviceFault == FALSE            'committed (a trim that failed leaves the file whole), else left as it was..
              start_modify(handle, H_APPEND, hHeadBlockID[handle], $FFFFFF, true) '..reopen file in append mode

        H_READWRITE:                                                            'modify mode?
          if hHeadPending[handle]                                               'a "w+" file not yet committed..
            if field[IDToBlock][hHeadBlockID[handle]] < BLOCKS or hModified[handle] '..that holds data (one holding none is left as it is)
              fileOffset := hSeekFileOffset[handle]
              status := commit_new_chain(handle)                                '....commit it now
              if fsDeviceFault == FALSE                                         '....a failed flash write leaves the handle to the fault exit
                seekStatus := seek_no_locks(handle, fileOffset)                 '....and return to the position, which the commit may have left
                if status == SUCCESS                                            '....a failed commit is the status, not the seek after it
                  status := seekStatus
          elseif hModified[handle]                                              'if block was modified...
            status := rewrite_block(handle)                                     '..rewrite block
            if status == SUCCESS                                                '..a block that is not rewritten stays modified in the buffer
              hModified[handle]~                                                '..clear modified flag

        other:                                                                  'other mode?
          status := E_FILE_MODE                                                 'a read handle has nothing to flush, abort

    status := release_lock(status)                                              ' release the lock, we're done with it

  LONG[@errorCode][cogid()] := status                                           'every path leaves its status in error() for this cog


PUB close(handle) : status

'' Close an open file, completes any pending writes then frees the handle
'' -- a file opened with "w" or "w+" replaces any existing file of the same name now; closed with no
''    write, it leaves no file: an existing file of that name is deleted, and the status is still
''    SUCCESS (use exists() to check)
'' -- a circular file that a flush() committed over its limit, because the trim found no free
''    block, is trimmed now
'' -- the handle is freed whatever the status: a file that could not be committed for lack of a free
''    block is closed without the data it had not written (flush() keeps the handle open for another
''    try)
''
'' @param handle - a handle to an open file
'' @returns status - return style status: 0 (SUCCESS) if successful,
'' .. E_NOT_MOUNTED if filesystem has not been mounted,
'' .. E_BAD_HANDLE if the handle is not an open handle,
'' .. E_DRIVE_FULL if the flash has no free block for the commit, the trim or the rewrite,
'' .. E_FLASH_TIMEOUT if the flash chip did not finish a write in time: the filesystem is unmounted
''    and every handle freed, and the next mount() recovers the flash as it would after a power
''    loss

  handle := handle_index(handle)                                                'from here on handle is the index in the handle tables
  ifnot fsMounted
    status := E_NOT_MOUNTED
  elseif handle < 0 or handle > MAX_FILES_OPEN - 1
    status := E_BAD_HANDLE
  else
    'debug("close(", udec_(handle), ") ENTRY get sem #", udec_(fsLock))
    repeat while locktry(fsLock) == 0                                           ' lock for exlusive use

    ifnot fsMounted                                                             'unmount() may have run while this cog waited for the lock
      status := E_NOT_MOUNTED
    elseif hStatus[handle]                                                      'is this handle open?
      status := close_no_lock(handle, TRUE)                                     'commit our file changes, SUCCESS or the reason the commit failed
      hCircularLength[handle] := 0                                              'clear prior length
      hHeadBlockID[handle] := NOT_VALID                                         'clear association with external file

      fsFreeHndlCt++                                                            'show that handle is now avail
      hStatus[handle]~                                                          'show no file-mode associated
    else
      status := E_BAD_HANDLE                                                    'a handle that is not open frees nothing

    status := release_lock(status)                                              ' release the lock, we're done with it
    'debug("close(", sdec_(handle), ") EXIT freed sem #", udec_(fsLock))

  LONG[@errorCode][cogid()] := status                                           'every path leaves its status in error() for this cog


PUB rename(p_cur_filename, p_new_filename) : status | signature, new_block_address, cur_block_address

'' Rename a file named {p_cur_filename} to {p_new_filename}
''
'' A rename needs room for one block. Without it the result is E_DRIVE_FULL, the file keeps its old
'' name and the flash is unchanged.
' A rename needs a free block ID and one free block for the new head block, and both are checked before anything
' changes.
''
'' When more than one reason applies, the one reported is the first of these checks, in this order:
'' E_NOT_MOUNTED, E_BAD_FILENAME, E_FILE_OPEN, E_DRIVE_FULL, E_FILE_EXISTS, E_FILE_NOT_FOUND. So
'' when the new name is in use and the old file does not exist the result is E_FILE_EXISTS, and a
'' full flash hides both.
''
'' @param p_cur_filename - address of a zstring containing the existing filename
'' @param p_new_filename - address of a zstring containing the new filename
'' @returns status - return style status: 0 (SUCCESS) if successful,
'' .. E_NOT_MOUNTED if filesystem has not been mounted,
'' .. E_BAD_FILENAME if either filename is a null pointer, empty or longer than 127 characters,
'' .. E_FILE_OPEN if either file is open,
'' .. E_DRIVE_FULL if no available space left in filesystem,
'' .. E_FILE_EXISTS if new file already exists,
'' .. E_FILE_NOT_FOUND if old file doesn't exist,
'' .. E_FLASH_TIMEOUT if the flash chip did not finish a write in time: the filesystem is unmounted,
''    and the next mount() finds the file under its old name or its new one, as after a power loss

' Local Variables:
' @local signature - block state bits of block being renamed
' @local new_block_address - the block offset within the file system for the new block
' @local cur_block_address - the block offset within the file system for the old block

  ifnot fsMounted
    status := E_NOT_MOUNTED
  elseif not valid_filename(p_cur_filename) or not valid_filename(p_new_filename)
    status := E_BAD_FILENAME
  else
    repeat while locktry(fsLock) == 0                                           ' lock for exlusive use

    status := SUCCESS                                                           ' new operation

    ifnot fsMounted                                                             'unmount() may have run while this cog waited for the lock
      status := E_NOT_MOUNTED

    elseif is_file_open(p_cur_filename, H_READ_WRITE)                          'if old file is open, abort
      status := E_FILE_OPEN

    elseif is_file_open(p_new_filename, H_READ_WRITE)                           'if new file is open, abort
      status := E_FILE_OPEN

    elseifnot available_blocks()                                                'if no block ID is free, abort
      status := E_DRIVE_FULL

    elseifnot has_free_blocks(ONE_FREE_BLOCK)                                   'if no block is free for the new head block, abort
      status := E_DRIVE_FULL

    elseif get_file_head_signature(p_new_filename)                              'if new file exists, abort
      status := E_FILE_EXISTS

    elseifnot signature := get_file_head_signature(p_cur_filename)              'if old file doesn't exist, abort
      status := E_FILE_NOT_FOUND

    else
      ' a file rename consists of replacing the current head block of the file with a new head block containing the new filename
      ' then cancelling the old head block
      new_block_address := next_block_address(0)                                'get a new block to use for renaming (may move head block)
      if new_block_address < 0                                                  'no free block (E_DRIVE_FULL, nothing was changed), or a block move failed (E_FLASH_TIMEOUT)
        status := new_block_address
      else
        cur_block_address := field[IDToBlock][signature.[19..8]]                'get head block of file to rename (a block move may have changed it)

        flash_read_block_addr(cur_block_address, @tmpBlockBuffer, $000, $FFF)   'read head block of file to rename
        LONG[@tmpBlockBuffer][1].[31..12] := filename_crc(p_new_filename)       'install new filename CRC
        bytefill(@tmpBlockBuffer + $008, $E5, FILENAME_SIZE)                    'clear filename space to prevent old trailing chrs
        strcopy(@tmpBlockBuffer + $008, p_new_filename, FILENAME_SIZE - 1)      'copy new filename into filename space
        flash_activate_updated_block(new_block_address, @tmpBlockBuffer)        'program updated block
        if fsDeviceFault                                                        'the flash failed: the old head block stays, as a power loss here leaves it
          status := E_FLASH_TIMEOUT
        else
          flash_cancel_block(cur_block_address)                                 'cancel old block

          field[IDToBlock][signature.[19..8]] := new_block_address              'update IDToBlock
          field[BlockState][new_block_address] := B_HEAD                        'make new block HEAD
          field[BlockState][cur_block_address] := B_FREE                        'make old block FREE

    status := release_lock(status)                                              ' release the lock, we're done with it

  LONG[@errorCode][cogid()] := status                                           'every path leaves its status in error() for this cog


PUB delete(p_filename) : status | signature

'' Delete a named file
''
'' @param p_filename - address of a zstring containing the filename
'' @returns status - return style status: 0 (SUCCESS) if successful,
'' .. E_NOT_MOUNTED if filesystem has not been mounted,
'' .. E_BAD_FILENAME if the filename is a null pointer, empty or longer than 127 characters,
'' .. E_FILE_OPEN if file is open,
'' .. E_FILE_NOT_FOUND if file doesn't exist,
'' .. E_FLASH_TIMEOUT if the flash chip did not finish a write in time: the filesystem is unmounted,
''    and the next mount() removes what is left of the file, as after a power loss

' Local Variables:
' @local signature - block state bits of block being removed

  ifnot fsMounted
    status := E_NOT_MOUNTED
  elseifnot valid_filename(p_filename)
    status := E_BAD_FILENAME
  else
    repeat while locktry(fsLock) == 0                                           ' lock for exlusive use

    status := SUCCESS                                                           ' new operation

    ifnot fsMounted                                                             'unmount() may have run while this cog waited for the lock
      status := E_NOT_MOUNTED

    elseif is_file_open(p_filename, H_READ_WRITE)                               'if file open in any mode, abort
      status := E_FILE_OPEN

    elseifnot signature := get_file_head_signature(p_filename)                  'if file doesn't exist, abort
      status := E_FILE_NOT_FOUND

    else
      ' a file delete consists of cancelling all blocks in the file chain
      delete_chain_from_id(signature.[19..8], 0, 0, False)                      'cancel and free all blocks in file, don't keep first ID valid

    status := release_lock(status)                                              ' release the lock, we're done with it

  LONG[@errorCode][cogid()] := status                                           'every path leaves its status in error() for this cog


PUB create_file(p_filename, fill_value, byte_count) : status | signature, head_block_id, block_id, block_address, notHead, dataOffset, isLast, currOffset, NextID_EndPtr, bSkipChecks

'' Make a file of a byte_count size filled with fill_value bytes - "open read/write extended" to
'' rewrite contents
''
'' The flash must have room for the whole file. Without it the result is E_DRIVE_FULL, the file is
'' not created, and the flash holds nothing of it.
' The file needs a free block ID and a free block for each of its blocks. A free block ID, and every block the
' file needs, are checked before anything changes. If the block IDs still run out part way, every block already
' written for the file is cancelled and freed again with its block ID.
''
'' @param p_filename - address of a zstring containing the filename
'' @param fill_value - initial value for all bytes in the new file
'' @param byte_count - desired length of file in bytes (at least 1)
'' @returns status - return style status: 0 (SUCCESS) if successful,
'' .. E_NOT_MOUNTED if filesystem has not been mounted,
'' .. E_BAD_FILENAME if the filename is a null pointer, empty or longer than 127 characters,
'' .. E_BAD_FILE_LENGTH if byte_count is negative or zero (no file is created),
'' .. E_FILE_OPEN if file is open,
'' .. E_DRIVE_FULL if no available space left in filesystem (no file is created),
'' .. E_FILE_EXISTS if the file already exists,
'' .. E_FLASH_TIMEOUT if the flash chip did not finish a write in time: nothing written is undone,
''    the filesystem is unmounted, and the next mount() removes the partly written file

' Local Variables:
' @local signature - temporary block state bits
' @local head_block_id - the head block id for this new file
' @local block_id - ID of the block being written, which has no block yet when the loop stops short
' @local block_address - the block offset within the file system
' @local notHead - T/F where T means is not first block in file
' @local dataOffset - temp integer containing the initial data offset
' @local isLast - T/F where T means this is last block
' @local currOffset - temporary block offset
' @local NextID_EndPtr - temporary nextID/EndPtr value
' @local bSkipChecks - TRUE when this call skips the free-ID and free-block checks

  bSkipChecks := fsSkipCreateChecks                                             'take the one-call skip of the space checks..
  fsSkipCreateChecks := false                                                   '..and clear it, whatever this call returns

  ifnot fsMounted
    status := E_NOT_MOUNTED
  elseifnot valid_filename(p_filename)
    status := E_BAD_FILENAME
  elseif byte_count < 1
    status := E_BAD_FILE_LENGTH
  else
    repeat while locktry(fsLock) == 0                                           ' lock for exlusive use

    status := SUCCESS                                                           ' new operation

    ifnot fsMounted                                                             'unmount() may have run while this cog waited for the lock
      status := E_NOT_MOUNTED

    elseif is_File_Open(p_filename, H_READ_WRITE)                               'if file is open, abort
      status := E_FILE_OPEN

    elseif not bSkipChecks and not available_blocks()                           'if no block ID is free, abort
      status := E_DRIVE_FULL

    elseif not bSkipChecks and not has_free_blocks(size_in_blocks(byte_count))  'if too few blocks are free for the whole file, abort
      status := E_DRIVE_FULL

    elseif signature := get_file_head_signature(p_filename)                     'if file exists, abort
      status := E_FILE_EXISTS

    else
      notHead := false
      currOffset := 0
      block_id := head_block_id := next_available_block_id()                    'get initial ID
      if block_id < 0                                                           'no free block ID: nothing was changed, error() holds E_DRIVE_FULL
        status := block_id
      else
        repeat
          block_address := next_block_address(0)                                'get a new block now (may alter tmpBlockBuffer and IDToBlock)
          if block_address < 0                                                  'no free block (E_DRIVE_FULL), or a block move failed (E_FLASH_TIMEOUT)
            status := block_address
            quit
          ifnot notHead                                                         'if HEAD block..
            build_head_block(@tmpBlockBuffer, p_filename, 0)                    '..build head block in buffer
            dataOffset := $088                                                  '..set data start for head block
          else                                                                  'if BODY block..
            dataOffset := $004                                                  '..set data start for body block
          bytefill(@tmpBlockBuffer + dataOffset, fill_value, BLOCK_SIZE - dataOffset) '..clear buffer for body block
          if isLast := byte_count <= (currOffset += $FFC - dataOffset)          'if last block.. (update position and check if last block)
            NextID_EndPtr := byte_count - currOffset + $FFC                     '..get EndPtr
          else                                                                  'if not last block..
            NextID_EndPtr := next_available_block_id()                          '..get NextID
            if NextID_EndPtr < 0                                                '..no free block ID: the block taken for this block is not written
              field[BlockState][block_address] := B_FREE
              status := NextID_EndPtr
              quit
          LONG[@tmpBlockBuffer].[0] := !isLast                                  'set more/last bit
          LONG[@tmpBlockBuffer].[1] := notHead                                  'set head/body bit
          LONG[@tmpBlockBuffer].[19..8] := block_id                             'set ThisID
          LONG[@tmpBlockBuffer].[31..20] := NextID_EndPtr                       'set NextID or EndPtr
          flash_program_block(block_address, @tmpBlockBuffer, %011)             'program block
          if fsDeviceFault                                                      'the flash failed: the file stops here, as a power loss here leaves it
            status := E_FLASH_TIMEOUT
            quit
          field[IDToBlock][block_id] := block_address                           'set IDToBlock
          if notHead                                                            'if not head block..
            flash_activate_block(block_address, %011)                           '..activate body block
            if fsDeviceFault                                                    '..the flash failed: the file stops here
              status := E_FLASH_TIMEOUT
              quit
            field[BlockState][block_address] := B_BODY                          '..an active body block is B_BODY
          block_id := NextID_EndPtr                                             'switch to next ID
          notHead := true
        until isLast                                                            'loop until last block done

        if status == SUCCESS
          block_address := field[IDToBlock][head_block_id]
          flash_activate_block(block_address, %011)                             'now activate head block to activate file
          field[BlockState][block_address] := B_HEAD                            'the head block is B_HEAD only once it is active (a failed activate is taken by the fault exit)
        elseif fsDeviceFault == FALSE                                           'stopped short for lack of space: undo every block this call wrote (after a flash failure nothing is undone)
          if notHead                                                            'if the head block was written..
            delete_chain_from_id(head_block_id, block_id, 2, false)             '..cancel and free the head through the block that leads to block_id
          field[IDValid][block_id]~                                             'release the ID that got no block

    status := release_lock(status)                                              ' release the lock, we're done with it

  LONG[@errorCode][cogid()] := status                                           'every path leaves its status in error() for this cog


PUB exists(p_filename) : bool | status

'' Determine if named file is present in the file system
''
'' @param p_filename - address of a zstring containing the filename
'' @returns bool - return style boolean: True/False where True means the file exists
'' (a file that does not exist is an answer, not an error: it returns false and error() is SUCCESS)
'' (sets error() to E_NOT_MOUNTED and returns false if filesystem has not been mounted)
'' (sets error() to E_BAD_FILENAME and returns false if the filename is a null pointer, empty or
'' longer than 127 characters)

' Local Variables:
' @local status - SUCCESS when the answer was found, or the reason it was not

  bool := false
  ifnot fsMounted
    status := E_NOT_MOUNTED
  elseifnot valid_filename(p_filename)
    status := E_BAD_FILENAME
  else
    repeat while locktry(fsLock) == 0                                           ' lock for exlusive use

    ifnot fsMounted                                                             'unmount() may have run while this cog waited for the lock
      status := E_NOT_MOUNTED
    else
      status := SUCCESS                                                         ' a file that does not exist is an answer, not an error
      bool := exists_no_lock(p_filename)

    status := release_lock(status)                                              ' release the lock, we're done with it

  LONG[@errorCode][cogid()] := status                                           'every path leaves its status in error() for this cog


PUB file_size(p_filename) : size_in_bytes | status, signature

'' Return size of file in bytes
'' -- the size is of the file on the flash: bytes a handle holds and has not yet written are not
''    counted (file_size_for_handle() counts them)
'' -- a circular file that has been trimmed is the length that can be read from it
''
'' @param p_filename - address of a zstring containing the filename
'' @returns size_in_bytes - return style value-or-code: either the count of bytes contained in the
'' .. file or
'' .. E_NOT_MOUNTED if filesystem has not been mounted,
'' .. E_BAD_FILENAME if the filename is a null pointer, empty or longer than 127 characters,
'' .. E_FILE_NOT_FOUND if the file doesn't exist

' Local Variables:
' @local status - SUCCESS, or the reason no size is returned
' @local signature - block state bits of block being checked

  ifnot fsMounted
    status := E_NOT_MOUNTED
  elseifnot valid_filename(p_filename)
    status := E_BAD_FILENAME
  else
    repeat while locktry(fsLock) == 0                                           ' lock for exlusive use

    status := SUCCESS                                                           ' new operation

    ifnot fsMounted                                                             'unmount() may have run while this cog waited for the lock
      status := E_NOT_MOUNTED
    elseif signature := get_file_head_signature(p_filename)                     'does file exist?
      ' the lookup gave the head block's format (.[2] is 0 for an old-format head), so the name is not read again
      size_in_bytes, _, _ := count_file_bytes(signature.[19..8], head_data_start_of_format(signature.[19..8], signature.[2] == 0)) 'the bytes a read can reach
    else
      status := E_FILE_NOT_FOUND

    status := release_lock(status)                                              ' release the lock, we're done with it

  if status < 0
    size_in_bytes := status                                                     'a failed call returns its code in place of a size
  LONG[@errorCode][cogid()] := status                                           'every path leaves its status in error() for this cog


PUB file_size_for_handle(handle) : size_in_bytes | status

'' Return size of file in bytes
'' -- the size counts the bytes the handle holds and has not yet written to the flash
'' -- for a file open with "w" or "a" it is the file as the handle will commit it
'' -- a circular file that has been trimmed is the length that can be read from it
'' -- for an old-format circular file read with open_circular() it is the bytes the handle can read,
''    counted from the first byte it keeps, as its seek positions are
''
'' @param handle - a handle to an open file
'' @returns size_in_bytes - return style value-or-code: either the count of bytes contained in the
'' .. file or
'' .. E_NOT_MOUNTED if filesystem has not been mounted,
'' .. E_BAD_HANDLE if the handle is not an open handle

' Local Variables:
' @local status - SUCCESS, or the reason no size is returned

  handle := handle_index(handle)                                                'from here on handle is the index in the handle tables
  ifnot fsMounted
    status := E_NOT_MOUNTED
  elseif handle < 0 or handle > MAX_FILES_OPEN - 1
    status := E_BAD_HANDLE
  else
    repeat while locktry(fsLock) == 0                                           ' lock for exlusive use

    status := SUCCESS                                                           ' new operation

    ifnot fsMounted                                                             'unmount() may have run while this cog waited for the lock
      status := E_NOT_MOUNTED
    elseif hStatus[handle]                                                      'is this handle open?
      size_in_bytes := handle_file_length(handle)                               'includes bytes written to the handle and not yet on the flash
    else
      status := E_BAD_HANDLE

    status := release_lock(status)                                              ' release the lock, we're done with it

  if status < 0
    size_in_bytes := status                                                     'a failed call returns its code in place of a size
  LONG[@errorCode][cogid()] := status                                           'every path leaves its status in error() for this cog


PUB file_size_unused(p_filename) : size_in_bytes_unused | status, signature

'' Return the number of bytes not yet written in the last allocated block
''
'' @param p_filename - address of a zstring containing the filename
'' @returns size_in_bytes_unused - return style value-or-code: either the count of unwritten bytes
'' .. of the file or
'' .. E_NOT_MOUNTED if filesystem has not been mounted,
'' .. E_BAD_FILENAME if the filename is a null pointer, empty or longer than 127 characters,
'' .. E_FILE_NOT_FOUND if the file doesn't exist

' Local Variables:
' @local status - SUCCESS, or the reason no size is returned
' @local signature - block state bits of block being checked

  ifnot fsMounted
    status := E_NOT_MOUNTED
  elseifnot valid_filename(p_filename)
    status := E_BAD_FILENAME
  else
    repeat while locktry(fsLock) == 0                                           ' lock for exlusive use

    status := SUCCESS                                                           ' new operation

    ifnot fsMounted                                                             'unmount() may have run while this cog waited for the lock
      status := E_NOT_MOUNTED
    elseif signature := get_file_head_signature(p_filename)                     'does file exist?
      _, size_in_bytes_unused, _ := count_file_bytes(signature.[19..8], head_data_start_of_format(signature.[19..8], signature.[2] == 0))
    else
      status := E_FILE_NOT_FOUND

    'debug("file_size_unused(", zstr_(p_filename), ") = (", sdec_(size_in_bytes_unused), ")")

    status := release_lock(status)                                              ' release the lock, we're done with it

  if status < 0
    size_in_bytes_unused := status                                              'a failed call returns its code in place of a size
  LONG[@errorCode][cogid()] := status                                           'every path leaves its status in error() for this cog


PUB seek(handle, position, whence) : end_position | status, file_position, block_id, endPtr, fileOffset

'' Seek the file pointer to a position within the file or at the end of the file
'' -- use 0, SK_FILE_START for position to seek to the START of the file
'' -- use POSX, SK_FILE_START (largest positive LONG value) for position to seek to the current END
''    of the file
'' -- use +/- value, SK_CURRENT_POSN to move RELATIVE to the current position within the file
'' -- in "r+"/"w+" mode a modified block is rewritten before the seek leaves it; with no free block
''    for that the position does not change and E_DRIVE_FULL is returned
'' -- positions of an old-format circular file read with open_circular() count from the first byte
''    it keeps
'' -- in "r+"/"w+" mode bytes written past the end of the file and not yet flushed are part of the
''    file, and a seek can reach them
''
'' @param handle - a handle to an open file
'' @param position - position (in bytes) within the file (0 to length-1, posx)
''  use  seek(handle, POSX, SK_FILE_START) to seek to end of the file
'' @param whence - meaning of position: [SK_FILE_START, SK_CURRENT_POSN]
'' @returns end_position - return style value-or-code: within the file to which the file pointer
'' .. was set, or
'' .. E_NOT_MOUNTED if filesystem has not been mounted,
'' .. E_BAD_HANDLE if the handle is not an open handle,
'' .. E_BAD_SEEK_ARG if invalid whence value,
'' .. E_FILE_MODE if the file is not open in a mode supporting seeks (only "r", "r+" and "w+" do),
'' .. E_FILE_SEEK if attempted seek past either end of file (and didn't use POSX for tail),
'' .. E_DRIVE_FULL if a modified block could not be rewritten,
'' .. E_FLASH_TIMEOUT if the flash chip did not finish the rewrite of a modified block in time (the
''    filesystem is unmounted)

' Local Variables:
' @local status - SUCCESS, or the reason the position was not set
' @local file_position - temporary for calculated seek position
' @local block_id - the block holding the located position, or the last block when the file ends before it
' @local endPtr - offset within that block of the located position
' @local fileOffset - the position located: the one asked for, or the end of the file when that comes first

  handle := handle_index(handle)                                                'from here on handle is the index in the handle tables
  ifnot fsMounted
    status := E_NOT_MOUNTED
  elseif handle < 0 or handle > MAX_FILES_OPEN - 1
    status := E_BAD_HANDLE
  elseif hStatus[handle] == 0                                                   'a handle in the range that is not open
    status := E_BAD_HANDLE
  elseif whence <> SK_FILE_START and whence <> SK_CURRENT_POSN
    status := E_BAD_SEEK_ARG
  elseif whence == SK_FILE_START and position < 0
    'debug("seek() early out")
    status := E_FILE_SEEK
  elseif hStatus[handle] <> H_READ and hStatus[handle] <> H_READWRITE           'only READ, and WRITE and MODIFY, allow direct access
    status := E_FILE_MODE                                                       ' no, abort with error (open mode does not support seeking)
  else
    repeat while locktry(fsLock) == 0                                           ' lock for exlusive use

    status := SUCCESS                                                           ' new operation

    ifnot fsMounted                                                             'unmount() may have run while this cog waited for the lock
      status := E_NOT_MOUNTED
    elseif hStatus[handle] == 0                                                 'the handle may have been closed while this cog waited for the lock
      status := E_BAD_HANDLE
    elseif hStatus[handle] <> H_READ and hStatus[handle] <> H_READWRITE         '..or opened again in another mode
      status := E_FILE_MODE
    else
      if whence == SK_FILE_START                                                ' if seeking from current position
          ' for SK_FILE_START
        file_position := position
      else
        ' for SK_CURRENT_POSN, we need to calculate the adjusted position
        file_position := hSeekPtr[handle] <> NOT_ENABLED ? hSeekFileOffset[handle] : buffered_file_offset(handle) ' if seek mode enabled, use seek offset, else count the blocks before the buffered one
        file_position += position - hWindowStart[handle]                        ' calculate the adjusted position, counted from the start of the data

      if position <> POSX and file_position < 0                                 ' a position before the first byte
        status := E_FILE_SEEK
      else
        ' locate the position, or the end of the file when that comes first, including bytes written but not yet on the flash
        block_id, endPtr, fileOffset := seek_locate(handle, position == POSX ? POSX : file_position + hWindowStart[handle])

        if position == POSX                                                     ' attempting to seek beyond, limit to end of file (0 for an empty file)
          file_position := fileOffset - hWindowStart[handle]

        'debug("seek(", sdec_(position), "), ", sdec(file_position), udec(fileOffset))

        if hCircularLength[handle] > 0 and file_position > hCircularLength[handle] ' if circular file and position is out of range
          status := E_FILE_SEEK                                                 ' abort with error
        elseif fileOffset - hWindowStart[handle] < file_position                ' the file ends before the position (its end itself can be reached, for append)
          status := E_FILE_SEEK                                                 ' abort with error
        else
          status := seek_to(handle, block_id, endPtr, fileOffset)               ' SUCCESS, or the reason the position was not set
          end_position := file_position

    status := release_lock(status)                                              ' release the lock, we're done with it

  if status < 0
    end_position := status                                                      'a failed seek returns its code in place of a position
  LONG[@errorCode][cogid()] := status                                           'every path leaves its status in error() for this cog


PUB write(handle, p_buffer, count) : bytes_written | status

'' Write count bytes from p_buffer to the file (open for write/append/modify) associated with the
'' handle
'' -- if fewer than count bytes could be written, bytes_written is the number written so far and
''    error() holds the reason the write stopped; those bytes stay in the file (unless
''    E_FLASH_TIMEOUT unmounted it)
'' -- if no byte could be written because of an error, the negative code is returned in place of the
''    count
'' -- when the flash has no room for the block the next byte needs, the write stops with
''    E_DRIVE_FULL; a full block that is waiting to be written stays in the handle, and close() or
''    flush() commits it if a free block is left
''
'' @param handle - the handle to the file to which to write byte(s)
'' @param p_buffer - the address of the buffer containing the users' data to write
'' @param count - the number of bytes to write to the file (0 writes nothing and is not an error)
'' @returns bytes_written - return style count-or-code: the count of bytes written to the file or,
'' .. E_NOT_MOUNTED if filesystem has not been mounted,
'' .. E_BAD_HANDLE if the handle is not an open handle,
'' .. E_FILE_MODE if the file is not open for writing,
'' .. E_BAD_FILE_LENGTH if count is negative (nothing is written),
'' .. E_DRIVE_FULL if the flash has no room for the block the next byte needs (returned when no
''    byte was written; otherwise the count written, with E_DRIVE_FULL in error()),
'' .. E_FLASH_TIMEOUT if the flash chip did not finish a write in time (the filesystem is unmounted;
''    returned when no byte was written, otherwise the count written, with E_FLASH_TIMEOUT in
''    error())

' Local Variables:
' @local status - SUCCESS, or the reason the write stopped

  handle := handle_index(handle)                                                'from here on handle is the index in the handle tables
  bytes_written := 0
  ifnot fsMounted
    status := E_NOT_MOUNTED
  else
    'debug("write(", udec_(handle), ") ENTRY get sem #", udec_(fsLock))
    repeat while locktry(fsLock) == 0                                           ' lock for exlusive use

    'debug("write(", udec(handle), uhex_long(p_buffer), udec(count) ,")")

    ifnot fsMounted                                                             'unmount() may have run while this cog waited for the lock
      status := E_NOT_MOUNTED
    else
      status := ensure_handle_mode(handle, H_WRITE)                             ' E_BAD_HANDLE or E_FILE_MODE unless the handle is open for writing
      if status == SUCCESS and count < 0                                        ' a negative count writes nothing, so it returns the code
        status := E_BAD_FILE_LENGTH
      if status == SUCCESS
        'debug("write() [",zstr_(p_buffer),"](",udec_(count),")")
        bytes_written, status := wr_bytes_no_locks(handle, p_buffer, count)     ' the bytes written, and SUCCESS or the reason the write stopped (the bytes already written stay written)

    status := release_lock(status)                                              ' release the lock, we're done with it
    'debug("write(", udec_(handle), ") EXIT freed sem #", udec_(fsLock))

  if bytes_written == 0 and status < 0                                          ' no byte was written: return this cog's code
    bytes_written := status
  LONG[@errorCode][cogid()] := status                                           'every path leaves its status in error() for this cog


PUB wr_byte(handle, byte_value) : status

'' Write a byte to the file (open for write/append) associated with the handle
''
'' @param handle - handle to a file that is open for write or rewrite
'' @param byte_value - value to write to the file
'' @returns status - return style status: 0 (SUCCESS) if successful,
'' .. E_NOT_MOUNTED if filesystem has not been mounted,
'' .. E_BAD_HANDLE if the handle is not an open handle,
'' .. E_FILE_MODE if the file is not open for writing,
'' .. E_DRIVE_FULL if the flash has no room for the block the byte needs (the byte is not written),
'' .. E_FLASH_TIMEOUT if the flash chip did not finish a write in time (the filesystem is unmounted)

  handle := handle_index(handle)                                                'from here on handle is the index in the handle tables
  ifnot fsMounted
    status := E_NOT_MOUNTED
  else
    'debug("wr_byte(", udec_(handle), ") ENTRY get sem #", udec_(fsLock))
    repeat while locktry(fsLock) == 0                                           ' lock for exlusive use

    ifnot fsMounted                                                             'unmount() may have run while this cog waited for the lock
      status := E_NOT_MOUNTED
    else
      status := ensure_handle_mode(handle, H_WRITE)                             ' E_BAD_HANDLE or E_FILE_MODE unless the handle is open for writing
      if status == SUCCESS
        _, status := wr_bytes_no_locks(handle, @byte_value, 1)                  ' the low byte of byte_value, the first in hub memory

    status := release_lock(status)                                              ' release the lock, we're done with it
    'debug("wr_byte(", udec_(handle), ") EXIT freed sem #", udec_(fsLock))

  LONG[@errorCode][cogid()] := status                                           'every path leaves its status in error() for this cog


PUB wr_word(handle, word_value) : status | writeLength

'' Write WORD (16-bits) to the file (open for write/append) associated with the handle
'' -- order is Little Endian
'' -- a write that stops part-way returns the reason it stopped; the bytes already written stay in
''    the file
''
'' @param handle - the handle of the file to which to write the WORD
'' @param word_value - the 16 bit WORD to write to the file
'' @returns status - return style status: 0 (SUCCESS) if successful,
'' .. E_NOT_MOUNTED if filesystem has not been mounted,
'' .. E_BAD_HANDLE if the handle is not an open handle,
'' .. E_FILE_MODE if the file is not open for writing,
'' .. E_DRIVE_FULL if the flash has no room for the block a byte needs (fewer than 2 bytes may be
''    written),
'' .. E_FLASH_TIMEOUT if the flash chip did not finish a write in time (the filesystem is unmounted)

' Local Variables:
' @local writeLength - what write() returned: the bytes written, or its code

  writeLength := write(handle, @word_value, 2)
  if writeLength < 0
    status := writeLength
  elseif writeLength <> 2                                                       'a short write: error() holds the reason write() stopped
    status := LONG[@errorCode][cogid()]
  else
    status := SUCCESS
  LONG[@errorCode][cogid()] := status                                           'every path leaves its status in error() for this cog


PUB wr_long(handle, long_value) : status | writeLength

'' Write LONG (32-bits) to the file (open for write/append) associated with the handle
'' -- order is Little Endian
'' -- a write that stops part-way returns the reason it stopped; the bytes already written stay in
''    the file
''
'' @param handle - the handle of the file to which to write the LONG
'' @param long_value - the 32 bit LONG to write to the file
'' @returns status - return style status: 0 (SUCCESS) if successful,
'' .. E_NOT_MOUNTED if filesystem has not been mounted,
'' .. E_BAD_HANDLE if the handle is not an open handle,
'' .. E_FILE_MODE if the file is not open for writing,
'' .. E_DRIVE_FULL if the flash has no room for the block a byte needs (fewer than 4 bytes may be
''    written),
'' .. E_FLASH_TIMEOUT if the flash chip did not finish a write in time (the filesystem is unmounted)

' Local Variables:
' @local writeLength - what write() returned: the bytes written, or its code

  writeLength := write(handle, @long_value, 4)
  if writeLength < 0
    status := writeLength
  elseif writeLength <> 4                                                       'a short write: error() holds the reason write() stopped
    status := LONG[@errorCode][cogid()]
  else
    status := SUCCESS
  LONG[@errorCode][cogid()] := status                                           'every path leaves its status in error() for this cog


PUB wr_str(handle, p_str) : status | writeLength, strBytes

'' Write string (including the terminator) from p_str to the file (open for write/append) associated
'' with the handle
'' -- a write that stops part-way returns the reason it stopped; the bytes already written stay in
''    the file
''
'' @param handle - the handle of the file to which to write the zString
'' @param p_str - the address of the zString to write to the file
'' @returns status - return style status: 0 (SUCCESS) if successful,
'' .. E_NOT_MOUNTED if filesystem has not been mounted,
'' .. E_BAD_HANDLE if the handle is not an open handle,
'' .. E_FILE_MODE if the file is not open for writing,
'' .. E_DRIVE_FULL if the flash has no room for the block a byte needs (fewer bytes than the string
''    may be written),
'' .. E_FLASH_TIMEOUT if the flash chip did not finish a write in time (the filesystem is unmounted)

' Local Variables:
' @local writeLength - what write() returned: the bytes written, or its code
' @local strBytes - bytes of the string including its terminator

  strBytes := strsize(p_str) + 1                                                ' include string terminator
  'debug("write_str() [",zstr_(p_str),"](",udec_(strBytes),")")
  writeLength := write(handle, p_str, strBytes)
  if writeLength < 0
    status := writeLength
  elseif writeLength <> strBytes                                                'a short write: error() holds the reason write() stopped
    status := LONG[@errorCode][cogid()]
  else
    status := SUCCESS
  LONG[@errorCode][cogid()] := status                                           'every path leaves its status in error() for this cog


PUB read(handle, p_buffer, count) : bytes_read | status

'' Read count bytes from the file associated with handle into p_buffer
'' -- returns count of bytes read (may be less than requested if reached end of file)
'' -- check for error() == SUCCESS before using contents of p_buffer
'' -- if error() <> SUCCESS then bytes_read is number of bytes read before error occurred
'' -- "bytes_read < expected" indicates an E_END_OF_FILE or another non-SUCCESS value in error()
''
'' @param handle - the handle to the file from which to read bytes
'' @param p_buffer - address of the buffer into which to place the bytes read
'' @param count - the maximum number of bytes to place into the buffer (0 reads nothing and is not
'' .. an error)
'' @returns bytes_read - return style count: the number of bytes actually read from the file (0 when
'' .. the call fails at once)
'' --> If error() <> SUCCESS then it will be one of the following reasons:
'' .. E_NOT_MOUNTED if filesystem has not been mounted,
'' .. E_BAD_HANDLE if the handle is not an open handle,
'' .. E_FILE_MODE if the file is not open for reading (modes "r", "r+" and "w+" read),
'' .. E_BAD_FILE_LENGTH if count is negative (no bytes are read),
'' .. E_END_OF_FILE if attempted read beyond written data,
'' .. E_DRIVE_FULL if a modified "r+"/"w+" block could not be rewritten for lack of a free block
''    (the read stops there, and the block stays modified in the handle),
'' .. E_FLASH_TIMEOUT if the flash chip did not finish the rewrite of a modified "r+"/"w+" block in
''    time (the filesystem is unmounted)

' Local Variables:
' @local status - SUCCESS, or the reason the read stopped

  handle := handle_index(handle)                                                'from here on handle is the index in the handle tables
  bytes_read := 0
  ifnot fsMounted
    status := E_NOT_MOUNTED
  else
    repeat while locktry(fsLock) == 0                                           ' lock for exlusive use

    ifnot fsMounted                                                             'unmount() may have run while this cog waited for the lock
      status := E_NOT_MOUNTED
    else
      status := ensure_handle_mode(handle, H_READ | H_MODIFY)                   ' E_BAD_HANDLE or E_FILE_MODE unless the handle is open for reading, 0 bytes read
      if status == SUCCESS and count < 0                                        ' a negative count reads nothing
        status := E_BAD_FILE_LENGTH
      if status == SUCCESS
        bytes_read, status := rd_bytes_no_locks(handle, p_buffer, count, FALSE) ' the bytes read, and SUCCESS or the reason the read stopped

    'debug("read(", udec_(count),") = (", sdec_(bytes_read),")")

    status := release_lock(status)                                              ' release the lock, we're done with it

  LONG[@errorCode][cogid()] := status                                           'every path leaves its status in error() for this cog


PUB rd_byte(handle) : byte_value | status

'' Read next byte from file associated with handle
'' -- negative value indicates error or end of file
''
'' @param handle - the handle to the file from which to read a byte
'' @returns byte_value - return style value-or-code: the next byte [0-255] from the file, or
'' .. E_NOT_MOUNTED if filesystem has not been mounted,
'' .. E_BAD_HANDLE if the handle is not an open handle,
'' .. E_FILE_MODE if the file is not open for reading,
'' .. E_END_OF_FILE if no more data,
'' .. E_DRIVE_FULL if a modified "r+"/"w+" block could not be rewritten for lack of a free block,
'' .. E_FLASH_TIMEOUT if the flash chip did not finish the rewrite of a modified "r+"/"w+" block in
''    time (the filesystem is unmounted)

' Local Variables:
' @local status - SUCCESS, or the reason no byte was read

  handle := handle_index(handle)                                                'from here on handle is the index in the handle tables
  byte_value := 0                                                               'the byte read lands in the low byte, so the value is 0..255
  ifnot fsMounted
    status := E_NOT_MOUNTED
  else
    repeat while locktry(fsLock) == 0                                           ' lock for exlusive use

    ifnot fsMounted                                                             'unmount() may have run while this cog waited for the lock
      status := E_NOT_MOUNTED
    else
      status := ensure_handle_mode(handle, H_READ | H_MODIFY)                   ' E_BAD_HANDLE or E_FILE_MODE unless the handle is open for reading
      if status == SUCCESS
        _, status := rd_bytes_no_locks(handle, @byte_value, 1, FALSE)           ' read a byte from the file (or seek location), or the reason none was read

    status := release_lock(status)                                              ' release the lock, we're done with it

  if status < 0
    byte_value := status                                                        'a failed read returns its code in place of a byte
  LONG[@errorCode][cogid()] := status                                           'every path leaves its status in error() for this cog


PUB rd_word(handle) : word_value | status, readLength

'' Read next WORD from file associated with the handle
'' -- negative value indicates error or end of file
''
'' @param handle - the handle to the file from which to read a WORD
'' @returns word_value - return style value-or-code: the WORD value read from the file [0-65535],
'' .. or:
'' .. E_NOT_MOUNTED if filesystem has not been mounted,
'' .. E_BAD_HANDLE if the handle is not an open handle,
'' .. E_FILE_MODE if the file is not open for reading,
'' .. E_END_OF_FILE if attempted read beyond written data (fewer than 2 bytes were left),
'' .. E_DRIVE_FULL if a modified "r+"/"w+" block could not be rewritten for lack of a free block,
'' .. E_FLASH_TIMEOUT if the flash chip did not finish the rewrite of a modified "r+"/"w+" block in
''    time (the filesystem is unmounted)

' Local Variables:
' @local status - SUCCESS, or the reason read() stopped
' @local readLength - the bytes read() placed in word_value

  word_value := 0
  readLength := read(handle, @word_value, 2)
  status := LONG[@errorCode][cogid()]                                           ' read() left its reason, SUCCESS when both bytes were read
  if readLength <> 2
    word_value := status                                                        'a short read returns its code in place of a WORD
  LONG[@errorCode][cogid()] := status                                           'every path leaves its status in error() for this cog


PUB rd_long(handle) : long_value | status, readCount

'' Read next LONG from file associated with the handle
'' -- NOTE: negative values can be legitimate values, so
'' -- check for error() == SUCCESS before using value
''
'' @param handle - the handle to the file from which to read a LONG
'' @returns long_value - return style value: the LONG value read from the file (0 when it fails:
'' .. fewer than four bytes are read, and none of the bytes read are returned)
''  error() when not SUCCESS could be:
'' .. E_NOT_MOUNTED if filesystem has not been mounted,
'' .. E_BAD_HANDLE if the handle is not an open handle,
'' .. E_FILE_MODE if the file is not open for reading,
'' .. E_END_OF_FILE if attempted read beyond written data (fewer than 4 bytes were left),
'' .. E_DRIVE_FULL if a modified "r+"/"w+" block could not be rewritten for lack of a free block,
'' .. E_FLASH_TIMEOUT if the flash chip did not finish the rewrite of a modified "r+"/"w+" block in
''    time (the filesystem is unmounted)

' Local Variables:
' @local status - SUCCESS, or the reason read() stopped
' @local readCount - the bytes read() placed in long_value

  long_value := 0
  readCount := read(handle, @long_value, 4)
  status := LONG[@errorCode][cogid()]                                           ' read() left its reason, SUCCESS when all four bytes were read
  if readCount <> 4
    long_value := 0                                                             'fewer than four bytes are no LONG: the bytes read are not returned
  LONG[@errorCode][cogid()] := status                                           'every path leaves its status in error() for this cog


PUB rd_str(handle, p_str, buf_size) : bytes_read | status

'' Read zstring from file at handle into buffer at p_str (buf_size is max length of string +
'' terminator)
'' -- check for error() == SUCCESS before using value
'' -- the buffer is cleared first, and the string is always zero terminated (when buf_size is at
''    least 1): at most buf_size - 1 characters and the terminator are placed in it
'' -- a string whose terminator does not fit in buf_size bytes gives E_TRUNCATED_STRING: buf_size
''    bytes are read from the file, the first buf_size - 1 are placed in the buffer, and the
''    terminator is placed where the last byte read would go, so that byte is not kept
'' -- a file that ends before a terminator gives E_INCOMPLETE_STRING: the bytes read are placed in
''    the buffer and a terminator follows them
''
'' @param handle - the handle to the file from which to read a zstring
'' @param p_str - the address of the buffer into which to place the zstring
'' @param buf_size - the size in bytes of the buffer p_str points to, which holds the string and
'' .. its terminator (0 reads nothing and is not an error)
'' @returns bytes_read - return style count: the number of characters placed into the buffer, not
'' .. counting the terminator (strsize() of the string read)
''  error() when not SUCCESS could be:
'' .. E_NOT_MOUNTED if filesystem has not been mounted,
'' .. E_BAD_HANDLE if the handle is not an open handle,
'' .. E_FILE_MODE if the file is not open for reading,
'' .. E_BAD_FILE_LENGTH if buf_size is negative (no bytes are read, the buffer is untouched),
'' .. E_END_OF_FILE if attempted read beyond written data (nothing was read),
'' .. E_TRUNCATED_STRING if the buffer filled before the string's terminator was read,
'' .. E_INCOMPLETE_STRING if the file ended before the string's terminator,
'' .. E_DRIVE_FULL if a modified "r+"/"w+" block could not be rewritten for lack of a free block,
'' .. E_FLASH_TIMEOUT if the flash chip did not finish the rewrite of a modified "r+"/"w+" block in
''    time (the filesystem is unmounted)

' Local Variables:
' @local status - SUCCESS, or the reason the read stopped

  handle := handle_index(handle)                                                'from here on handle is the index in the handle tables
  bytes_read := 0
  ifnot fsMounted
    status := E_NOT_MOUNTED
  else
    repeat while locktry(fsLock) == 0                                           ' lock for exlusive use

    ifnot fsMounted                                                             'unmount() may have run while this cog waited for the lock
      status := E_NOT_MOUNTED
    else
      status := ensure_handle_mode(handle, H_READ | H_MODIFY)                   ' E_BAD_HANDLE or E_FILE_MODE unless the handle is open for reading, the users buffer is untouched
      if status == SUCCESS and buf_size < 0                                     ' a negative size reads nothing and leaves the users buffer untouched
        status := E_BAD_FILE_LENGTH
      if status == SUCCESS
        bytefill(p_str, 0, buf_size)                                            ' clear the users buffer
        ' every byte is read under the one hold of the lock taken above, so the whole string is read as one call
        bytes_read, status := rd_bytes_no_locks(handle, p_str, buf_size, TRUE)  ' read through the terminator, and no more than buf_size bytes
        if status == E_END_OF_FILE and bytes_read > 0                           ' the file ended before a terminator..
          BYTE[p_str][bytes_read] := 0                                          '..place a 0 terminator after the bytes read
          status := E_INCOMPLETE_STRING
        elseif status == SUCCESS and bytes_read > 0                             ' the last byte read is the terminator, or the byte at the end of the buffer
          bytes_read--                                                          '..which is not counted
          if BYTE[p_str][bytes_read] <> 0                                       '..the buffer filled before a terminator was read
            BYTE[p_str][bytes_read] := 0                                        '....place a 0 terminator at its end in place of that byte
            status := E_TRUNCATED_STRING

    status := release_lock(status)                                              ' release the lock, we're done with it

  LONG[@errorCode][cogid()] := status                                           'every path leaves its status in error() for this cog


PUB directory(p_block_id, p_filename, p_file_size) : status | blockID, block_address, filenameCrcWord, startOfs

'' Get next file's filename and size in bytes via current blockID
'' -- NOTE: p_filename must be address of a 128 byte buffer!
'' -- call until the filename returned is a zero length string: that call reports SUCCESS, a file
''    size of 0 and no file, and the next call reports the same
''
'' @param p_block_id - address of a LONG holding the next block ID to check for a file head. (Set
'' .. the LONG to 0 before the first call; each call advances it)
'' @param p_filename - the filename of the file found (or a zero length string if no more files,
'' .. must be address of 128 byte buffer!)
'' @param p_file_size - address of a LONG that receives the number of bytes in the file found (0
'' .. when no more files)
'' @returns status - return style status: 0 (SUCCESS) if successful,
'' .. E_NOT_MOUNTED if filesystem has not been mounted

' Local Variables:
' @local blockID - the id of the block being checked
' @local block_address - the offset within the file system of the block being checked
' @local filenameCrcWord - the filename CRC word of the head block found: the CRC32 of its filename in an old-format head
' @local startOfs - the file offset of the first data byte position of that head block: 0, or minus its data offset

  ifnot fsMounted
    status := E_NOT_MOUNTED
  else
    repeat while locktry(fsLock) == 0                                           ' lock for exlusive use

    status := SUCCESS                                                           ' new operation

    ifnot fsMounted                                                             'unmount() may have run while this cog waited for the lock
      status := E_NOT_MOUNTED
    else
      BYTE[p_filename][0] := 0                                                  'reset filename
      LONG[p_file_size] := 0                                                    'reset size, both stay so at the end of the list

      repeat while LONG[p_block_id] < BLOCKS                                    'scan any remaining blockID's for file heads
            blockID := LONG[p_block_id]++                                       'get current blockID and post-increment it
            if field[IDValid][blockID]                                          'block ID valid?
              block_address := field[IDToBlock][blockID]                        'yes, get block addr from block ID
              if block_address < BLOCKS                                         'the head of a new "w+" file may have no copy on the flash yet
                if field[BlockState][block_address] == B_HEAD                   'is this a HEAD block?
                  flash_read_block_addr(block_address, p_filename, $008, $087)  'yes, read filename
                  flash_read_block_addr(block_address, @filenameCrcWord, ADDR_HEAD_FN_CRC, ADDR_HEAD_SONAME - 1) '..and the filename CRC word before it
                  startOfs := filenameCrcWord == filename_crc32(p_filename) ? 0 : -(filenameCrcWord.[11..0]) 'old format has no data offset: the name read gives the format
                  LONG[p_file_size], _, _ := count_file_bytes(blockID, startOfs) 'get file size, as file_size() gives it
                  quit

    status := release_lock(status)                                              ' release the lock, we're done with it

  LONG[@errorCode][cogid()] := status                                           'every path leaves its status in error() for this cog


PUB stats() : used_blocks, free_blocks, file_count | status, block_address

'' Get filesystem status: used/free block counts and file count
''
'' @returns used_blocks - return style values (this result is the code when the call fails): the
'' .. number of blocks in use (or E_NOT_MOUNTED if the file system is NOT mounted)
'' @returns free_blocks - the number of free blocks (or 0 if there is an error)
'' @returns file_count - the number of files recorded in filesystem (or 0 if there is an error)

' Local Variables:
' @local status - SUCCESS, or the reason no counts are returned
' @local block_address - the block offset within the file system

  used_blocks := 0
  free_blocks := 0
  file_count := 0

  ifnot fsMounted
    status := E_NOT_MOUNTED
  else
    repeat while locktry(fsLock) == 0                                           ' lock for exlusive use

    status := SUCCESS                                                           ' new operation

    ifnot fsMounted                                                             'unmount() may have run while this cog waited for the lock
      status := E_NOT_MOUNTED
    else
      repeat BLOCKS with block_address
        case field[BlockState][block_address]
          B_FREE: free_blocks++
          B_TEMP: used_blocks++
          B_HEAD: used_blocks++
                  file_count++
          B_BODY: used_blocks++

    status := release_lock(status)                                              ' release the lock, we're done with it

  if status < 0
    used_blocks := status                                                       'a failed call returns its code in place of the used count
  LONG[@errorCode][cogid()] := status                                           'every path leaves its status in error() for this cog


PUB string_for_error(status) : p_interpretation

'' Return an address of a zstring describing the error code
'' -- a code the driver does not define gives the text "???: Unknown error code ???"
'' -- does not change error()
''
'' @param status - the error code to translate
'' @returns p_interpretation - return style value: address of the zstring that interprets the
'' .. errcode

    case status
        SUCCESS:                p_interpretation := @"SUCCESS: No error"
        E_BAD_HANDLE:           p_interpretation := @"E_BAD_HANDLE: Handle is invalid"
        E_NO_HANDLE:            p_interpretation := @"E_NO_HANDLE: Out of available handles"
        E_FILE_NOT_FOUND:       p_interpretation := @"E_FILE_NOT_FOUND: File not present"
        E_DRIVE_FULL:           p_interpretation := @"E_DRIVE_FULL: Out of space on flash chip"
        E_FILE_WRITING:         p_interpretation := @"E_FILE_WRITING: File is open for writing"
        E_FILE_READING:         p_interpretation := @"E_FILE_READING: File is open for reading"
        E_FILE_OPEN:            p_interpretation := @"E_FILE_OPEN: File is open"
        E_FILE_EXISTS:          p_interpretation := @"E_FILE_EXISTS: the File exists"
        E_END_OF_FILE:          p_interpretation := @"E_END_OF_FILE: no more data available, at end of file"
        E_FILE_MODE:            p_interpretation := @"E_FILE_MODE: file not opened in desired mode"
        E_FILE_SEEK:            p_interpretation := @"E_FILE_SEEK: Attempted seek past either end of file"
        E_BAD_BLOCKS_REMOVED:   p_interpretation := @"E_BAD_BLOCKS_REMOVED: Block bit failure detected, bad blocks removed"
        E_NO_LOCK_AVAIL:        p_interpretation := @"E_NO_LOCK_AVAIL: Unable to obtain a LOCK for driver use"
        E_TRUNCATED_STRING:     p_interpretation := @"E_TRUNCATED_STRING: Buffer full, before reaching string terminator"
        E_INCOMPLETE_STRING:    p_interpretation := @"E_INCOMPLETE_STRING: End of file reached before string terminator"
        E_SHORT_TRANSER:        p_interpretation := @"E_SHORT_TRANSER: Too few bytes read or written"
        E_NOT_MOUNTED:          p_interpretation := @"E_NOT_MOUNTED: Filesystem NOT yet accessible"
        E_BAD_FILE_LENGTH:      p_interpretation := @"E_BAD_FILE_LENGTH: File length is negative or zero"
        E_BAD_SEEK_ARG:         p_interpretation := @"E_BAD_SEEK_ARG: Invalid seek argument"
        E_BAD_FILENAME:         p_interpretation := @"E_BAD_FILENAME: Filename is a null pointer, empty or longer than 127 characters"
        E_FLASH_TIMEOUT:        p_interpretation := @"E_FLASH_TIMEOUT: Flash chip did not finish an erase or program in time, filesystem unmounted"
        other:                  p_interpretation := @"???: Unknown error code ???"



CON ' --- Private Methods ---

CON ' >>>  parameter type (p_filename)  <<<

PRI finish_open_read(p_filename, max_file_length, signature) : handle | block_id, lenInBytes, offsetInBytes, bNeedSeek

' Open a file for reading, returning handle if success
'
' @param p_filename - address of a zstring containing the filename
' @param max_file_length - the circular file length limit in bytes, 0 for a file with no limit
' @param signature - the first long of the head block of the file of this name, as get_file_head_signature() returned it, or 0 when there is none
' @returns handle - handle to open file if successful,
' .. or E_FILE_NOT_FOUND if file doesn't exist,
' .. or E_NO_HANDLE if no handle is available,

' Local Variables:
' @local block_id - the head block id of the file, then the block an old-format circular read starts in
' @local lenInBytes - the length of an old-format circular file
' @local offsetInBytes - the file offset of the first byte an old-format circular read keeps
' @local bNeedSeek - TRUE when the handle starts at the first byte of the file

  'debug("* finish_open_read([", zstr_(p_filename), "], bytes=", udec_(max_file_length), ") - ENTRY")
  ifnot signature                                                               'if file doesn't exist, abort
    handle := (LONG[@errorCode][cogid()] := E_FILE_NOT_FOUND)
  else
    bNeedSeek := true
    handle := new_handle(p_filename)                                            'get new handle, E_NO_HANDLE if none is available
    if handle >= 0                                                              'no handle: nothing else is touched, error() holds E_NO_HANDLE
      hCircularLength[handle] := max_file_length                                'set size limit if non-zero
      hStatus[handle] := H_READ                                                 'set handle status to READ
      block_id := signature.[19..8]                                             'get head ID for use by Seek()
      hHeadBlockID[handle] := block_id                                          'get head ID for use by Seek()
      ' respond to special internal use isOldFormat (v1.4) file!
      if max_file_length > 0 and signature.[2] == 0
      ' calculate file offset the v1.4 way...
      '  we don't have data offset in file head block so calculate it
        lenInBytes, _, _ := count_file_bytes(block_id, head_data_start_of_format(block_id, TRUE)) 'get file length in bytes: an old-format head has no data offset
        if showRTdebug
          debug("*** OLD format circular read! ", udec(lenInBytes, max_file_length))
        if lenInBytes > max_file_length
          bNeedSeek := false                                                    'is file longer than requested length?
          offsetInBytes := lenInBytes - max_file_length                         'get offset to start of data in file
          hWindowStart[handle] := offsetInBytes                                 'seek positions of this handle count from the start of the data
          block_id, hEndPtr[handle], _ := locate_file_byte(block_id, offsetInBytes) 'reqest position beyond end to get last byte/block in file
          flash_read_block_id(block_id, buffer_pointer(handle), $000, $FFF)     'read new block into buffer
              'debug(" open_read() ", udec(offsetInBytes, block_address, endPtr))
      if bNeedSeek
        seek_no_locks(handle, 0)                                                'seek to start of file

  'debug(" -- open_read() freed sem #", udec_(fsLock))
  handle := release_lock(handle)                                                ' release the lock, we're done with it


PRI finish_open_write(p_filename, max_file_length, signature) : handle | head_block_id

' Open a file for (re)writing, returning handle if success
' -- (overwrites existing file, if you wish to prevent overwrite, use exists() to check!)
' -- an existing file stays on the flash, untouched, until close() replaces it, or deletes it when nothing was
'    written
' -- a new file takes a free block ID for its head block before anything else changes; with none free,
'    no handle is taken and E_DRIVE_FULL is returned
'
' @param p_filename - address of a zstring containing the filename
' @param max_file_length - the circular file length limit in bytes, 0 for a file with no limit
' @param signature - the first long of the head block of the file of this name, as get_file_head_signature() returned it, or 0 when there is none
' @returns handle - handle to open file if successful, E_NO_HANDLE if no handle is available,
' .. or E_DRIVE_FULL if a new file has no free block ID for its head block

' Local Variables:
' @local head_block_id - the head block id of a new file
    'debug("* finish_open_write(", zstr_(p_filename), ", bytes=", udec_(max_file_length), ") - ENTRY")

  head_block_id := 0
  ifnot signature                                                               'a new file needs a free block ID first
    head_block_id := next_available_block_id()

  if head_block_id < 0                                                          'no free block ID: nothing was changed, error() holds E_DRIVE_FULL
    handle := head_block_id
  else
    handle := new_handle(p_filename)                                            'get new handle, E_NO_HANDLE if none is available
    if handle >= 0                                                              'no handle: nothing else is touched, error() holds E_NO_HANDLE
      hCircularLength[handle] := max_file_length                                'set size limit if non-zero

      if signature
        'file already exists, overwrite it
        start_write(handle, H_APPEND, signature.[19..8], next_active_cycle(signature.[7..5]))
        hReplacedID[handle] := signature.[19..8]                                'close() deletes it if nothing is written
      else                          'else, write it
        start_write(handle, H_WRITE, head_block_id, %011)
        ' NO, we don't write empty files!
        ' hModified[handle]~~                 'force first block to be written in case no data
        'debug("open() WRITE ", uhex_word(hEndPtr[handle], handle))

  'debug(" -- open_write() freed sem #", udec_(fsLock))
  handle := release_lock(handle)                                              ' release the lock, we're done with it


PRI finish_open_append(p_filename, max_file_length, signature) : handle | head_block_id

' Open for append, returning handle if success
' -- NOTE: this is called only if file already exists
' -- (if it didn't exist finish_open_write() would have been called instead)
' -- a new file takes a free block ID for its head block before anything else changes; with none free,
'    no handle is taken and E_DRIVE_FULL is returned
'
' @param p_filename - address of a zstring containing the filename
' @param max_file_length - the circular file length limit in bytes, 0 for a file with no limit
' @param signature - the first long of the head block of the file of this name, as get_file_head_signature() returned it, or 0 when there is none
' @returns handle - handle to open file if successful, E_NO_HANDLE if no handle is available,
' .. or E_DRIVE_FULL if a new file has no free block ID for its head block

' Local Variables:
' @local head_block_id - the head block id of a new file

  'debug("* finish_open_append(", zstr_(p_filename), ", bytes=", udec_(max_file_length), ") - ENTRY")

  head_block_id := 0
  ifnot signature                                                               'a new file needs a free block ID first
    head_block_id := next_available_block_id()

  if head_block_id < 0                                                          'no free block ID: nothing was changed, error() holds E_DRIVE_FULL
    handle := head_block_id
  else
    'debug("finish_open_append() get handle")
    handle := new_handle(p_filename)                                            'get new handle, E_NO_HANDLE if none is available
    if handle >= 0                                                              'no handle: nothing else is touched, error() holds E_NO_HANDLE
      hCircularLength[handle] := max_file_length                                'set size limit if non-zero

      if signature                                                              'if file already exists, append it
        start_modify(handle, H_APPEND, signature.[19..8], $FFFFFF, true)
      else                          'else, write it
        start_write(handle, H_WRITE, head_block_id, %011)
        ' NO, we don't write empty files!
        'hModified[handle]~~                                                    'force first block to be written in case no data

  handle := release_lock(handle)                                                ' release the lock, we're done with it


PRI finish_open_readwrite(p_filename, bNewFile, signature) : handle | head_block_id, pBuff
' Open a file for reading and writing, returns handle
' -- "r+" (bNewFile FALSE) opens the existing file, to modify it in place and extend it at its end (no gaps)
' -- "w+" (bNewFile TRUE) starts a new file, which an existing file of the same name does not change: that file
'    stays on the flash, untouched, until close() replaces it with the new file, or deletes it when nothing was written
' -- a new file takes a free block ID for its head block before anything else changes; with none free,
'    no handle is taken and E_DRIVE_FULL is returned
' -- the head block of a new file is built in the buffer, holding no data, and has no copy on the flash until
'    its first rewrite: IDToBlock holds an address outside the file system for it, so that rewrite cancels nothing.
'    Every copy of it stays inactive on the flash until close() or flush() commits the file
'
' @param p_filename - address of a zstring containing the filename
' @param bNewFile - TRUE for "w+": start a new file, which replaces an existing file at close
' @param signature - the first long of the head block of the file of this name, as get_file_head_signature() returned it, or 0 when there is none
' @returns handle - handle to open file, E_NO_HANDLE if no handle is available,
' .. or E_DRIVE_FULL if a new file has no free block ID for its head block

' Local Variables:
' @local head_block_id - id of block being checked
' @local pBuff - the address of the 4KB buffer for the new file's head block

  head_block_id := 0
  if bNewFile or signature == 0                                                 'a new file needs a free block ID first
    head_block_id := next_available_block_id()                                  'get initial ID

  if head_block_id < 0                                                          'no free block ID: nothing was changed, error() holds E_DRIVE_FULL
    handle := head_block_id
  else
    handle := new_handle(p_filename)                                            'get new handle, E_NO_HANDLE if none is available
    if handle >= 0                                                              'no handle: nothing else is touched, error() holds E_NO_HANDLE
      if signature and not bNewFile                                             'if "r+" of a file that exists
        ' file exists, allow modification and append-only extension (no gaps)
        start_modify(handle, H_READWRITE, signature.[19..8], 0, true)
      else
        ' a new file, allow modification after append-only extension (no gaps)
        ' no starting block-id means create new head!
        pBuff := buffer_pointer(handle)                                         'get block buffer pointer
        build_head_block(pBuff, filename_pointer(handle), head_block_id)        'build head block in buffer
        long[pBuff].[31..20] := $088                                            'EndPtr at the first data byte: the new file holds no data
        field[IDToBlock][head_block_id] := BLOCKS                               'the head has no copy on the flash yet
        start_modify(handle, H_READWRITE, head_block_id, 0, false)              'go to start of file
        hHeadPending[handle] := TRUE                                            'the head stays inactive until the file is committed
        if signature
          hReplacedID[handle] := signature.[19..8]                              'the existing file that the commit replaces

  handle := release_lock(handle)                                                ' release the lock, we're done with it


PRI valid_filename(p_filename) : bValid

' Determine if a filename can name a file: a non-null pointer to a zstring of 1 to FILENAME_SIZE - 1 characters
' -- (the pointer is tested before the string is measured, so a null pointer is never dereferenced)
'
' @param p_filename - address of a zstring containing the filename
' @returns bValid - True/False where True means the filename is usable

  bValid := false
  if p_filename <> 0
    bValid := strsize(p_filename) > 0 and strsize(p_filename) < FILENAME_SIZE


PRI exists_no_lock(p_filename) : bool

' Determine if named file is present in the file system
' -- (internal version - for use when caller has already grabbed lock)
'
' @param p_filename - address of a zstring containing the filename
' @returns bool - True/False where True means the file exists

  bool := get_file_head_signature(p_filename) ? true : false


PRI get_file_head_signature(p_filename) : foundSignature | nameCrc19, nameCrc32, block_address, signature[2], bIsOldFmt

' Look up file by name and return the first long of the file's head block (or 0 if file not found)
'
' The long at $004 of a head block is its filename CRC word. A head block this driver writes holds the CRC19 of the
' filename in its upper 20 bits (and the data offset below them); an old-format head block holds the CRC32 of the
' filename, terminator included, in the whole word. Both CRCs of the name are computed once, and only a head block
' whose word matches one of them is read for its filename, which must then equal the name. A block whose name is
' the name always matches, so no file is missed, and the name comparison makes every match exact. The head block is
' old format when its word is the CRC32 of the name, the same test locate_file_byte() makes on it.
'
' @param p_filename - address of a zstring containing the filename
' @returns foundSignature - the first long of the head block (or 0 if file not found); bits .[4..2] of a head block
' .. are unused on the flash, and .[2] of the value returned is 0 for an old-format head block and 1 otherwise

' Local Variables:
' @local nameCrc19 - the CRC19 of the filename, as a head block this driver writes holds it
' @local nameCrc32 - the CRC32 of the filename, as an old-format head block holds it
' @local block_address - the block offset within the file system
' @local signature[2] - the first long of the block and its filename CRC word
' @local bIsOldFmt - TRUE when the head block found is old format

  foundSignature := 0
  bIsOldFmt := FALSE
  nameCrc19 := filename_crc(p_filename)
  nameCrc32 := filename_crc32(p_filename)

  repeat BLOCKS with block_address                                              'scan head blocks for filename
    if field[BlockState][block_address] == B_HEAD                               'if this is a head block..
      flash_read_block_addr(block_address, @signature, $000, $007)              '..read its first long and its filename CRC word
      if signature[1].[31..12] == nameCrc19 or signature[1] == nameCrc32        '..a CRC of the name matches: read the filename to confirm it
        flash_read_block_addr(block_address, @tmpBlockBuffer, ADDR_HEAD_SONAME, ADDR_HEAD_DATA - 1)
        if strcomp(p_filename, @tmpBlockBuffer)                                 '..the filename is the name
          foundSignature := signature[0]                                        '..the first long of a block is never zero
          bIsOldFmt := signature[1] == nameCrc32
          quit

  if foundSignature <> 0                                                        'tell the caller the format of the head block
    foundSignature.[2] := bIsOldFmt ? 0 : 1


PRI build_head_block(pBuff, p_filename, head_block_id)

' initialize empty block with control information
'
' @param pBuff - address of block in RAM
' @param p_filename - address of a zstring containing the filename
' @param head_block_id - the head block id for this new file

  bytefill(pBuff, $FF, BLOCK_SIZE)                                              'erase block buffer to build new head block
  long[pBuff].[1..0] := %00                                                     'set head/last
  long[pBuff].[19..8] := head_block_id                                          'set head block ID
  long[pBuff][1].[11..0] := $000                                                'clear data offset
  long[pBuff][1].[31..12] := filename_crc(p_filename)                           'set filename CRC
  bytefill(pBuff + $008, $E5, FILENAME_SIZE)                                    'erase filename portion of block
  strcopy(pBuff + $008, p_filename, FILENAME_SIZE - 1)                          'set filename


PRI is_file_open(p_filename, open_mode_bits) : result | handle

' Return true if named file is open
'
' @param p_filename - address of a zstring containing the filename
' @param open_mode_bits - some combination of H_READ, H_WRITE, H_FORK and H_MODIFY
' @returns result - True/False where True means the file is open

' Local Variables:
' @local handle - temporary handle to check for availability

  result := FALSE
  repeat MAX_FILES_OPEN with handle                                             'for each handle is already open?
    if hStatus[handle] & open_mode_bits
      if strcomp(@hFilename + handle * FILENAME_SIZE, p_filename)
        result := TRUE
        quit
{
      else
        debug("is_open() no filename match ", zstr_(p_filename), " vs ", zstr_(@hFilename + handle * FILENAME_SIZE))
    else
      debug("is_open() no mode match ", uhex_byte(hStatus[handle], open_mode_bits))
'}

PRI new_handle(p_filename) : handle | possible_handle

' Calculate and return next available handle
'
' @returns handle - the next available handle, or
' .. E_NO_HANDLE if no handle is available

' Local Variables:
' @local possible_handle - temporary handle to check for availability

  handle := E_NO_HANDLE                                                         'if no handle is available... return this
  repeat MAX_FILES_OPEN with possible_handle                                    'find first free handle
    ifnot hStatus[possible_handle]                                              'if handle not in use
      handle := possible_handle                                                 '..select as handle to use
      fsFreeHndlCt--
      quit                                                                      '..exit loop, we have our answer

  'debug("new_handle() = ", sdec(handle))
  if handle < 0                                                                 'if error, set error code
    LONG[@errorCode][cogid()] := handle
  else
    'record the filename for this handle
    ' NOTE this buffer is $00-filled while in our blocks they are $FF-filled
    bytefill(@hFilename + handle * FILENAME_SIZE, 0, FILENAME_SIZE)             ' empty filename buffer
    strcopy(@hFilename + handle * FILENAME_SIZE, p_filename, FILENAME_SIZE - 1) ' copy new filename into buffer
    hHeadPending[handle] := FALSE                                               ' a handle starts with no new head and replaces no file,
    hTrimPending[handle] := FALSE                                               ' .. owes no trim,
    hReplacedID[handle] := NOT_VALID                                            ' .. whatever a handle abandoned by mount() left here
    hWindowStart[handle] := 0                                                   ' and its positions count from the first byte of the file
    hCacheBlockID[handle] := NO_CACHED_BLOCK                                    ' its seek cache holds no block of a file it had open before


PRI filename_crc(p_filename) : filenameCRC

' Return the CRC19 value calculated for the filename zstring
'
' @param p_filename - address of a zstring containing the filename
' @returns filenameCRC - the calculated CRC value

  filenameCRC := getcrc(p_filename, $B5827 rev 19, strsize(p_filename))         'compute CRC of filename


PRI filename_crc32(p_filename) : filenameCRC

' Return the CRC32 value calculated for the filename zstring, terminator included, as an old-format head block holds it
'
' @param p_filename - address of a zstring containing the filename
' @returns filenameCRC - the calculated CRC value

  filenameCRC := getcrc(p_filename, $AD0424F3 rev 31, strsize(p_filename) + 1)  'compute CRC of filename and its terminator



CON ' >>>  parameter type (handle)  <<<

PRI start_write(handle, open_mode, head_block_id, head_cycle)

' configure file for H_WRITE or H_APPEND
'
' @param handle - a handle to an open file
' @param open_mode - desired open mode
' @param head_block_id - the head block id for this new file
' @param head_cycle - the lifecycle the first block the handle writes is programmed with

  build_head_block(buffer_pointer(handle), filename_pointer(handle), head_block_id) 'build head block in buffer

  hStatus[handle] := open_mode                                                  'set status
  hHeadBlockID[handle] := head_block_id                                         'set head block ID
  hChainBlockID[handle] := head_block_id                                        'set fork block ID to head block ID
  hChainLifeCycle[handle] := head_cycle                                         'set fork cycle to head cycle
  hEndPtr[handle] := $088                                                       'point to first byte in head block
  hCacheBlockID[handle] := NO_CACHED_BLOCK                                      'the seek cache starts empty for the file the handle now has


PRI start_modify(handle, open_mode, head_block_id, file_position, bFileExists) | block_id, pBuff

' configure file for H_APPEND or H_READWRITE
'
' @param handle - a handle to an open file
' @param open_mode - desired open mode
' @param head_block_id - the head block id for this new file
' @param file_position - the file offset the handle starts at ($FFFFFF for the end of the file)
' @param bFileExists - TRUE when the file is on the flash, FALSE for a new file whose head block is already in the buffer

' Local Variables:
' @local block_id - temporary block id
' @local pBuff - a temporary pointer to the handles block buffer

    'debug("* srt_modify() ", udec(handle, head_block_id, file_position))

    hCacheBlockID[handle] := NO_CACHED_BLOCK                                    'the seek cache starts empty for the file the handle now has
    pBuff := buffer_pointer(handle)                                             'get block buffer pointer
    if bFileExists                                                              'if file exists... (new file block is already in buffer)
      block_id, hEndPtr[handle], hSeekFileOffset[handle] := locate_file_byte(head_block_id, file_position)    'locate block and block pointer by file_position
      flash_read_block_id(block_id, pBuff, $000, $FFF)                          '.. read located block into buffer
      if open_mode == H_READWRITE                                               '.. if read/modify/write
        hSeekPtr[handle] := hEndPtr[handle]                                     '.... enable seek
    else
      hSeekPtr[handle] := hEndPtr[handle] := $088                               'new file, seek is enabled and
      hSeekFileOffset[handle] := 0                                              'file offset starts at zero

    hStatus[handle] := open_mode                                                'set status
    hHeadBlockID[handle] := head_block_id                                       'set head block ID
    hChainBlockID[handle] := block_id                                           'set fork block ID to located block ID
    hChainLifeCycle[handle] := next_active_cycle(long[pBuff].[7..5])            'set fork cycle to next cycle of located block
    'debug(" -- ", uhex_word(hChainBlockAddr[handle]), udec(block_id), uhex_word(hEndPtr[handle]), udec(hSeekFileOffset[handle]))


PRI rd_bytes_no_locks(handle, p_buffer, count, bToTerminator) : bytes_read, status | pBuff, signature, bSeeking, endPtr, runLength, bTerminated, scanIdx

' Read up to count bytes from the file associated with handle into p_buffer, moving one run of bytes per block
'
' Each run is copied with BYTEMOVE out of the block buffer: as many bytes as are still wanted, no more than the
' buffered block holds before the end of its data area, and in the last block no more than the file holds. The next
' block is read only when another byte is wanted from it, so a read that ends at the end of a block leaves that
' block in the buffer. In modify mode a modified block is rewritten before the next block is read. With no free
' block for the rewrite the read stops where it is, the block stays in the buffer still modified, and the status is
' E_DRIVE_FULL. The seek pointer, when it is in use, or else the end pointer moves with every run.
'
' With bToTerminator TRUE the bytes of each run are scanned in the block buffer before they are moved, and the run
' ends at the first 0 byte: the read stops just past that terminator, which is the last byte moved.
'
' @param handle - the handle to the file from which to read bytes
' @param p_buffer - address of the buffer into which to place the bytes read
' @param count - the maximum number of bytes to place into the buffer (0 or below reads nothing and is not an error)
' @param bToTerminator - TRUE to stop just past the first 0 byte read, FALSE to read count bytes
' @returns bytes_read - the number of bytes actually read from the file
' @returns status - SUCCESS when count bytes were read, or the reason the read stopped:
' .. E_END_OF_FILE if no more data,
' .. E_FILE_MODE if read not allowed for this file,
' .. E_DRIVE_FULL if a modified block could not be rewritten,
' .. E_FLASH_TIMEOUT if the flash chip did not finish the rewrite in time (the read stops at the one exit)

' Local Variables:
' @local pBuff - the address of the 4KB buffer for the file associated with this handle
' @local signature - the first long of the buffered block: its type bits and its NextID or EndPtr
' @local bSeeking - TRUE when the seek pointer is in use in place of the end pointer
' @local endPtr - offset in the buffered block of the next byte to read
' @local runLength - the count of bytes one run moves out of the buffered block
' @local bTerminated - TRUE once a run has ended at a terminator
' @local scanIdx - the index in a run of the byte being checked for a terminator

  bytes_read := 0
  status := SUCCESS
  bTerminated := FALSE
  if count > 0                                                                  'a count of zero or below moves nothing
    if hStatus[handle] <> H_READ and hStatus[handle] <> H_READWRITE
      status := E_FILE_MODE                                                     'read not allowed, nothing is moved
    else
      bSeeking := hSeekPtr[handle] <> NOT_ENABLED                               'is the seek pointer in use?
      endPtr := bSeeking ? hSeekPtr[handle] : hEndPtr[handle]
      pBuff := buffer_pointer(handle)
      repeat
        runLength := 0
        signature := LONG[pBuff]
        if signature.[0] and endPtr == ADDR_DATA_END                            'the data of a block that has a next block is used up..
          if (hStatus[handle] & H_MODIFY) and hModified[handle]                 '..in modify mode a modified block is rewritten first (might move a block)
            status := rewrite_block(handle)
            if status == SUCCESS
              hModified[handle]~
          if status == SUCCESS
            flash_read_block_addr(field[IDToBlock][signature.[31..20]], pBuff, 0, BLOCK_SIZE - 1) '..load the next block
            endPtr := ADDR_BODY_DATA                                            '..its first data byte
            signature := LONG[pBuff]
        if status == SUCCESS
          runLength := ((signature.[0] ? ADDR_DATA_END : signature.[31..20]) - endPtr) #> 0 <# (count - bytes_read)
          if runLength == 0                                                     'the last block holds no more data
            status := E_END_OF_FILE
          else
            if bToTerminator                                                    'a string read: the run ends at the first terminator in it
              repeat runLength with scanIdx
                if BYTE[pBuff][endPtr + scanIdx] == 0
                  runLength := scanIdx + 1
                  bTerminated := TRUE
                  quit
            bytemove(p_buffer + bytes_read, pBuff + endPtr, runLength)
            endPtr += runLength
            bytes_read += runLength
        if bSeeking == TRUE                                                     'the pointer names the block now in the buffer, after every pass
          hSeekPtr[handle] := endPtr
          hSeekFileOffset[handle] += runLength                                  '..and the seek offset counts every byte read
        else
          hEndPtr[handle] := endPtr
        if status <> SUCCESS                                                    'the one exit from the loop on a failure: whatever a pass leaves in status (the end
          quit                                                                  '..of the file, a next block that could not be reached) stops the read here, the bytes already moved kept
      while bytes_read < count and bTerminated == FALSE


PRI wr_bytes_no_locks(handle, p_buffer, count) : bytes_written, status | pBuff, nextBlockID, bSeeking, endPtr, newBlockAddress, runLength

' Write up to count bytes from p_buffer to a file that is open for write or rewrite, moving one run of bytes per block
'
' Each run is copied with BYTEMOVE into the block buffer: as many bytes as are still to be written, and no more than
' fit before the end of the block's data area. The next block is started only when another byte is to be written,
' so a write that ends at the end of a block leaves that block full in the buffer.
'
' A full block is written to the flash only when the next block can follow it: a free block ID for the next block,
' and a free block left over for it once this one is written. Otherwise the write stops where it is, the full block
' stays in the buffer for close() to write, and the status is E_DRIVE_FULL. In modify mode a modified block that
' cannot be rewritten for lack of a free block stays in the buffer, still modified, with the same status.
'
' In modify mode a write at or past the end of the file grows it, as in C. Within the last block the EndPtr moves
' with the write. At the end of a full last block a new last block holding the next byte is written and activated
' first, then the full block is rewritten with a NextID link to it, so the chain on the flash is whole at every
' step. That needs a free block ID and two free blocks; without them the write stops where it is, nothing more
' changes, and the status is E_DRIVE_FULL.
'
' @param handle - handle to a file that is open for write or rewrite
' @param p_buffer - the address of the buffer containing the users' data to write
' @param count - the number of bytes to write to the file (0 or below writes nothing and is not an error)
' @returns bytes_written - the count of bytes written to the file
' @returns status - SUCCESS when count bytes were written, or the reason the write stopped:
' .. E_FILE_MODE if the file is not open for writing,
' .. E_DRIVE_FULL if the flash has no room for the block the next byte needs,
' .. E_FLASH_TIMEOUT if the flash chip did not finish a write in time (the write stops at the one exit, and
'    nothing written is undone)

' Local Variables:
' @local pBuff - the address of the 4KB buffer for the file associated with this handle
' @local nextBlockID - block ID of the next block to write to the file
' @local bSeeking - TRUE when the seek pointer is in use in place of the end pointer
' @local endPtr - offset in the buffered block of the next byte to write
' @local newBlockAddress - the block offset within the file system of the new last block of a growing file
' @local runLength - the count of bytes one run moves into the buffered block

  bytes_written := 0
  status := SUCCESS
  if count > 0                                                                  'a count of zero or below moves nothing
    if hStatus[handle] <> H_WRITE and hStatus[handle] <> H_APPEND and hStatus[handle] <> H_READWRITE
      status := E_FILE_MODE                                                     'write not allowed, nothing is moved
    else
      bSeeking := hSeekPtr[handle] <> NOT_ENABLED                               'is the seek pointer in use?
      endPtr := bSeeking ? hSeekPtr[handle] : hEndPtr[handle]
      pBuff := buffer_pointer(handle)
      repeat
        runLength := 0
        if endPtr >= ADDR_DATA_END and hStatus[handle] <> H_READWRITE           'write/rewrite/append mode, and the block is full..
          nextBlockID := next_available_block_id()                              '..get next ID to link to
          if nextBlockID < 0                                                    '..no free block ID: error() holds E_DRIVE_FULL
            status := nextBlockID
          else
            status := write_block(handle, nextBlockID, true)                    '..write current full block with NextID link
            if status < 0                                                       '..no free block for it and the next (E_DRIVE_FULL), or the flash failed (E_FLASH_TIMEOUT)
              field[IDValid][nextBlockID]~                                      '....release the ID that got no block
            else
              bytefill(pBuff, $FF, BLOCK_SIZE)                                  '..erase block buffer to build new body block
              long[pBuff].[0]~                                                  '..make last block
              long[pBuff].[19..8] := nextBlockID                                '..set ID
              endPtr := ADDR_BODY_DATA                                          '..point to start of data in new block
        elseif endPtr >= ADDR_DATA_END                                          'modify mode, and the block is full..
          if long[pBuff].[0] == 0                                               '..and if it is the last block, the file grows into a new last block
            nextBlockID := next_available_block_id()                            '....get the ID of the new last block
            if nextBlockID < 0                                                  '....no free block ID: error() holds E_DRIVE_FULL
              status := nextBlockID
            else
              newBlockAddress := next_block_address(NEXT_BLOCK_SPARE)           '....get its block, keeping one for the rewrite of this block
              if newBlockAddress < 0                                            '....no free block for both (E_DRIVE_FULL), or a block move failed (E_FLASH_TIMEOUT)
                status := newBlockAddress
                field[IDValid][nextBlockID]~                                    '......release the ID that got no block
              else
                bytefill(@tmpBlockBuffer, $FF, BLOCK_SIZE)                      '....build the new last block, holding the next byte
                LONG[@tmpBlockBuffer].[1..0] := %10                             '......body/last
                LONG[@tmpBlockBuffer].[19..8] := nextBlockID                    '......set ID
                LONG[@tmpBlockBuffer].[31..20] := ADDR_BODY_DATA + 1            '......EndPtr after its one data byte
                BYTE[@tmpBlockBuffer][ADDR_BODY_DATA] := BYTE[p_buffer][bytes_written] '......its data byte
                flash_program_block(newBlockAddress, @tmpBlockBuffer, %011)     '....write and activate it before any block links to it
                flash_activate_block(newBlockAddress, %011)
                if fsDeviceFault                                                '....the flash failed: the write stops here, as a power loss here leaves it
                  status := E_FLASH_TIMEOUT
                else
                  field[BlockState][newBlockAddress] := B_BODY
                  field[IDToBlock][nextBlockID] := newBlockAddress
                  long[pBuff].[0] := 1                                          '....this block now has a next block..
                  long[pBuff].[31..20] := nextBlockID                           '....and its NextID replaces its EndPtr
                  status := rewrite_block(handle)                               '....rewrite this block with the link (might move a block)
                  if status == SUCCESS
                    hModified[handle]~
                  elseif fsDeviceFault == FALSE                                 '....no block for the rewrite: undo the new last block (after a flash failure nothing is undone)
                    long[pBuff].[0] := 0                                        '......this block is the last block again..
                    long[pBuff].[31..20] := endPtr                              '......full to its end
                    flash_cancel_block(newBlockAddress)
                    field[BlockState][newBlockAddress] := B_FREE
                    field[IDValid][nextBlockID]~                                '......release the ID
          elseif hModified[handle]                                              '..else if block was modified
            status := rewrite_block(handle)                                     '..then rewrite block (might move a block)
            if status == SUCCESS
              hModified[handle]~
          if status == SUCCESS
            flash_read_block_id(long[pBuff].[31..20], pBuff, 0, BLOCK_SIZE - 1) '..read next block (a new last block already holds the next byte)
            endPtr := ADDR_BODY_DATA                                            '..point to start of data in next block
        if status == SUCCESS
          runLength := (ADDR_DATA_END - endPtr) <# (count - bytes_written)      'the bytes that fit in this block
          hModified[handle]~~                                                   'set modified flag
          bytemove(pBuff + endPtr, p_buffer + bytes_written, runLength)
          endPtr += runLength
          bytes_written += runLength
          if hStatus[handle] == H_READWRITE and long[pBuff].[0] == 0 and endPtr > long[pBuff].[31..20]
            long[pBuff].[31..20] := endPtr                                      'a write past the end of the last block moves its EndPtr: the file grows
        if bSeeking == TRUE                                                     'the pointer names the block now in the buffer, after every pass
          hSeekPtr[handle] := endPtr
          hSeekFileOffset[handle] += runLength                                  '..and the seek offset counts every byte written
        else
          hEndPtr[handle] := endPtr
        if status <> SUCCESS                                                    'the one exit from the loop on a failure: whatever a pass leaves in status (a next
          quit                                                                  '..block that could not be started) stops the write here, the bytes already written kept
      while bytes_written < count


PRI seek_no_locks(handle, file_position) : status | block_id, endPtr, fileOffset

' seek file associted with handle to new position: locate it with seek_locate(), then move there with seek_to()
' -- a position past the end of the file is the end of the file
'
' @param handle - handle to open file
' @param file_position - desired file postion
' @returns status - 0 (SUCCESS) if the position was set, E_DRIVE_FULL if a modified block could not be rewritten,
' .. E_FLASH_TIMEOUT if the flash chip did not finish that rewrite in time

' Local Variables:
' @local block_id - the block holding the located position
' @local endPtr - offset within the located block of the byte at file_position
' @local fileOffset - the position within the file that was located

    block_id, endPtr, fileOffset := seek_locate(handle, file_position)
    status := seek_to(handle, block_id, endPtr, fileOffset)


PRI seek_locate(handle, file_position) : block_id, endPtr, fileOffset | pBuff, extraBytes

' Locate a position in the file a handle has open, changing neither the handle's position nor the flash
'
' A position past the end of the file is the end of the file, so fileOffset is file_position or the file length,
' whichever is less. The head block of a new "w+" file with no copy on the flash yet is the whole file, and the
' position is found in the buffer without reading the flash. Otherwise locate_handle_byte() walks the chain on the
' flash. In modify mode, when the located block is the last block and is the one in the buffer, bytes written to it
' and not yet on the flash are part of the file and the position can lie in them.
'
' @param handle - handle to open file
' @param file_position - desired file postion
' @returns block_id - the block holding the located position
' @returns endPtr - offset within the located block of the byte at file_position
' @returns fileOffset - the position within the file that was located

' Local Variables:
' @local pBuff - a temporary pointer to the handles block buffer
' @local extraBytes - bytes from the end of the flash copy of the last block to file_position, written but not yet flushed

    pBuff := buffer_pointer(handle)                                             'get block buffer pointer
    if field[IDToBlock][hHeadBlockID[handle]] > BLOCKS - 1                      'no copy of the head on the flash yet: the file is the head block in the buffer
      block_id := hHeadBlockID[handle]
      fileOffset := file_position #> 0 <# (long[pBuff].[31..20] - ADDR_HEAD_DATA) '..a position past the end is the end, as locate_file_byte() gives it
      endPtr := ADDR_HEAD_DATA + fileOffset
    else
      block_id, endPtr, fileOffset := locate_handle_byte(handle, file_position) 'locate byte in file
      if (hStatus[handle] & H_MODIFY) and block_id == long[pBuff].[19..8] and long[pBuff].[0] == 0 '..the buffered last block: its buffered end is past the end of its flash copy when the file grew
        extraBytes := (file_position - fileOffset) #> 0 <# (long[pBuff].[31..20] - endPtr)
        endPtr += extraBytes
        fileOffset += extraBytes
    'debug("seek_locate() ", udec(block_id, file_position, fileOffset), uhex_word(endPtr))


PRI seek_to(handle, block_id, endPtr, fileOffset) : status | pBuff, bInBuffer

' Move the handle to a position seek_locate() found
'
' In modify mode the buffer always holds the handle's current block, so a seek within that block keeps the buffer
' and any edits in it, and the block is not read again. A seek to another block first rewrites a modified block.
' With no free block for the rewrite the position does not change, the block stays in the buffer still modified,
' and the status is E_DRIVE_FULL. In read mode the located block is always read: the buffer of a newly opened
' handle can hold a block left from an earlier file. A block move made by the rewrite keeps every block ID, so the
' located block is read by its ID.
'
' @param handle - handle to open file
' @param block_id - the block holding the located position
' @param endPtr - offset within the located block of the byte at the located position
' @param fileOffset - the position within the file that was located
' @returns status - 0 (SUCCESS) if the position was set, E_DRIVE_FULL if a modified block could not be rewritten,
' .. E_FLASH_TIMEOUT if the flash chip did not finish that rewrite in time (the located block is not read)

' Local Variables:
' @local pBuff - a temporary pointer to the handles block buffer
' @local bInBuffer - TRUE when the located block is the modify-mode block already in the buffer

    status := SUCCESS
    bInBuffer := FALSE
    pBuff := buffer_pointer(handle)                                             'get block buffer pointer
    if hStatus[handle] & H_MODIFY                                               'if modify mode..
      if block_id == long[pBuff].[19..8]                                        '..and the block is the one in the buffer, keep it
        bInBuffer := TRUE
      elseif hModified[handle]                                                  '..else if the buffered block was modified
        status := rewrite_block(handle)                                         '..then rewrite block (might move a block)
        if status == SUCCESS
          hModified[handle]~

    if status == SUCCESS
      hSeekFileOffset[handle] := fileOffset                                     ' we moved keep track
      hSeekPtr[handle] := hEndPtr[handle] := endPtr                             ' point to start of data in body block
      if bInBuffer == FALSE
        flash_read_block_id(block_id, pBuff, $000, $FFF)                        'read new block into buffer


PRI locate_handle_byte(handle, file_position) : block_id, blockOfs, fileOffset | startID, startOfs, blockStart

' Locate a position in the file a handle has open, as locate_file_byte() does, walking on from the handle's seek cache
'
' The cache names the block the last locate of the handle found, and the file offset of its first data byte
' position. A position at or past that offset is looked for from the cached block on; any other position, and every
' position while the cache is empty, from the head block. The head block's format is read from the flash while the
' cache is empty and kept with it, so a walk from the head block of an old-format file reads no filename. The block
' found becomes the cached block. A walk with no stop block, from a block that has a copy on the flash, returns a
' block it read and the offset it counted for that block, so any locate, whatever position it asks for, leaves the
' cache holding a true pair. The one block that can have no copy, the head of a new "w+" file, never reaches here:
' seek_locate() finds positions in it in the buffer.
'
' The cache stays correct while the handle is open: the file is open on no other handle, so delete(), rename() and
' create_file() never touch it, and the only changes to its chain are these. A block move (a rewrite, or the move of
' a block that an allocation picks) keeps the block ID, and every flash read goes through IDToBlock. A write within
' the chain changes no block's place in the file, and a write past the end adds blocks after the last one. A commit,
' a trim, an open, a close and a mount can take blocks out of the chain or change its head, and each empties the cache.
'
' @param handle - handle to open file
' @param file_position - the byte offset from the beginning of the file
' @returns block_id - the block id of the block containing the desired location, or of the last block when the file ends first
' @returns blockOfs - the offset into the block containing the desired location, or the end of the data of the last block
' @returns fileOffset - the location within the entire file: file_position, or the file length when the file ends first

' Local Variables:
' @local startID - the block id of the block the walk starts at
' @local startOfs - the file offset of the first data byte position of that block
' @local blockStart - the file offset of the first data byte position of the block found

  if hCacheBlockID[handle] <> NO_CACHED_BLOCK and file_position >= hCacheStart[handle] 'the position is not before the cached block: walk on from it
    startID := hCacheBlockID[handle]
    startOfs := hCacheStart[handle]
  else
    startID := hHeadBlockID[handle]
    if hCacheBlockID[handle] == NO_CACHED_BLOCK                                 'an empty cache: read the head block's format with its data start
      startOfs, hCacheOldFmt[handle] := head_data_start(startID)
    else                                                                        'the cache kept the format: an old-format head reads nothing, others only the data offset
      startOfs := head_data_start_of_format(startID, hCacheOldFmt[handle])

  block_id, blockOfs, fileOffset, blockStart, _ := walk_file_bytes(startID, field[IDToBlock][startID], startOfs, file_position, NO_STOP_BLOCK)
  hCacheBlockID[handle] := block_id
  hCacheStart[handle] := blockStart


PRI buffered_file_offset(handle) : fileOffset | pBuff, blockID, blockAddress, signature, startOfs

' Return the file offset of the byte the end pointer names in the block in the buffer
' -- walk_file_bytes() counts the data of every block before the buffered one, stopping at the buffered block, which
'    it does not read: the buffer holds a copy newer than the flash
' -- for a handle with no seek offset the walk starts at the head block, at the data start head_data_start() gives
'    it, so the data offset of a trimmed circular file is not counted
' -- a handle writing a new file, or a file over an existing name, counts from the first block it wrote, whose
'    copy on the flash is the one the handle programmed, and that block is a head block it built with no data offset
' -- a handle appending to an existing file counts from the block it started in, which begins where the file
'    length at open, less the data that block already held, puts it; that length is the one locate_file_byte() gave,
'    so a head block's data offset is already out of it
'
' @param handle - a handle to an open file
' @returns fileOffset - the count of file bytes before that byte

' Local Variables:
' @local pBuff - the address of the 4KB buffer for the file associated with this handle
' @local blockID - the block id of the block the walk starts at
' @local blockAddress - the block offset within the file system of the copy of that block the walk reads
' @local signature - the first long of the flash copy, at open, of the block an appending handle started in
' @local startOfs - the file offset of the first data byte position of the block the walk starts at

  pBuff := buffer_pointer(handle)
  if hStatus[handle] == H_WRITE or hStatus[handle] == H_APPEND                  'the handle writes: it counts from the block it started in
    blockID := hChainBlockID[handle]
    blockAddress := hChainBlockAddr[handle]
    startOfs := 0
    if hStatus[handle] == H_APPEND and hReplacedID[handle] == NOT_VALID         'appending: that block holds data that was there at open
      flash_read_block_id(blockID, @signature, $000, $003)                      'its flash copy is the one at open, whose last-block EndPtr ends the old data
      startOfs := hSeekFileOffset[handle] - (signature.[31..20] - (signature.[1] ? ADDR_BODY_DATA : ADDR_HEAD_DATA))
  else
    blockID := hHeadBlockID[handle]
    blockAddress := field[IDToBlock][blockID]
    startOfs, _ := head_data_start(blockID)

  _, _, _, fileOffset, _ := walk_file_bytes(blockID, blockAddress, startOfs, POSX, long[pBuff].[19..8]) 'the offset of the buffered block
  fileOffset += hEndPtr[handle] - (long[pBuff].[19..8] == hHeadBlockID[handle] ? ADDR_HEAD_DATA : ADDR_BODY_DATA) 'then the bytes before the end pointer in it


PRI handle_file_length(handle) : byteCount

' Return the length of the file a handle has open, counting bytes the handle holds that are not yet on the flash
' -- a file the handle is writing ("w", "a"): the file as the handle will commit it, from the blocks it wrote and its
'    buffer (buffered_file_offset()), never from a head that has no copy on the flash or from the file a "w" replaces
' -- every other handle: the end of the file as seek(handle, POSX, SK_FILE_START) locates it (seek_locate()), so the
'    two always agree. That counts a "w+" head with no copy on the flash as the buffered block alone, and a last block
'    that grew in the buffer as longer than its flash copy, and leaves out a trimmed circular file's data offset
' -- an old-format circular read counts from the first byte it keeps (hWindowStart), as its seek positions do
'
' @param handle - a handle to an open file
' @returns byteCount - the count of bytes in the file

  if hStatus[handle] == H_WRITE or hStatus[handle] == H_APPEND                  'a handle that writes: the file is what it will commit, and IDToBlock may hold nothing, or an older file, for its head
    byteCount := buffered_file_offset(handle)
  else
    _, _, byteCount := seek_locate(handle, POSX)
    byteCount -= hWindowStart[handle]


PRI close_no_lock(handle, bFreeHandle) : status | open_mode, chain_block_address, head_block_id, chain_block_id, chainState, bKeepHandle

' Close an open file, completes the file write, rewrite, or read-modify-write then frees handle
' . (do all the close operations, caller has locked and will release)
'
' A file open for writing is committed by activating the first block its handle wrote. That needs one free block
' for the last block, which is still in the buffer. With no free block the last block is not written and nothing is
' activated, so the file stays as it was at its last commit (a new file is not created) and the status is
' E_DRIVE_FULL. A circular file is committed first and then trimmed; with no free block for the trim it stays
' committed and whole, and the status is E_DRIVE_FULL. After a flush() whose trim found no free block the handle
' owes that trim (hTrimPending), and the close() that follows retries it even when nothing more was written; a
' retried trim with no free block is again E_DRIVE_FULL. A modified block of a file open for read/write that cannot
' be rewritten keeps its last written contents on the flash, and the status is E_DRIVE_FULL.
'
' A file opened with "w" or "w+" that holds no data is not created: an existing file it would replace is deleted,
' the head block ID a new "w+" file took is released, and the status is SUCCESS. A "w+" file that holds data is
' committed by commit_new_chain(), which replaces an existing file of the same name.
'
' When the handle is being freed, a new file that is not created gives back the head block ID its open took: a new
' "w"/"a" file closed with nothing written, and a new "w"/"a" or "w+" file whose commit finds no free block. No
' committed block uses that ID. An ID that a committed block uses (the head of an existing file being replaced or
' appended to, the last block of an appended file) is kept. A flush() keeps the handle, and with it the ID.
'
' A flush() of a "w"/"a" file whose last block cannot be written leaves the handle as it was: its mode, IDs,
' buffer, pointers and commit-chain fields are kept and it stays modified, so a later flush() or close() commits it.
'
' @param handle - a handle to an open file
' @param bFreeHandle - TRUE when the handle is freed after this close (close(), unmount()), FALSE for flush()
' A flash write that fails stops the close at that step: nothing written is undone, and the status is
' E_FLASH_TIMEOUT. The caller's release of the lock unmounts the filesystem.
'
' @returns status - 0 (SUCCESS) if successful,
' .. E_DRIVE_FULL if the flash has no free block for the last block, the trim, the rewrite or a "w+" head block,
' .. E_FLASH_TIMEOUT if the flash chip did not finish a write in time

' Local Variables:
' @local open_mode - the mode the handle is open in
' @local chain_block_address - the block offset within the file system of the first block the handle wrote
' @local head_block_id - the head block id of the file
' @local chain_block_id - the block id of the first block the handle wrote
' @local chainState - the block state the first block the handle wrote takes once active
' @local bKeepHandle - TRUE when a flush() commits nothing and the handle keeps its state

  status := LONG[@errorCode][cogid()] := SUCCESS                                'new operation clear any prior error code
  bKeepHandle := FALSE
  open_mode := hStatus[handle]                                                  'get file open mode for handle
  head_block_id := hHeadBlockID[handle]                                         'get head ID

  if hHeadPending[handle]                                                       'a "w+" file, not yet committed..
    if field[IDToBlock][head_block_id] > BLOCKS - 1 and not hModified[handle]   '..that holds no data: no file is left
      field[IDValid][head_block_id]~                                            '....release the head block ID it took
      field[IDToBlock][head_block_id] := 0                                      '....which no longer marks a head with no copy
      if hReplacedID[handle] <> NOT_VALID                                       '....and delete the existing file it replaces
        delete_chain_from_id(hReplacedID[handle], 0, 0, False)
    else
      status := commit_new_chain(handle)                                        '..that holds data: commit it
      if status < 0 and bFreeHandle                                             '..not committed: no committed block uses the IDs it took
        if fsDeviceFault == FALSE and field[IDToBlock][head_block_id] < BLOCKS  '....no room, and its inactive head copy is on the flash:
          delete_chain_from_id(head_block_id, 0, 0, false)                      '......cancel and free the copy and the body blocks it links to
        field[IDValid][head_block_id]~                                          '....release the head block ID its open took
        field[IDToBlock][head_block_id] := 0

  elseif hModified[handle] or hTrimPending[handle]                              ' if modified, or committed and still owing its trim
    case open_mode
      H_WRITE, H_APPEND:                                                        'write/rewrite/append mode?
        if hModified[handle]                                                    'bytes written since the last commit: write the last block and commit
          status := write_block(handle, hEndPtr[handle], false)                 'write updated last block with EndPtr

          if status == SUCCESS                                                  'commit only once the last block is written
            chain_block_id := hChainBlockID[handle]                             'get fork ID
            chain_block_address := hChainBlockAddr[handle]                      'get fork block
            chainState := chain_block_id == head_block_id ? B_HEAD : B_BODY     'get fork block state

            flash_activate_block(chain_block_address, hChainLifeCycle[handle])  'replace old head block if rewrite or old last block if append

            if fsDeviceFault == FALSE and (open_mode & H_FORK)                  'if append (and the activate reached the flash)..
              delete_chain_from_id(chain_block_id, 0, 0, True)                  '..delete old fork block through end of file, keeping first ID valid

            if fsDeviceFault                                                    'the flash failed: the commit stops here, as a power loss here leaves it
              status := E_FLASH_TIMEOUT
            else
              field[BlockState][chain_block_address] := chainState              'change new fork block status from sTEMP to sHEAD/sBODY
              field[IDToBlock][chain_block_id] := chain_block_address           'update IDToBlock to point to new fork block

          elseifnot bFreeHandle                                                 'flush(): nothing was committed, so the handle keeps its state..
            bKeepHandle := TRUE                                                 '..and its unwritten bytes, for a later commit

          elseif open_mode == H_WRITE                                           'a new file not created: no committed block uses the head ID its open took
            field[IDValid][head_block_id]~                                      '..release it

        if status == SUCCESS and hCircularLength[handle]                        'a committed file with a size limit: committed now, or by a flush whose trim found no free block..
          status := froncate_file(head_block_id, hCircularLength[handle])       '..froncate file to size limit
          hTrimPending[handle] := status < 0                                    '..a trim with no free block is owed until a later close() finds one

      H_READWRITE:                                                              'modify mode?
        if hModified[handle]~                                                   '..and if block was modified (post-clears)
          status := rewrite_block(handle)                                       '..rewrite block

  elseif hReplacedID[handle] <> NOT_VALID                                       ' a "w" file of an existing name with nothing written: no file is left
    delete_chain_from_id(hReplacedID[handle], 0, 0, False)                      '..delete the existing file, as replacing it with no data would

  elseif open_mode == H_WRITE and bFreeHandle                                   ' a new "w"/"a" file with nothing written: no file is left
    field[IDValid][head_block_id]~                                              '..release the head block ID its open took

  if fsDeviceFault                                                              ' a flash write of this close failed, at whichever step: that is the status
    status := E_FLASH_TIMEOUT

  hCacheBlockID[handle] := NO_CACHED_BLOCK                                      ' a commit or a trim can take blocks out of the chain: empty the seek cache
  ifnot bKeepHandle
    hEndPtr[handle] := 0                                                        ' no valid end pointer any more
    hSeekPtr[handle] := NOT_ENABLED                                             ' Ensure seek mode is disabled for this handle
    hSeekFileOffset[handle] := 0                                                ' reset user requested postion within file
    hChainBlockID[handle] := 0                                                  ' Clear commit-chain info
    hChainBlockAddr[handle] := 0
    hChainLifeCycle[handle] := 0
    hModified[handle]~                                                          ' clear modified flag
    hHeadPending[handle] := FALSE                                               ' the handle has no new head and replaces no file
    hReplacedID[handle] := NOT_VALID

PRI write_block(handle, NextID_EndPtr, bHasNext) : status | pBuff, block_id, block_address

' Write current block in buffer to next avail. block address
'
' A block with a next block is written only while a free block is left over for that next block. With no block
' for it, nothing is changed: the buffer, the tables and the flash are as they were.
'
' @param handle - a reference to a file open for write
' @param NextID_EndPtr - the next block id, -OR- the pointer to end of data in last block
' @param bHasNext - TRUE when NextID_EndPtr is the next block id, FALSE when this is the last block
' A flash write that fails leaves the block as a power loss would, changes no table, and the status is
' E_FLASH_TIMEOUT.
'
' @returns status - 0 (SUCCESS) if the block was written, E_DRIVE_FULL if the flash has no room for it,
' .. E_FLASH_TIMEOUT if the flash chip did not finish the write in time

' Local Variables:
' @local pBuff - a temporary pointer to the handles block buffer
' @local block_id - temporary block id
' @local block_address - the block offset within the file system

  status := SUCCESS
  block_address := next_block_address(bHasNext ? NEXT_BLOCK_SPARE : 0)          'get a new block, keeping one for the next block (may alter IDToBlock)

  if block_address < 0                                                          'no free block (E_DRIVE_FULL), or a block move failed (E_FLASH_TIMEOUT)
    status := block_address
  else
    pBuff := buffer_pointer(handle)                                             'get block buffer pointer
    long[pBuff].[0] := bHasNext                                                 'set more/last bit
    long[pBuff].[31..20] := NextID_EndPtr                                       'set NextID/EndPtr
    block_id := long[pBuff].[19..8]                                             'get block ID of block

    ' the first block the handle writes stays B_TEMP until close activates it, so no block move can take it

    if showRTdebug
      debug("* wr_block() ", uhex_word(block_address), udec(block_id), uhex_word(NextID_EndPtr))

    if block_id == hChainBlockID[handle]                                        'if this is the head of commit chain block
      flash_program_block(block_address, pBuff, hChainLifeCycle[handle])        '..program block with chain head cycle
    else                                                                        'else, this is a body block
      flash_program_block(block_address, pBuff, %011)                           '..program body block with new cycle
      flash_activate_block(block_address, %011)                                 '..activate block

    if fsDeviceFault                                                            'the flash failed: no table is changed
      status := E_FLASH_TIMEOUT
    elseif block_id == hChainBlockID[handle]
      hChainBlockAddr[handle] := block_address                                  '..remember the block so that it can be activated on close
    else
      field[BlockState][block_address] := B_BODY                                '..change block state from sTEMP to sBODY
      field[IDToBlock][block_id] := block_address                               '..set IDToBlock


PRI rewrite_block(handle) : status | pBuff, block_id, block_address, oldBlockAddress

' Write block over existing (issed mew lifeCycle to make heigher priority
'
' The new copy takes the next lifecycle of the old copy, is activated, and then the old copy is cancelled. The head
' block of a "w+" file not yet committed is the exception: its copy stays inactive on the flash, B_TEMP, until
' commit_new_chain() activates it, so the file is not on the flash before it is committed. Each copy is programmed
' with the first active lifecycle, and any earlier copy, also inactive, is cancelled. The head of a new file with
' no copy on the flash yet, which IDToBlock shows with an address outside 0..BLOCKS-1, has nothing to cancel.
' With no free block for the new copy nothing is changed: the old copy stays on the flash and the buffer keeps
' the modified block.
'
' @param handle - a reference to a file open for read/modify/write
' A flash write that fails leaves both copies as a power loss would, and the status is E_FLASH_TIMEOUT.
'
' @returns status - 0 (SUCCESS) if the block was rewritten, E_DRIVE_FULL if the flash has no free block for it,
' .. E_FLASH_TIMEOUT if the flash chip did not finish the rewrite in time

' Local Variables:
' @local pBuff - a temporary pointer to the handles block buffer
' @local block_id - temporary block id
' @local block_address - the block offset within the file system
' @local oldBlockAddress - original block address for this block

  status := SUCCESS
  block_address := next_block_address(0)                                        'get a new block (may alter IDToBlock)

  if block_address < 0                                                          'no free block (E_DRIVE_FULL), or a block move failed (E_FLASH_TIMEOUT)
    status := block_address
  else
    pBuff := buffer_pointer(handle)                                             'get block buffer pointer
    block_id := long[pBuff].[19..8]                                             'get block ID

    oldBlockAddress := field[IDToBlock][block_id]\block_address                 'get the old block -AND- update IDToBlock to new block

    if hHeadPending[handle] and block_id == hHeadBlockID[handle]                'the head of a "w+" file not yet committed..
      flash_program_block(block_address, pBuff, %011)                           '..program the copy with the first active lifecycle, not activated: it stays B_TEMP
      if oldBlockAddress < BLOCKS                                               '..an earlier copy, never activated, is cancelled
        flash_cancel_block(oldBlockAddress)
        field[BlockState][oldBlockAddress] := B_FREE
    else
      flash_activate_updated_block(block_address, pBuff)                        'program updated block
      flash_cancel_block(oldBlockAddress)                                       'cancel the old block
      field[BlockState][block_address] := field[BlockState][oldBlockAddress]\B_FREE 'copy old block state to new -AND- free old

    if fsDeviceFault                                                            'the flash failed at one of the writes above
      status := E_FLASH_TIMEOUT


PRI commit_new_chain(handle) : status | pBuff, head_block_id, replaced_block_id, head_address, block_address, cycleBits, oldCycleBits

' Commit a "w+" file that holds data: activate its head block, which has stayed inactive on the flash until now
'
' A modified body block in the buffer is rewritten first, and the head block is brought back into the buffer. A new
' file whose head copy on the flash is current has that copy activated. Otherwise the head block is written to a
' new block and activated, and an earlier inactive copy is cancelled. When the file replaces an existing file, the
' head block is written with the head block ID of that file and the next lifecycle of its head, so that one
' activation makes the new head supersede the old one; only then is the old file's chain cancelled, and the ID the
' new file took at open is released. A power loss at any step leaves the old file or the new one: before the
' activation the new head is inactive and mount() keeps the old file (cancelling the new file's body blocks as
' unreached), after it mount() keeps the newer of the two heads. With no free block for a rewrite or for the head
' block nothing is activated, the file stays uncommitted, any existing file stays as it was, and the status is
' E_DRIVE_FULL. A flash write that fails stops the commit at that step, as a power loss there would, and the
' status is E_FLASH_TIMEOUT.
'
' @param handle - a handle to a "w+" file that is not yet committed and holds data
' @returns status - 0 (SUCCESS) if the file was committed, E_DRIVE_FULL if the flash has no free block for it,
' .. E_FLASH_TIMEOUT if the flash chip did not finish a write in time

' Local Variables:
' @local pBuff - a temporary pointer to the handles block buffer
' @local head_block_id - the head block ID of the file: at open, then once committed
' @local replaced_block_id - the head block ID of the existing file being replaced, or NOT_VALID
' @local head_address - the block offset within the file system of the inactive head copy, or BLOCKS for none
' @local block_address - the block offset within the file system of the head block being committed
' @local cycleBits - the lifecycle the committed head block is activated with
' @local oldCycleBits - first byte of the head block of the file being replaced, holding its lifecycle

  status := SUCCESS
  hCacheBlockID[handle] := NO_CACHED_BLOCK                                      'the commit can change the head block ID and release the one cached: empty the seek cache
  pBuff := buffer_pointer(handle)                                               'get block buffer pointer
  head_block_id := hHeadBlockID[handle]
  replaced_block_id := hReplacedID[handle]
  head_address := field[IDToBlock][head_block_id]

  if long[pBuff].[19..8] <> head_block_id                                       'the buffer holds a body block..
    if hModified[handle]                                                        '..rewrite it if it was modified
      status := rewrite_block(handle)
      if status == SUCCESS
        hModified[handle]~
    if status == SUCCESS                                                        '..then bring back the head, which has a copy whenever a body exists
      flash_read_block_addr(head_address, pBuff, $000, $FFF)

  if status == SUCCESS
    if head_address < BLOCKS and replaced_block_id == NOT_VALID and not hModified[handle] 'a new file whose inactive head copy is current..
      flash_activate_block(head_address, %011)                                  '..activate it with the first active lifecycle it was programmed with
      BYTE[pBuff].[7..5] := %011                                                '..the buffer, read back from an inactive copy, takes that lifecycle too
      field[BlockState][head_address] := B_HEAD
    else
      block_address := next_block_address(0)                                    'get a new block for the head (may alter IDToBlock)
      if block_address < 0                                                      'no free block (E_DRIVE_FULL), or a block move failed (E_FLASH_TIMEOUT)
        status := block_address
      else
        cycleBits := %011                                                       'a new file starts at the first active lifecycle
        if replaced_block_id <> NOT_VALID                                       'a replacement takes the old head's ID and its next lifecycle,
          flash_read_block_addr(field[IDToBlock][replaced_block_id], @oldCycleBits, $000, $000) '..read after the allocation, which may have moved that head
          cycleBits := next_active_cycle(oldCycleBits.[7..5])
          long[pBuff].[19..8] := replaced_block_id
        flash_program_block(block_address, pBuff, cycleBits)                    'program the head..
        flash_activate_block(block_address, cycleBits)                          '..and activate it: the file is committed
        if fsDeviceFault == FALSE                                               'a failed head write leaves the old file and the new head as a power loss here would
          if replaced_block_id <> NOT_VALID
            delete_chain_from_id(replaced_block_id, 0, 0, True)                 'cancel the old head and its bodies, keeping the head ID valid
            field[IDValid][head_block_id]~                                      'release the ID the new file took at open
            field[IDToBlock][head_block_id] := 0
            head_block_id := replaced_block_id
            hHeadBlockID[handle] := head_block_id
          if head_address < BLOCKS                                              'cancel the earlier inactive copy of the head
            flash_cancel_block(head_address)
            field[BlockState][head_address] := B_FREE
          field[IDToBlock][head_block_id] := block_address
          field[BlockState][block_address] := B_HEAD
          hModified[handle]~

  if fsDeviceFault                                                              'a flash write of the commit failed, at whichever step
    status := E_FLASH_TIMEOUT

  if status == SUCCESS
    hHeadPending[handle] := FALSE                                               'the file is on the flash: from here the handle is an "r+" handle
    hReplacedID[handle] := NOT_VALID


PRI filename_pointer(handle) : p_filename

' Return pointer to filename for this handle
'
' @param handle - a handle to an open file
' @returns p_filename - address of a zstring containing the filename

  p_filename := @hFilename + handle << FILENAME_SIZE_EXP                              'get filename pointer by handle


PRI buffer_pointer(handle) : p_buffer

' Return a pointer to the block buffer for this handle
'
' @param handle - a handle to an open file
' @returns p_buffer -  the address of the 4KB buffer associated with this handle

  p_buffer := @hBlockBuff + handle << BLOCK_SIZE_EXP


PRI handle_index(handle) : hndlIdx

' Return the index into the handle tables of a handle the caller holds
' -- the index is the handle less HANDLE_BASE; a value that is not a handle gives an index outside 0..MAX_FILES_OPEN-1
'
' @param handle - a handle as the caller holds it
' @returns hndlIdx - the index of the handle in the handle tables

  hndlIdx := handle - HANDLE_BASE


PRI ensure_handle_mode(handle, open_mode_bits) : status

' Determine if handle is open with desired mode
'
' @param handle - index in the handle tables of a file that might be open for read or read/write (not the caller's handle)
' @param open_mode_bits - some combination of H_READ, H_WRITE, H_FORK and H_MODIFY
' @returns status - 0 (SUCCESS) if successful,
' .. E_BAD_HANDLE if the handle is outside the range of handles or is not open,
' .. E_FILE_MODE if the file is open, but not in desired mode,

  if handle < 0 or handle > MAX_FILES_OPEN - 1
    status := E_BAD_HANDLE
  elseif hStatus[handle] == 0                                                   'a handle in the range that is not open
    status := E_BAD_HANDLE
  elseif hStatus[handle] & open_mode_bits
    status :=  SUCCESS
  else
    status :=  E_FILE_MODE


CON ' >>>  parameter type (block_id)  <<<

PRI froncate_file(head_block_id, limit_in_bytes) : status | size_in_bytes, block_address, new_head_block_id, block_offset, body_signature, delete_mode, prior_block_id, data_offset

' Remove leading block(s) from file that exceeds the circular size limit
'
' The trim writes a new head block first. With no free block for it nothing is changed and the file stays whole.
' A flash write that fails stops the trim at that step, as a power loss there would.
'
' The walk to the block before the data block follows at most BLOCKS links, the longest a chain can be: a walk
' that reaches that bound takes the last block it reached as that block, as it does at the end of the chain.
'
' @param head_block_id - block id of file
' @param limit_in_bytes - the file size limit in bytes
' @returns status - 0 (SUCCESS) if the file is within the limit or was trimmed to it, E_DRIVE_FULL if the flash
' .. has no free block for the new head block, E_FLASH_TIMEOUT if the flash chip did not finish a write in time

' Local Variables:
' @local size_in_bytes - current length of file in bytes
' @local block_address - the block offset within the file system
' @local new_head_block_id - id of block about to become the file head
' @local block_offset - temporary offset into block
' @local body_signature - temporary signature bits for body block
' @local delete_mode - desired delete mode for prior-file chain
' @local prior_block_id - former head block id
' @local data_offset - temporary offset in block

  status := SUCCESS
  _, _, size_in_bytes := locate_file_byte(head_block_id, POSX)                                          'get size of file: the end of the file, past which no position lies

  ' if have extra blocks beyond limit requested at open, then remove them
  if size_in_bytes > limit_in_bytes                                                                     'if file is oversize..
    block_address := next_block_address(0)                                                              'get a new block now (may alter tmpBlockBuffer and IDToBlock)
    if block_address < 0                                                                                'no free block (E_DRIVE_FULL, the file stays whole), or a block move failed (E_FLASH_TIMEOUT)
      status := block_address

  if size_in_bytes > limit_in_bytes and status == SUCCESS                                               'if file is oversize and has its new head block..

      new_head_block_id, block_offset, _ := locate_file_byte(head_block_id, size_in_bytes - limit_in_bytes) 'find block with start of data (might be head block)
      if showRTdebug
        debug("* froncate(id=", udec_(head_block_id), ", ", udec_(limit_in_bytes), ") ", udec(size_in_bytes, new_head_block_id), uhex_word(block_offset), "(", udec_word_(block_offset), ")")

      if block_offset > $88
        ' make this block the new head
        flash_read_block_id(new_head_block_id, @body_signature, $000, $003)                             'get data block signature
        flash_read_block_id(new_head_block_id, @tmpBlockBuffer + $88, $088, $FFF)                       'load data bytes into head block buffer
        data_offset := block_offset - $088                                                              '..set data offset to point within head block

      else
      ' locate prior block in chain to make it the new head with calc offset
        ' locate prior block
        prior_block_id := head_block_id
        repeat BLOCKS                                                                                   'a chain has no more than BLOCKS blocks
          flash_read_block_id(prior_block_id, @body_signature, $000, $003)                              'get head block signature
          if body_signature.[0] == 1                                                                    ' if more block
            if body_signature.[31..20] <> new_head_block_id                                             ' ..if this block does NOT immediately preceed our data block
              prior_block_id := body_signature.[31..20]                                                 ' ....get block id of next block
            else
              quit
          else
            quit
        ' prior block is our new head
        if showRTdebug
          debug("* froncate(id=", udec_(head_block_id), ", ", udec_(limit_in_bytes), ") ", udec(size_in_bytes), ", AWAKEN PRIOR HEAD ", udec(prior_block_id))
        flash_read_block_id(prior_block_id, @body_signature, $000, $003)                                'get data block signature
        flash_read_block_id(prior_block_id, @tmpBlockBuffer + $88, $088, $FFF)                          'load data bytes into head block buffer
        data_offset := block_offset + 3956 - 4                                                              '..set data offset to point within next data block

      flash_read_block_id(head_block_id, @tmpBlockBuffer, $000, $087)                                   'overlay file-head data
      LONG[@tmpBlockBuffer].[0] := body_signature.[0]                                                   '..copy more/last bit from data block
      LONG[@tmpBlockBuffer].[31..20] := body_signature.[31..20]                                         '..copy NextID/EndPtr from data block
      LONG[@tmpBlockBuffer][1].[11..0] := data_offset                                                   '..set data offset to point within next data block
      if showRTdebug
        if body_signature.[0]
          debug("- header [", uhex_word_(block_address), "] thisID=", udec_(LONG[@tmpBlockBuffer].[19..8]), ", nextID=", udec_(LONG[@tmpBlockBuffer].[31..20]), ", sig=[", uhex_long_(LONG[@tmpBlockBuffer]), "]")
        else
          debug("- header [", uhex_word_(block_address), "] thisID=", udec_(LONG[@tmpBlockBuffer].[19..8]), ", endPtr=", uhex_word_(LONG[@tmpBlockBuffer].[31..20]), ", sig=[", uhex_long_(LONG[@tmpBlockBuffer]), "]")
      delete_mode := 1                                                                                  '..delete old head block through data block

      flash_activate_updated_block(block_address, @tmpBlockBuffer)                                      'program updated block

      if fsDeviceFault == FALSE                                                                         'a failed head write leaves the file as a power loss here would
        delete_chain_from_id(head_block_id, body_signature.[19..8], delete_mode, True)                  'delete old head block through or before data block, keep first block ID valid

        field[IDToBlock][head_block_id] := block_address                                                'point IDToBlock to new head block
        field[BlockState][block_address] := B_HEAD                                                      'change state of new head block from sTEMP to sHEAD

  if fsDeviceFault                                                                                      'a flash write of the trim failed, at whichever step
    status := E_FLASH_TIMEOUT

PRI count_file_bytes(block_id, startOfs) : bytes_used, bytes_free, block_count | endPtr

' Return information about a file: blocks allocated, bytes used, bytes free
' -- the file is measured by the one chain walk every length and position comes from (walk_file_bytes()), from
'    the data start of its head block, which the caller gives from what its own lookup read: the format the name
'    lookup found, or the filename CRC word, so no filename is read twice (a caller with no lookup measures the file
'    with locate_file_byte(), which reads the head with head_data_start()). So bytes_used is the bytes a read can
'    reach: a trimmed circular file's data offset is not counted, and an old-format head block has none
' -- the walk reads at most BLOCKS blocks, the longest a chain can be; a walk that reaches that bound stops there,
'    as at a last block: the counts are those of the blocks it read, and bytes_free is 0 (each of them was full)
'
' @param block_id - the block id of the file head
' @param startOfs - the file offset of the first data byte position of the head block: 0, or minus the data offset
' @returns bytes_used - the number of bytes written to file
' @returns bytes_free - the number of bytes allocated but not yet written (in the last block)
' @returns block_count - the number of blocks allocation to this file

' Local Variables:
' @local endPtr - the end of the data of the last block the walk read

  _, endPtr, bytes_used, _, block_count := walk_file_bytes(block_id, field[IDToBlock][block_id], startOfs, POSX, NO_STOP_BLOCK)
  bytes_free := ADDR_DATA_END - endPtr


PRI locate_file_byte(block_id, file_position) : rID, rBlockOfs, rLocation | startOfs

' locate position (file_offset) within file list of blocks
' -- the head block tells where the file's first byte is: walk_file_bytes() then follows the chain from it
'
' @param block_id - the block id of the file head
' @param file_position - the byte offset from the beginning of the file
' @returns rID - the block id of the block containing the desired location
' @returns rBlockOfs - the offset into the block containing the desired location
' @returns rLocation - the location within the entire file

' Local Variables:
' @local startOfs - the file offset of the first data byte position of the head block

  startOfs, _ := head_data_start(block_id)
  rID, rBlockOfs, rLocation, _, _ := walk_file_bytes(block_id, field[IDToBlock][block_id], startOfs, file_position, NO_STOP_BLOCK)


PRI walk_file_bytes(block_id, block_address, startOfs, file_position, stop_id) : rID, rBlockOfs, rLocation, rBlockStart, rBlockCount | signature, currOfs, srtOfs, endOfs, bFound

' Locate a position in a file by following its chain of blocks from one of them: the one chain walk that every file
' length and file position comes from
'
' The walk starts at block_id, whose first data byte position (ADDR_HEAD_DATA in a head block, ADDR_BODY_DATA in a
' body block) stands for file offset startOfs: a head block's data offset, or an old-format head block's lack of one,
' is in startOfs. It reads each block's first long from the flash, the first block at block_address and every later
' block at the address IDToBlock holds for its ID. A position before startOfs is never looked for, so the walk starts
' at the head block, or at a block before the position.
'
' The walk stops before it reads a block whose ID is stop_id, the block a handle holds in its buffer, whose copy
' there is newer than the one on the flash, or whose address is outside 0..BLOCKS-1, a block with no copy on the
' flash, which it never reads through. It ends there as at the end of a full block: rID is that block, rBlockStart
' and rLocation the file offset of its first data byte position, and rBlockOfs ADDR_DATA_END. NO_STOP_BLOCK stops at
' no block.
'
' The walk reads at most BLOCKS blocks, the longest a chain can be. A walk that reaches that bound ends at the
' last block it read, as it ends at a last block: rID is that block, rBlockOfs the end of its data area, and
' rLocation and rBlockStart count only the bytes of the blocks it read.
'
' @param block_id - the block id of the block the walk starts at
' @param block_address - the block offset within the file system of the copy of that block the walk reads
' @param startOfs - the file offset of the first data byte position of that block (negative for a head block with a data offset)
' @param file_position - the byte offset from the beginning of the file
' @param stop_id - the block id of the block the walk stops before, or NO_STOP_BLOCK
' @returns rID - the block id of the block containing the desired location, or of the last block when the file ends first
' @returns rBlockOfs - the offset into the block containing the desired location, or the end of the data of the last block
' @returns rLocation - the location within the entire file: file_position, or the file length when the file ends first
' @returns rBlockStart - the file offset of the first data byte position of block rID
' @returns rBlockCount - the count of blocks the walk read

' Local Variables:
' @local signature - temp long containing the block signature bits
' @local currOfs - the file offset of the first data byte position of the block being read
' @local srtOfs - start of data in block
' @local endOfs - end of data in block
' @local bFound - TRUE once the block holding the position, the last block, or a block the walk stops before is reached

  file_position := file_position #> 0 <# $FFFFFF                                'limit offset into file from 0 to 16MB
  currOfs := startOfs
  rBlockCount := 0
  endOfs := ADDR_DATA_END
  bFound := FALSE

  repeat BLOCKS                                                                 'trace blocks to count file bytes (a chain has no more than BLOCKS blocks)
    rID := block_id
    rBlockStart := currOfs
    if block_id == stop_id or block_address > BLOCKS - 1                        'the buffered block, or a block with no copy on the flash: it is not read
      rBlockOfs := ADDR_DATA_END
      rLocation := currOfs
      bFound := TRUE
    else
      flash_read_block_addr(block_address, @signature, $000, $003)              'read block header
      rBlockCount++
      srtOfs := signature.[1] ? ADDR_BODY_DATA : ADDR_HEAD_DATA                 'body or head?
      endOfs := signature.[0] ? ADDR_DATA_END : signature.[31..20]              'more or last?
      if file_position >= currOfs and file_position < currOfs + endOfs - srtOfs 'if location is within block..
        rBlockOfs := file_position - currOfs + srtOfs                           '..the block, the offset into it, and the target location
        rLocation := file_position
        bFound := TRUE
      else
        currOfs += endOfs - srtOfs                                              'not within block, advance position to next block
        ifnot signature.[0]                                                     'if last block..
          rBlockOfs := endOfs                                                   '..the block, the end of its data, and the end-of-file location
          rLocation := currOfs
          bFound := TRUE
        else
          block_id := signature.[31..20]                                        'get next block ID
          block_address := field[IDToBlock][block_id]
    if bFound == TRUE
      quit

  if bFound == FALSE                                                            'BLOCKS blocks were read: the last one ends the walk, as a last block does
    rBlockOfs := endOfs
    rLocation := currOfs


PRI head_data_start(head_block_id) : startOfs, bOldFmt

' Return where the data of a file starts in its head block, read from the flash
'
' The filename CRC word and the filename are read together. The head block is old format when its word is the CRC32
' of its filename, terminator included, and its data then starts at its first data byte. Otherwise the low 12 bits of
' the word are the data offset, the count of bytes at the start of the head block's data area that are not part of
' the file. Reads into tmpBlockBuffer. A head block with no copy on the flash (IDToBlock holds an address outside
' 0..BLOCKS-1 for it) is a head this driver built, with no data offset: it is not read.
'
' @param head_block_id - the block id of the file head
' @returns startOfs - the file offset of the first data byte position of the head block: 0, or minus the data offset
' @returns bOldFmt - TRUE when the head block is old format

  startOfs := 0
  bOldFmt := FALSE
  if field[IDToBlock][head_block_id] < BLOCKS                                   'never read the flash through the mark of a head with no copy
    flash_read_block_id(head_block_id, @tmpBlockBuffer, ADDR_HEAD_FN_CRC, ADDR_HEAD_DATA - 1) 'the filename CRC word, then the filename
    bOldFmt := LONG[@tmpBlockBuffer] == filename_crc32(@tmpBlockBuffer + ADDR_HEAD_SONAME - ADDR_HEAD_FN_CRC)
    startOfs := bOldFmt ? 0 : -(LONG[@tmpBlockBuffer].[11..0])


PRI head_data_start_of_format(head_block_id, bOldFmt) : startOfs | filenameCrcWord

' Return where the data of a file starts in its head block, for a caller whose own lookup already told it the head
' block's format, as head_data_start() would return it
' -- an old-format head block has no data offset, and nothing is read; otherwise only the filename CRC word, whose
'    low 12 bits are the data offset, is read: no filename is read again
' -- a head block with no copy on the flash (IDToBlock holds an address outside 0..BLOCKS-1 for it) is a head this
'    driver built, with no data offset: it is not read
'
' @param head_block_id - the block id of the file head
' @param bOldFmt - TRUE when the head block is old format
' @returns startOfs - the file offset of the first data byte position of the head block: 0, or minus the data offset

' Local Variables:
' @local filenameCrcWord - the filename CRC word of the head block

  startOfs := 0
  if bOldFmt == FALSE and field[IDToBlock][head_block_id] < BLOCKS              'never read the flash through the mark of a head with no copy
    flash_read_block_id(head_block_id, @filenameCrcWord, ADDR_HEAD_FN_CRC, ADDR_HEAD_SONAME - 1) 'the filename CRC word alone
    startOfs := -(filenameCrcWord.[11..0])


PRI delete_chain_from_id(block_id, EndID, delete_mode, KeepFirstIDValid) | block_address, signature

' remove selected part of a file chain
' -- a cancel that fails raises fsDeviceFault and ends the walk there: the rest of the chain stays on the flash, as
'    a power loss at that point would leave it, and no block is read from a chip that may still be busy
' -- modes 1 and 2 stop only at the block EndID names: they have no guard for the end of the chain, so the caller
'    passes an EndID that the chain from block_id reaches
'
' @param block_id - starting block id
' @param EndID - ending block id
' @param delete_mode - do we delete through end or up to EndID (or including EndID)
' @param KeepFirstIDValid - T/F where T means don't invalidate first block

' Local Variables:
' @local block_address - temporary block address
' @local signature - temporary block state bits

' delete_mode  Deletes to...
'---------------------------------
' 0 last block, [EndID ignored] (all of chain - thru last block)
' 1 block whose ThisID = EndID (end block too)
' 2 block whose NextID = EndID (leave end block in place)

  block_address := field[IDToBlock][block_id]           'translate block ID to block
  if showRTdebug
    debug("* delChnFmID() [", uhex_word_(block_address), "] ", udec(block_id, EndID, delete_mode), sdec(KeepFirstIDValid))

  ' FIXME: TODO: :
  '   - wipe field[IDValid][block_id] for all but first block? (first is conditional)
  '   - reset field[IDToBlock][block_id] for all blocks?

  repeat                                                                        'trace block chain and cancel IDs, block states, and blocks
    ifnot KeepFirstIDValid~                                                     'keep first block block ID valid?
      field[IDValid][block_id]~                                                 'clear block ID valid flag
    block_address := field[IDToBlock][block_id]                                 'translate block ID to block
    field[BlockState][block_address] := B_FREE                                  'set block state to sFREE
    flash_cancel_block(block_address)                                           'cancel block
    if fsDeviceFault                                                            'the flash failed: the walk ends here
      quit
    flash_read_block_addr(block_address, @signature, $000, $003)                'read block header
    block_id := signature.[31..20]                                              'get block ID of next block
  while lookupz(delete_mode: signature.[0], ...                                 'mode 0: delete to last block
              signature.[19..8] <> EndID,  ...                                  'mode 1: delete to ThisID = EndID
              block_id <> EndID)                                                'mode 2: delete to NextID = EndID


CON ' >>>  parameter type (block_address)  <<<

PRI check_block_read_only(thisBlockAddress): bad_count, dupe_count | otherBlockAddress, thisCycleBits, otherCycleBits, thisBlockID

' Check one block as check_block_fix_dupe_id() does for mount(), changing no block on the flash
' -- a block that is not active stays B_FREE and is not counted
' -- an active block whose CRC does not match, or whose IDs, end pointer or data offset are out of range
'    (block_fields_in_range()), is a bad block: it is counted and stays B_FREE, and its ID indexes no table
' -- a good block takes its ID: B_TEMP, and when another good block already holds the ID the newer of the two is
'    kept B_TEMP, the older left B_FREE, and the duplicate counted
'
' @param thisBlockAddress - the block offset within the file system for "this" block
' @returns bad_count - 1 when mount() would cancel "this" block as a bad block, 0 otherwise
' @returns dupe_count - 1 when another good block already holds the ID of "this" block, 0 otherwise

' Local Variables:
' @local otherBlockAddress -the block offset within the file system for the "other" block
' @local thisCycleBits - the lifecycle bits of "this" block
' @local otherCycleBits - the lifecycle bits of the "other" block
' @local thisBlockID - the blockID of "this" block

  bad_count := 0
  dupe_count := 0
  flash_read_block_addr(thisBlockAddress, @thisCycleBits, $000, $000)           'read first byte of block

  if lookdown(thisCycleBits.[7..5]: %011, %101, %110)                           'is block active? (a canceled or inactive block stays B_FREE)
    flash_read_block_addr(thisBlockAddress, @tmpBlockBuffer, $000, $FFF)        'read entire block

    if LONG[@tmpBlockBuffer + $FFC] <> block_crc(@tmpBlockBuffer)               'is CRC bad?
      bad_count := 1                                                            '..mount would cancel it: block status remains B_FREE
    elseifnot block_fields_in_range(@tmpBlockBuffer)                            'an ID, end pointer or data offset that would index past a table or a data area?
      bad_count := 1                                                           '..mount would cancel it as a bad block: block status remains B_FREE
    else
      thisBlockID := LONG[@tmpBlockBuffer].[19..8]                              'this block is good, get its ID

      ifnot field[IDValid][thisBlockID]~~                                       'set ID flag and if it wasn't already set.. (after test, bit := 1)
        field[IDToBlock][thisBlockID] := thisBlockAddress                       '..set IDToBlock to this block
        field[BlockState][thisBlockAddress] := B_TEMP                           '..set B_TEMP status for this block
      else
        otherBlockAddress := field[IDToBlock][thisBlockID]                      'ID flag was already set, get other block with same ID
        dupe_count := 1

        flash_read_block_addr(otherBlockAddress, @otherCycleBits, $000, $000)   'read first byte of other block

        if lookdown(thisCycleBits.[7..5] << 3 | otherCycleBits.[7..5]: %011_110, %101_011, %110_101)  'if this block is newer..
          field[IDToBlock][thisBlockID] := thisBlockAddress                     '..set IDToBlock to this block
          field[BlockState][thisBlockAddress] := B_TEMP                         '..set B_TEMP status for this block
          field[BlockState][otherBlockAddress] := B_FREE                        '..set B_FREE status for other block


PRI check_block_fix_dupe_id(thisBlockAddress) : bBadCancelled | otherBlockAddress, thisCycleBits, otherCycleBits, thisBlockID, thisBlockState

' If there is more than one block with this blocks ID, cancel the older block
' -- an active block whose CRC does not match, or whose IDs, end pointer or data offset are out of range
'    (block_fields_in_range()), is a bad block: it is cancelled and stays B_FREE, and its ID indexes no table. A newer copy that is bad leaves
'    the older copy of its ID, if any, to be kept as the only good one
' -- a good block that is kept is marked B_HEAD when it is a head block and B_TEMP when it is a body block, so
'    that mount can find the head blocks without reading any block again; mount traces each B_HEAD block's chain
' -- each cancel is the last flash write of a call; one that fails raises fsDeviceFault, which the caller tests
'
' @param thisBlockAddress - the block offset within the file system for "this" block
' @returns bBadCancelled - TRUE when "this" block was cancelled as a bad block, FALSE otherwise

' Local Variables:
' @local otherBlockAddress -the block offset within the file system for the "other" block
' @local thisCycleBits - the lifecycle bits of "this" block
' @local otherCycleBits - the lifecycle bits of the "other" block
' @local thisBlockID - the blockID of "this" block
' @local thisBlockState - the state "this" block takes when it is kept: B_HEAD for a head block, B_TEMP for a body block

  bBadCancelled := FALSE
  flash_read_block_addr(thisBlockAddress, @thisCycleBits, $000, $000)           'read first byte of block

  if lookdown(thisCycleBits.[7..5]: %011, %101, %110)                           'is block active? (a canceled or inactive block stays B_FREE)
    flash_read_block_addr(thisBlockAddress, @tmpBlockBuffer, $000, $FFF)        'read entire block

    if LONG[@tmpBlockBuffer + $FFC] <> block_crc(@tmpBlockBuffer)               'is CRC bad?
      flash_cancel_block(thisBlockAddress)                                      '..if so, cancel block to inhibit future CRC checks
      bBadCancelled := TRUE                                                     '..block status remains B_FREE, done
    elseifnot block_fields_in_range(@tmpBlockBuffer)                            'an ID, end pointer or data offset that would index past a table or a data area?
      flash_cancel_block(thisBlockAddress)                                      '..if so, cancel it as a bad block
      bBadCancelled := TRUE                                                     '..block status remains B_FREE, done
    else
      thisBlockID := LONG[@tmpBlockBuffer].[19..8]                              'this block is good, get its ID
      thisBlockState := LONG[@tmpBlockBuffer].[1] ? B_TEMP : B_HEAD             'its state once kept: a head block is B_HEAD, a body block B_TEMP

      ' if first block with this ID
      ifnot field[IDValid][thisBlockID]~~                                       'set ID flag and if it wasn't already set.. (after test, bit := 1)
        field[IDToBlock][thisBlockID] := thisBlockAddress                       '..set IDToBlock to this block
        field[BlockState][thisBlockAddress] := thisBlockState                   '..set B_HEAD or B_TEMP status for this block
      else
        ' we have a dupe ID, which do we keep?
        otherBlockAddress := field[IDToBlock][thisBlockID]                      'ID flag was already set, get other block with same ID

        flash_read_block_addr(otherBlockAddress, @otherCycleBits, $000, $000)   'read first byte of other block

        if lookdown(thisCycleBits.[7..5] << 3 | otherCycleBits.[7..5]: %011_110, %101_011, %110_101)  'if this block is newer..
          ' keep this one, cancel other
          field[IDToBlock][thisBlockID] := thisBlockAddress                     '..set IDToBlock to this block
          field[BlockState][thisBlockAddress] := thisBlockState                 '..set B_HEAD or B_TEMP status for this block
          field[BlockState][otherBlockAddress] := B_FREE                        '..set B_FREE status for other block
          flash_cancel_block(otherBlockAddress)                                 '..cancel other block
        else
          ' keep other, cancel this one
          flash_cancel_block(thisBlockAddress)                                  'else, cancel this block, block status remains B_FREE


PRI trace_file_set_flags(block_address, set) : valid | signature, block_id, bBroken

' Trace file chain marking (or clearing) block states until end of file is reached (or an error in block sequence is found)
' -- the chain is broken, and the file invalid, at a NextID that is not a block ID (BLOCKS or above), at a NextID no
'    good block holds, and at a head block inside the chain. A NextID of BLOCKS or above indexes no table: it is
'    tested before IDValid is read. The first pass of mount() and of can_mount() already treats a block holding such a
'    NextID as a bad block, so this test is the last guard, not the first
' -- a broken chain is not cut short at the break: the caller retraces it with set FALSE, and the blocks it reached
'    then go with the other blocks no chain reaches, which mount() cancels and can_mount() counts
' -- the walk follows at most BLOCKS links, the longest a chain can be; a chain still going at that bound is invalid
'
' @param block_address - the block offset within the file system for the block to trace
' @param set - true to set block states to B_HEAD/B_BODY, false to set block states to B_TEMP
' @returns valid - true if file is valid, false if file is invalid

' Local Variables:
' @local signature - block state bits of block being checked
' @local block_id - the blockID of the block being checked
' @local bBroken - TRUE once a link of the chain is found broken

  valid := FALSE
  bBroken := FALSE
  flash_read_block_addr(block_address, @signature, $000, $003)                  'read first long of initial block
  field[BlockState][block_address] := set ? B_HEAD : B_TEMP                     'set first block state to (set-pass: B_HEAD or clear-pass: B_TEMP)

  repeat BLOCKS                                                                 'limit repeat to BLOCKS so an endless chain is invalid
    ifnot signature.[0]                                                         'if last block, file is complete
      valid := TRUE
      quit
    block_id := signature.[31..20]                                              'get "next" ID from this full block
    if block_id > BLOCKS - 1                                                    'a NextID past the last block ID: broken, and no table is indexed with it
      bBroken := TRUE
    elseifnot field[IDValid][block_id]                                          'a NextID no good block holds (bit == 0): broken
      bBroken := TRUE
    else
      block_address := field[IDToBlock][block_id]                               'get address of block having this ID
      flash_read_block_addr(block_address, @signature, $000, $003)              'read first long of "next" block
      ifnot signature.[1]                                                       'if "next" is head block: broken
        bBroken := TRUE
      else
        field[BlockState][block_address] := set ? B_BODY : B_TEMP               'set block state to (set-pass: B_BODY or clear-pass: B_TEMP)
    if bBroken == TRUE
      quit



CON ' >>>  parameter type (no parameter)  <<<

PRI blocks_free() : count | block_address

' Return the count of available blocks
'
' @returns count - the number of filesystem blocks that are not in use

' Local Variables:
' @local block_address - the block offset within the file system

  repeat BLOCKS with block_address                                              'count free blocks
    ifnot field[BlockState][block_address]                                      'if the block is B_FREE
        count++


PRI has_free_blocks(blockCount) : bHasFree | block_address, freeCount

' Return TRUE when at least blockCount blocks are free, counting free blocks only until that many are found
'
' @param blockCount - the number of free blocks needed (0 or below is always met)
' @returns bHasFree - TRUE when at least blockCount blocks are B_FREE

' Local Variables:
' @local block_address - the block offset within the file system
' @local freeCount - the count of free blocks found so far

  freeCount := 0
  bHasFree := blockCount < 1                                                    'needing no block is always met
  if bHasFree == FALSE
    repeat BLOCKS with block_address                                            'count free blocks until there are enough
      ifnot field[BlockState][block_address]                                    'if the block is B_FREE
        if ++freeCount >= blockCount
          bHasFree := TRUE
          quit


PRI next_available_block_id() : block_id | byteIdx, bitIdx, possible_block_id

' Get a next available block ID
' -- the lowest free ID is taken; a byte of IDValids whose 8 IDs are all in use is passed over whole
'
' @returns block_id - the next ID that is not in use (or E_DRIVE_FULL if no blockID's are available)

' Local Variables:
' @local byteIdx - index of the byte of IDValids being checked
' @local bitIdx - index of the ID flag being checked within that byte
' @local possible_block_id - prospective blockID to check for availability

  block_id := E_DRIVE_FULL                                                      ' preset error
  repeat FLAGS_SIZE with byteIdx                                                ' pick the first free block ID
    if BYTE[@IDValids][byteIdx] <> ID_FLAGS_ALL_USED                            ' a byte with a clear flag holds a free ID (or IDs past the last one)
      repeat ID_FLAGS_PER_BYTE with bitIdx
        possible_block_id := byteIdx * ID_FLAGS_PER_BYTE + bitIdx               ' the flags of a byte are its IDs, lowest bit first
        if possible_block_id < BLOCKS                                           ' an ID past the last one is never taken
          ifnot field[IDValid][possible_block_id]~~                             ' set IDValid, was IDValid previously clear? (after test, bit := 1)
            block_id := possible_block_id                                       ' if IDValid was clear, return new ID
            quit
      if block_id >= 0                                                          ' an ID was taken: the search is done
        quit

  if block_id < 0                                                               ' if error, set error code
    LONG[@errorCode][cogid()] := block_id


PRI available_blocks() : bool | blk8Idx

' Return true if there are any available blocks
'
' @returns bool - true/false where true means blocks are available for write

' Local Variables:
' @local blk8Idx - index into the blocks allocated array

    'debug("available_blocks() ENTRY")
    bool := false
    ' TODO: if field[IDValids] ever has extra bits at end this code won't work!
    repeat FLAGS_SIZE with blk8Idx
        if BYTE[@IDValids][blk8Idx] <> $FF
            bool := true
            quit
    'debug("available_blocks() EXIT")


PRI next_block_address(spareBlocks) : block_address | blockFreeCount, freeBlockAddress, freeIndex, next_cycle_bits, pickAddress, bFull, bFault

' Return the address of the next block to which we should write
'
' The block is picked at random from the blocks that are not B_TEMP. A B_HEAD/B_BODY block that is picked is first
' moved to a free block: the copy is given the next lifecycle and activated at once. A block written but not yet
' activated is kept B_TEMP until it is activated, so a move only ever copies an active block. While fsTargetBlock
' names a block that is not B_TEMP, that block is taken in place of the random pick. On E_DRIVE_FULL no table and
' no block is changed.
'
' The pick is made first, and the free blocks are counted after it, only as far as the pick needs: a free block
' that is picked is taken at once when no spare block is asked for, and otherwise once spareBlocks more free blocks
' are found; a block that is picked to be moved needs a free block for the copy beyond the spare ones, and the full
' count, from which the free block is chosen at random.
'
' The random pick tries at most RANDOM_PICK_TRIES blocks. When every try lands on a B_TEMP block, each block is
' checked once, on from the last try, and the first one that is not B_TEMP is picked; when every block is B_TEMP
' there is nothing to pick and the result is E_DRIVE_FULL. Every E_DRIVE_FULL leaves at the one exit at the end.
'
' A flash write of a move that fails leaves the two copies as a power loss would, changes no table, and leaves at
' the same exit with E_FLASH_TIMEOUT, so every caller stops on the negative result as it does on E_DRIVE_FULL.
'
' @param spareBlocks - free blocks that must remain once this block is taken (0 when none need to)
' @returns block_address - the address of the next block to use, now B_TEMP, or E_DRIVE_FULL if no more than
' .. spareBlocks blocks are free, or every block is B_TEMP, or E_FLASH_TIMEOUT if a flash write of a move failed

' Local Variables:
' @local blockFreeCount - the count of free blocks
' @local freeBlockAddress - the offset within the file system of the free block
' @local freeIndex - a counter of free blocks
' @local next_cycle_bits - the next lifecycle bits to use for the new block
' @local pickAddress - the block offset within the file system of the block a try or the scan checks
' @local bFull - TRUE when no block can be taken: the result is E_DRIVE_FULL and nothing is changed
' @local bFault - TRUE when a flash write of the move failed: the result is E_FLASH_TIMEOUT and no table is changed

  bFull := FALSE
  bFault := FALSE
  block_address := fsTargetBlock                                                'a named block is taken while it is not B_TEMP
  if block_address <> NOT_ENABLED
    if field[BlockState][block_address] == B_TEMP
      block_address := NOT_ENABLED
  if block_address == NOT_ENABLED
    repeat RANDOM_PICK_TRIES                                                    'randomly pick an B_FREE/B_HEAD/B_BODY (not an B_TEMP) block
      pickAddress := getrnd() +// BLOCKS                                        '(random block selection results in +-5% wear leveling; the unsigned remainder is never negative)
      if field[BlockState][pickAddress] <> B_TEMP
        block_address := pickAddress
        quit
    if block_address == NOT_ENABLED                                             'every try was B_TEMP: check each block once, on from the last try
      repeat BLOCKS
        pickAddress := (pickAddress + 1) // BLOCKS
        if field[BlockState][pickAddress] <> B_TEMP
          block_address := pickAddress
          quit

  if block_address == NOT_ENABLED                                               'every block is B_TEMP: there is no block to pick
    bFull := TRUE
  elseif field[BlockState][block_address] == B_FREE                             'a free block is picked: it is one of the free blocks
    if spareBlocks > 0
      ifnot has_free_blocks(spareBlocks + ONE_FREE_BLOCK)                       'too few free blocks are left beside it
        bFull := TRUE
    ifnot bFull                                                                 'if the block can be taken, change its state to B_TEMP
      field[BlockState][block_address] := B_TEMP
  else
    blockFreeCount := blocks_free()                                             'a block to move: count the free blocks, one of which takes its copy
    if blockFreeCount <= spareBlocks                                            'no free block can be taken
      bFull := TRUE
    else
      ' now we are using head or body so we have to move it!
      if block_address == fsTargetBlock                                         'a named block stays named until it is moved
        fsTargetBlock := NOT_ENABLED
      freeIndex := getrnd() +// blockFreeCount                                  'randomly pick an B_FREE block to move the B_HEAD/B_BODY block to
      repeat BLOCKS with freeBlockAddress                                       'block is sHEAD/sBODY, must relocate it to an sFREE block
        ifnot field[BlockState][freeBlockAddress]                               'if the block is B_FREE
          ifnot freeIndex--
            quit

      ' evict this block!
      'debug("* nbaddr() evicting block ", uhex_word(block_address, freeBlockAddress))
      flash_read_block_addr(block_address, @tmpBlockBuffer, $000, $FFF)         'read the B_HEAD/B_BODY block
      next_cycle_bits := next_active_cycle(LONG[@tmpBlockBuffer].[7..5])        'advance its lifecycle
      flash_program_block(freeBlockAddress, @tmpBlockBuffer, next_cycle_bits)   'program the B_FREE block with the B_HEAD/B_BODY data
      flash_activate_block(freeBlockAddress, next_cycle_bits)                   'activate the B_FREE block, now superior to the original block
      flash_cancel_block(block_address)                                         'cancel the original block to complete the move

      if fsDeviceFault                                                          'the flash failed: no table is changed, the move is left as a power loss leaves it
        bFault := TRUE
      else
        field[IDToBlock][LONG[@tmpBlockBuffer].[19..8]] := freeBlockAddress     'update IDToBlock table
        field[BlockState][freeBlockAddress] := field[BlockState][block_address]\B_TEMP 'free block gets curr block state, -AND- set new block to B_TEMP

  if bFull                                                                      'no block can be taken: fail with E_DRIVE_FULL, nothing was changed
    block_address := (LONG[@errorCode][cogid()] := E_DRIVE_FULL)
  elseif bFault                                                                 'a flash write of the move failed
    block_address := E_FLASH_TIMEOUT


PRI mount_no_lock() : status | block_address, signature

' Build the tables from the flash and mark the filesystem mounted
' -- (internal version - for use when caller has already grabbed lock)
' -- every handle is freed, any open handle is abandoned; fsMounted becomes TRUE only once the tables are built
' -- the first pass reads every active block whole and leaves each good one B_HEAD (a head block) or B_TEMP (a body
'    block); the second traces the chain of each B_HEAD block, and the third cancels the blocks no chain reached
' -- a bad block is cancelled in the first pass: one whose CRC does not match, or whose ThisID, NextID, EndPtr or
'    head data offset is out of range, so no ID read from the flash indexes past a table. A file that loses a block that way loses its
'    whole chain in the third pass, as a file whose chain names a missing block does
' -- a cancel that fails raises fsDeviceFault and stops the passes there: fsMounted stays FALSE, and the next
'    mount() starts over
'
' @returns status - E_BAD_BLOCKS_REMOVED if BAD blocks were found and fixed, E_FLASH_TIMEOUT if the flash chip did
' .. not finish a cancel in time, otherwise 0 for success

' Local Variables:
' @local block_address - the block offset within the file system
' @local signature - block state bits of block being checked

    status := (LONG[@errorCode][cogid()] := SUCCESS)                            ' preset to success

    'debug("- mounting...")
    bytefill(@hStatus, 0, MAX_FILES_OPEN)                                       'clear handles
    fsFreeHndlCt := MAX_FILES_OPEN                                              'every handle is free again, any open handle is abandoned
    wordfill(@hCacheBlockID, NO_CACHED_BLOCK, MAX_FILES_OPEN)                   'and no handle's seek cache holds a block

    wordfill(@IDToBlocks, 0, ID_TO_BLOCKS_SZ)                                   'clear ID-to-block translation table
    bytefill(@IDValids, 0, FLAGS_SIZE)                                          'clear ID flags
    bytefill(@BlockStates, 0, STATES_SIZE)                                      'clear block states to B_FREE

    IDToBlock  := ^@IDToBlocks.[11..0]                                          'set field pointers
    IDValid    := ^@IDValids.[0]
    BlockState := ^@BlockStates.[1..0]

    'debug("mnt: - fixing power-out leftovers...")
    repeat BLOCKS with block_address                                            'check each block and fix any duplicate IDs
        if check_block_fix_dupe_id(block_address)                               '(recovers from incomplete block switchover due to power loss)
            status := (LONG[@errorCode][cogid()] := E_BAD_BLOCKS_REMOVED)       'a bad block was cancelled: a CRC that does not match, or a field out of range
        if fsDeviceFault                                                        'a cancel failed: no further block is checked
            quit
        ' leaves B_HEAD for each good head block and B_TEMP for each good body block

    if fsDeviceFault == FALSE
        'debug("mnt: - locating files...")
        ' the head blocks the first pass marked B_HEAD are the files to trace; no block is read again to find them
        repeat BLOCKS with block_address                                        'trace head blocks and cancel any broken files
            if field[BlockState][block_address] == B_HEAD                       'is this a good head block?
                'debug("mnt: - head block ", uhex_word(block_address))
                ifnot trace_file_set_flags(block_address, true)                 'yes, trace file, set block states to B_HEAD/B_BODY
                    trace_file_set_flags(block_address, false)                  'if error, retrace file, return block states to B_TEMP
            ' actual files are now marked as B_HEAD/B_BODY while rest are now B_TEMP

        'debug("mnt: - clearing dead blocks...")
        ' clear remaining B_TEMP blocks
        repeat BLOCKS with block_address                                        'cancel B_TEMP blocks that didn't become B_HEAD/B_BODY blocks
            if field[BlockState][block_address] == B_TEMP                       'is this an B_TEMP block?
                flash_read_block_addr(block_address, @signature, $000, $003)    'if so, read first long of block to get ID
                field[IDValid][signature.[19..8]]~                              '..cancel ID flag (bit := 0): the first pass made only a block whose ID is in range B_TEMP
                field[BlockState][block_address] := B_FREE                      '..return block state to B_FREE (zero)
                flash_cancel_block(block_address)                               '..cancel block to inhibit future CRC checks
                'debug(" -- found dead block...")
                status :=  (LONG[@errorCode][cogid()] := E_BAD_BLOCKS_REMOVED)
                if fsDeviceFault                                                '..a cancel failed: no further block is cancelled
                    quit

    if fsDeviceFault                                                            'a cancel failed: the filesystem stays unmounted
        status := (LONG[@errorCode][cogid()] := E_FLASH_TIMEOUT)
    else
        fsMounted := true                                                       ' set "mounted" indication, now that the tables are built


PRI configuration_status() : status

' Tell whether the constants an OBJ line can override leave a driver that can run
' -- the compiler accepts MAX_FILES_OPEN below 1 and a HANDLE_BASE other than 0 or 1, so mount(), format() and
'    can_mount() ask here, before they take the lock or touch the flash
'
' @returns status - SUCCESS, E_NO_HANDLE when MAX_FILES_OPEN is below 1, or E_BAD_HANDLE when HANDLE_BASE is not 0 or 1

    status := SUCCESS
    if MAX_FILES_OPEN < MIN_FILES_OPEN
        status := E_NO_HANDLE
    elseif HANDLE_BASE < MIN_HANDLE_BASE or HANDLE_BASE > MAX_HANDLE_BASE
        status := E_BAD_HANDLE


PRI release_lock(callStatus) : status

' Release the lock a locked method holds, taking the fault exit when the call raised the device fault
' -- every locked method releases the lock here and only here, and assigns the result to the variable it returns
'    its status in, before its last statement leaves that status in error()
' -- fsMounted and fsDeviceFault are both set only inside the call that raised the fault: the fault exit clears
'    fsMounted before any other call can take the lock, mount() and format() clear fsDeviceFault before the tables
'    are built, and mount_no_lock() leaves fsMounted clear after a fault. A call that finds the filesystem not
'    mounted, or that raised the fault while it was not mounted, releases the lock as usual with its own status
'
' @param callStatus - the status of the call: SUCCESS, an error code, or a handle
' @returns status - callStatus, or E_FLASH_TIMEOUT when this call raised the device fault while mounted

    if fsMounted and fsDeviceFault                                              'this call raised the device fault..
        status := unmount_on_fault()                                            '..unmount, which releases the lock
    else
        lockrel(fsLock)
        status := callStatus


PRI clear_device_fault() : status

' Clear the device fault before the flash is scanned again: wait for the chip to finish any erase or program
' that a failed flash wait left running, under the same bound, then clear fsDeviceFault
' -- a busy W25Q ignores the read command, so no block is read before the chip is ready
' -- the wait counts down an armed fault countdown like every other flash wait
'
' @returns status - SUCCESS when the chip is ready and the fault is cleared, E_FLASH_TIMEOUT when the chip was still
' .. busy at the bound (fsDeviceFault is raised again)

    status := flash_wait()
    if status == SUCCESS
        fsDeviceFault := FALSE


PRI unmount_on_fault() : status

' Unmount the filesystem after a device fault, and release the lock: the fault exit of a locked method whose call
' raised fsDeviceFault while the filesystem was mounted, taken only through release_lock()
' -- a flash wait that timed out, or a block program that was refused, leaves the flash as a power loss at that
'    point would, so nothing on the flash is undone: the next mount() recovers it
' -- every handle is freed without a commit, and every later call finds E_NOT_MOUNTED until mount()
' -- fsDeviceFault stays set, so every block program is refused until mount() or format() clears it
'
' @returns status - E_FLASH_TIMEOUT

    fsMounted := false                                                          'every later call finds the filesystem not mounted
    bytefill(@hStatus, 0, MAX_FILES_OPEN)                                       'every handle is freed, any open handle is abandoned
    fsFreeHndlCt := MAX_FILES_OPEN
    lockrel(fsLock)                                                             'release the lock, it is kept for the next mount()
    status := E_FLASH_TIMEOUT


PRI setup_semaphore() : status | newLock

' Create the driver's lock when no cog has yet: an election decides which calling cog creates it, and the
' other callers wait until it exists
' -- runs only while fsLock is -1; once created, fsLock is kept for the life of the run
' -- a cog that finds ELECT_FAILED, left by an election that found no free hub lock, sets ELECT_NONE and elects
'    again; a waiting cog leaves its wait on a valid fsLock or on ELECT_FAILED, so no cog waits on an election
'    that has ended
'
' @returns status - E_NO_LOCK_AVAIL if no hub lock was free, otherwise SUCCESS (fsLock holds the lock)

' Local Variables:
' @local newLock - the lock the hub gave the winning cog, negative when none was free

    status := SUCCESS
    if fsLock == -1
        'debug("setupSemaphore() ENTRY")
        if fsElection == ELECT_FAILED                                           ' an earlier election found no free lock: elect again
            fsElection := ELECT_NONE

        if fsElection == ELECT_NONE and can_acquire_lock()                      ' a won election has set ELECT_ALLOCATING
            'debug("! DID WIN, installing lock")
            newLock := locknew()                                                'I'm allocating... reserve a lock for driver use
            if newLock < 0                                                      'if lock allocation failed
                'debug("EEE failed to allocate lock")
                longfill(@fsCogCts, ELECT_UNSET, ELECT_ENTRIES)                 '..no entry of this election may decide the next one
                fsElection := ELECT_FAILED                                      '..and every waiting cog leaves its wait
            else
                fsLock := newLock
                fsElection := ELECT_NONE
        else
            'debug("! didn't win, waiting...")
            repeat until fsLock <> -1 or fsElection == ELECT_FAILED             ' the winner either creates the lock or finds none free
            'debug("! done waiting")

        LONG[@fsCogCts][cogid()] := ELECT_UNSET                                 ' this cog is no longer in the election
        if fsLock == -1
            status := (LONG[@errorCode][cogid()] := E_NO_LOCK_AVAIL)            '..return error

PRI can_acquire_lock() : bItsMe | myCogId, myCount, tmpCogId, otherCount

' Enter the election that decides which cog creates the lock, and tell whether this cog won it
' -- the cog writes getct() into its entry of fsCogCts, then waits ELECT_WAIT_MS for other cogs to enter
' -- it has won when no other entry holds a lower count (on a tie the lower cog ID wins), and, read after that
'    scan, the lock still does not exist, no cog is creating it, and its own entry is still in place: a winner
'    that found no free lock clears every entry, which ends the election for the cogs still waiting in it
' -- the winner sets ELECT_ALLOCATING at once; a cog that lost takes its entry out again, so only cogs still
'    deciding hold entries
'
' @returns bItsMe - True/False where True means is first caller and therefore should acquire lock

' Local Variables:
' @local myCogId - hold codID of caller
' @local myCount - the count this cog wrote into its entry
' @local tmpCogId - tmep cogID for iteration
' @local otherCount - the count in the entry being compared

    myCogId := cogid()                                                          ' get our cog ID
    myCount := getct()
    LONG[@fsCogCts][myCogId] := myCount                                         ' set our cog timer value
    waitms(ELECT_WAIT_MS)                                                       'let any other cogs get in here too

    bItsMe := true
    repeat tmpCogId from 0 to ELECT_ENTRIES - 1                                 ' now scan to see if we win!
        otherCount := LONG[@fsCogCts][tmpCogId]
        if tmpCogId <> myCogId and otherCount <> ELECT_UNSET                    ' an unset entry is a cog not in the election
            if otherCount < myCount or (otherCount == myCount and tmpCogId < myCogId)
                bItsMe := false                                                 ' an earlier cog entered

    if bItsMe and fsLock == -1 and fsElection == ELECT_NONE and LONG[@fsCogCts][myCogId] == myCount
        fsElection := ELECT_ALLOCATING                                          ' every cog that decides from now on loses
    else
        bItsMe := false
        LONG[@fsCogCts][myCogId] := ELECT_UNSET                                 ' a cog that lost is no longer in the election
        'debug("acquire_lock_and_mount() ", udec(myCount, myCogId), sdec(bItsMe))


CON ' >>>  parameter type (miscellaneous, one-off)  <<<

PRI next_active_cycle(cycle_in) : cycle_out

' Calculate and return the next active lifecycle pattern in (3 -> 5 -> 6 -> 3 -> 5 -> 6 -> 3... pattern)
'
' @param cycle_in - current lifecycle pattern
' @returns cycle_out - next lifecycle pattern in sequence

  cycle_out := (cycle_in * %001_001) >> 1 & %111                                  'get next lifecycle pattern


PRI block_crc(p_block_buffer) : crc
' Calculate and return the CRC for this pointed to block
'
' @param p_block_buffer - the address of the 4KB buffer for the file associated with this handle
' @returns crc - the calculated CRC for the block

  crc := getcrc(p_block_buffer, $AD0424F3 rev 31, BLOCK_SIZE - 4)  'compute CRC of a buffered block


PRI block_fields_in_range(pBlock) : bInRange | signature, dataStart, dataOffset

' Tell whether a block read whole holds only control values the driver can use: a block whose CRC matches can still
' carry a field no block this driver writes has, and such a block is a bad block
' -- ThisID, and the NextID of a block that has a next block, must be a block ID, 0..BLOCKS-1: each indexes the
'    BLOCKS-entry tables IDToBlocks and IDValids
' -- the EndPtr of a last block must lie in its block's data area: from its first data byte (ADDR_HEAD_DATA in a
'    head block, ADDR_BODY_DATA in a body block) up to ADDR_DATA_END, the CRC, which the EndPtr of a full block names
' -- the data offset of a head block in this driver's format (its filename CRC word is not the CRC32 of its filename,
'    as an old-format head block's is) is the low 12 bits of that word. In a last head block the offset must leave
'    the EndPtr at or past the data it skips: EndPtr >= ADDR_HEAD_DATA + data offset. In a head block with a next
'    block it must be at most MAX_HEAD_DATA_OFFSET: a trim that keeps data starting near the front of the next block
'    skips the head's whole data area and the bytes of that block before ADDR_HEAD_DATA
' -- every value is taken from the block image already read for its CRC: no flash byte is read
'
' @param pBlock - address of the whole block, as read from the flash
' @returns bInRange - TRUE when every field is in range

' Local Variables:
' @local signature - the first long of the block: {EndPtr or NextID[31..20], ThisID[19..8], lifecycle, type bits}
' @local dataStart - the offset of the first data byte of the block
' @local dataOffset - the data offset of a head block in this driver's format, 0 for every other block

  signature := LONG[pBlock]
  dataStart := signature.[1] ? ADDR_BODY_DATA : ADDR_HEAD_DATA                  'body or head?
  dataOffset := 0
  ifnot signature.[1]                                                           'a head block: in this driver's format it has a data offset
    if LONG[pBlock + ADDR_HEAD_FN_CRC] <> filename_crc32(pBlock + ADDR_HEAD_SONAME)
      dataOffset := LONG[pBlock + ADDR_HEAD_FN_CRC].[11..0]

  if signature.[19..8] > BLOCKS - 1                                             'ThisID past the last block ID
    bInRange := FALSE
  elseif signature.[0]                                                          'a block with a next block: its NextID must be a block ID
    bInRange := signature.[31..20] < BLOCKS and dataOffset <= MAX_HEAD_DATA_OFFSET
  else                                                                          'a last block: its EndPtr must lie in its data area, past any data offset
    bInRange := signature.[31..20] >= dataStart + dataOffset and signature.[31..20] <= ADDR_DATA_END


PRI size_in_blocks(size_in_bytes) : block_count | remainingSize, overflowBodyCount

' Return number of blocks for given file size
'
' @param size_in_bytes - the number of bytes in the file
' @returns block_count - the number of blocks that would be needed to contain the file

' Local Variables:
' @local remainingSize - temporary variable to hold the number of bytes remaining after the head block
' @local overflowBodyCount - temporary variable to hold the number of bytes that will be in the tail block

    block_count := 1
    if size_in_bytes > BYTES_IN_HEAD_BLOCK
        remainingSize := size_in_bytes - BYTES_IN_HEAD_BLOCK
        block_count += remainingSize / BYTES_IN_BODY_BLOCK
        overflowBodyCount := remainingSize +// BYTES_IN_BODY_BLOCK
        if overflowBodyCount > 0
            block_count++
    'debug("size_in_blocks()  # bytes: ", udec_(size_in_bytes), ", blocks: ", udec_(block_count))



CON ' --- Flash Operations ---

PRI flash_read_block_id(block_id, p_buffer, firstByte, lastByte)

' Return byte(s) read from physical block into memory at p_buffer
'
' @param block_id - the ID of block within the file system
' @param p_buffer - memory location in which to place the data
' @param firstByte - address of first byte to read
' @param lastByte - address of last byte to read

  flash_read_block_addr(field[IDToBlock][block_id], p_buffer, firstByte, lastByte)


PRI flash_read_block_addr(block_address, p_buffer, firstByte, lastByte)

' Return byte(s) read from physical block into memory at p_buffer
'
' @param block_address - the block offset within the file system
' @param p_buffer - memory location in which to place the data
' @param firstByte - address of first byte to read
' @param lastByte - address of last byte to read

  'debug("* rb(", uhex_word_(block_address), ", ", uhex_word_(firstByte), ", ", uhex_word_(lastByte),")")
  flash_command($03 | (FIRST_BLOCK + block_address) << 20 | firstByte << 8, 4)  'read 4KB block
  flash_receive(p_buffer, lastByte - firstByte + 1)                             'receive block data


PRI flash_activate_updated_block(block_address, pBuff) | nextCycleBits

' Write block in memory at block_address to physical block with updated life-cycle bits
'
' @param block_address - the block offset within the file system
' @param pBuff - memory location from which to get the data

' Local Variables:
' @local nextCycleBits - updated lifeCycle bit-pattern to place into block
  if showRTdebug
    debug("* program_updated_block() ", uhex_word(block_address))

  nextCycleBits := next_active_cycle(long[pBuff].[7..5])                        'get next cycle
  flash_program_block(block_address, pBuff, nextCycleBits)                      'program new block to replace old block
  flash_activate_block(block_address, nextCycleBits)                            'activate new block


PRI flash_program_block(block_address, p_buffer, cycle_bits) | pageIndex

' Write block in memory at block_address to physical block
'
' The block is programmed inactive, its CRC computed with cycle_bits in the lifecycle field, and the
' buffer is left holding cycle_bits there: what the block holds once flash_activate_block() is given
' the same cycle_bits.
'
' A block_address outside 0..BLOCKS-1 is refused before any command reaches the chip: nothing is
' sent to the flash, fsRefusedBlocks is incremented and fsDeviceFault is raised.
'
' While fsDeviceFault is set every block is refused the same way, without the count: nothing is sent to the
' flash. A wait that times out raises fsDeviceFault and stops the programming there, so no later page is sent;
' the block is left erased or part programmed and inactive, as a power loss at that point would leave it.
'
' @param block_address - the block offset within the file system
' @param p_buffer - memory location from which to get the data
' @param cycle_bits - lifeCycle bit-pattern to place into block

' Local Variables:
' @local pageIndex - index [0-15] of 256-Byte page within 4KB block
  if block_address < 0 or block_address > BLOCKS - 1                            'refuse a block outside the file system, before any command reaches the chip
    fsRefusedBlocks++
    fsDeviceFault := TRUE
  elseif fsDeviceFault == FALSE                                                 'no flash wait has timed out and no program was refused
    if showRTdebug
      debug("- program_block() ", uhex_word(block_address))

    flash_command($06, 1)                                                       'enable write
    flash_command($20 | (FIRST_BLOCK + block_address) << 20, 4)                 'erase 4KB block

    BYTE[p_buffer].[7..5] := cycle_bits                                         'install lifecycle for CRC computation
    LONG[p_buffer + $FFC] := block_crc(p_buffer)                                'compute and install CRC
    BYTE[p_buffer].[7..5]~~                                                     'remove lifecycle (:= %111), block will be inactive until activated

    if flash_wait() == SUCCESS                                                  'wait for erasure to complete (~45ms); a timeout sends no page
      repeat 16 with pageIndex                                                  'program 16 pages within 4KB block
        flash_command($06, 1)                                                   'enable write
        flash_command($02 | (FIRST_BLOCK + block_address) << 20 | pageIndex << 16, 4)  'program
        flash_send(p_buffer + pageIndex << 8, 256)                              'send 256 bytes
        if flash_wait() <> SUCCESS                                              'wait for programming to complete (~400us)..
          quit                                                                  '..a timeout sends no further page

    BYTE[p_buffer].[7..5] := cycle_bits                                         'the buffer again matches the block once activated, so a rewrite from it takes the next lifecycle


PRI flash_activate_block(block_address, cycle_bits)

' Write new activation pattern into block
'
' @param block_address - the block offset within the file system
' @param cycle_bits - lifeCycle bit-pattern to place into block

  if showRTdebug
    debug("- activate_block() ", uhex_word(block_address))
  flash_program_bit(block_address, cycle_bits << 5 | %00011111)                 'clear one cycle bit to activate block


PRI flash_cancel_block(block_address)

' Clear the block's cycle bits to cancel it
'
' @param block_address - the block offset within the file system

  if showRTdebug
    debug("- cancel_block() ", uhex_word(block_address))

  flash_program_bit(block_address, %00011111)                                   'clear all cycle bits to cancel block


PRI flash_program_bit(block_address, bit_pattern)

' Write new bit_pattern into 1st byte of block (this contains the life-cycle bits) this is our most atomic operation
'
' A block_address outside 0..BLOCKS-1 is refused before any command reaches the chip: nothing is
' sent to the flash, fsRefusedBlocks is incremented and fsDeviceFault is raised.
'
' While fsDeviceFault is set every block is refused the same way, without the count: nothing is sent to the
' flash. A wait that times out raises fsDeviceFault.
'
' @param block_address - the block offset within the file system
' @param bit_pattern - the value to be placed in first byte of block

  if block_address < 0 or block_address > BLOCKS - 1                            'refuse a block outside the file system, before any command reaches the chip
    fsRefusedBlocks++
    fsDeviceFault := TRUE
  elseif fsDeviceFault == FALSE                                                 'no flash wait has timed out and no program was refused
    flash_command($06, 1)                                                       'enable write
    flash_command($02 | (FIRST_BLOCK + block_address) << 20, 4)                 'program
    flash_send(@bit_pattern, 1)                                                 'send byte with bit pattern
    flash_wait()                                                                'wait for programming to complete; a timeout raises fsDeviceFault


PRI flash_wait() : status | statusBits, startTicks, boundTicks

' Wait for FLASH Chip to become ready, for no longer than fsFlashWaitMs
'
' The BUSY bit of status register 1 is polled until it clears. The time is measured as the ticks elapsed since the
' wait began, getct() - startTicks, compared signed against the bound: the subtraction is correct across a wrap of
' the 32-bit counter, and the signed compare is correct while the elapsed count stays below 2^31 ticks, which the
' bound keeps it (FLASH_TIMEOUT_MS). A chip still busy past the bound is a timeout, and raises fsDeviceFault.
'
' While fsFaultCountdown is not FAULT_OFF each wait counts it down by one, and the wait that finds it at
' FAULT_THIS_WAIT reports a timeout without polling the chip, raises fsDeviceFault, and sets it to FAULT_OFF.
'
' @returns status - SUCCESS when the chip is ready, E_FLASH_TIMEOUT when it was still busy at the bound

' Local Variables:
' @local statusBits - status register bits read from FLASH Chip
' @local startTicks - the system counter when the wait began
' @local boundTicks - the bound in system clock ticks

  status := SUCCESS
  if fsFaultCountdown <> FAULT_OFF                                              'a fault is armed: count this wait (the one test in normal operation)
    if fsFaultCountdown == FAULT_THIS_WAIT                                      '..this is the wait that fails
      fsFaultCountdown := FAULT_OFF
      fsDeviceFault := TRUE
      status := E_FLASH_TIMEOUT
    else
      fsFaultCountdown--

  if status == SUCCESS
    boundTicks := clkfreq / MS_PER_SECOND * fsFlashWaitMs
    startTicks := getct()
    repeat
      flash_command($05, 1)                                                     ' read status register
      flash_receive(@statusBits, 1)
      if statusBits.[0] == 0                                                    ' BUSY bit clear: the chip is ready
        quit
      if getct() - startTicks > boundTicks                                      ' still busy at the bound (elapsed ticks, signed)
        fsDeviceFault := TRUE
        status := E_FLASH_TIMEOUT
        quit

{$flexspin
' flexspin stores local variables in registers, rather than HUB, so for flash commands we need HUB space for temporary storage
VAR
   LONG m_command                                                               ' HUB storage for flash_command use
}

PRI flash_command(command, count)

' Send flash command to FLASH Chip via SPI
'
' @param command - the command for the chip to execute
' @param count - number of bytes to send: must be between 1 and 4
'
' uses the member variable m_command as temporary storage

              org

              fltl      #SF_MISO                        '2!     DO input

              fltl      #SF_SCLK                        '2!     reset CK smart pin
              wrpin     ##%001000000_01_00101_0,#SF_SCLK '2      set CK for transition output, inverted - SPI mode 3
              wrpin     ##%001000000_00_00000_0,#SF_CS  '2      set CK for transition output, inverted - SPI mode 3
              wxpin     #4,#SF_SCLK                     '2      set timebase to 4 clocks per transition

              drvl      #SF_CS                          '2!     CS high
              waitx     #14                             '2+14   CS deselect is 50ns at 350 MHz (50 / 2.777ns = 18)
              drvh      #SF_CS                          '2!     CS low

              movbyts   command,#%%1230                 'reverse order of post-command address bytes for sending

              end
{$flexspin
#ifdef __FLEXSPIN__
  ' in flexspin we have to copy the register to HUB explicitly (otherwise @command will force command
  ' into HUB, which will conflict with using `command` in the inline assembly code)
  m_command := command                      'copy command from register to HUB memory
  flash_send(@m_command, count)             'send command
#else
}
  flash_send(@command, count)
{$flexspin #endif}

PRI flash_send(p_buffer, count) | tx_byte

' Write bytes to the FLASH Chip via SPI
'
' @param p_buffer - memory location from which to get the data
' @param byteCount - number of bytes to send

' Local Variables:
' @local tx_byte - the byte value being sent over SPI

              org

              rdfast    #0,p_buffer                     'start fast read

.byte         rfbyte    tx_byte                         '2  read byte to send
              shl       tx_byte,#24 + 1         wc      '2  msb-justify bits and get D7 into c

              rep       @.r,#1                          '2  protect from interrupts
              fltl      #SF_SCLK                        '2! reset smart pin CK
              drvl      #SF_SCLK                        '2! start smart pin CK, starts base period
              drvc      #SF_MOSI                        '2! output D7
              wypin     #16,#SF_SCLK                    '2* begin 16 clock transitions
              rep       @.r,#7                          '2  repeat to output D6..D0
              shl       tx_byte,#1              wc      '2    get data bit
              drvc      #SF_MOSI                        '2!   output data bit
              waitx     #2                              '2+2  delay makes 8 clocks/bit
.r
              djnz      count,#.byte                    '4|2 loop if another byte to send

              drvl      #SF_MOSI                        '2! DI low

              end


PRI flash_receive(p_buffer, count) | rx_byte

' Read bytes from the FLASH Chip via SPI
'
' @param p_buffer - memory location into which to put the data
' @param count - number of bytes to receive

' Local Variables:
' @local rx_byte - gather bits received into this byte

              org

              wrfast    #0,p_buffer                     'start fast write

.byte         rep       @.r,#1                          '2   protect from interrupts
              fltl      #SF_SCLK                        '2!     reset smart pin CK
              drvl      #SF_SCLK                        '2!     start smart pin CK, starts base period
              wypin     #16,#SF_SCLK                    '2*     begin 16 clock transitions
              waitx     #7                              '2+3    align TESTP's to before 2nd clock fall (DC..350MHz+)
              rep       @.r,#8                          '2      repeat to input D7..D0
              waitx     #2                              '2+2      delay makes 8 clocks/bit
              testp     #SF_MISO                wc      '2        input data bit
              rcl       rx_byte,#1                      '2        save data bit
.r
              wfbyte    rx_byte                         '2   write received byte
              djnz      count,#.byte                    '4|2 loop if another byte to receive

              drvl      #SF_CS                          '2!  CS high, terminates command
              fltl      #SF_SCLK                        '2!  reset smart pin forcing dir to be correct

              end


{   ' REMOVE BEFORE FLIGHT: uncomment this line before commit to git, and release!!!

' ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
'   these methods are for regression testing only - they are not used in production code

CON { constants exposed for regression testing }

     MAX_FILE_LEN_IN_BLOCKS = 16 ' not real, just our limit for passing data back to UT's

     ' status of a block hook given a block address outside 0..BLOCKS-1, or an operation it does not have
     E_TEST_BAD_BLOCK_ARG = -99

     ' The operations TEST_changeBlock() performs on one block:
     '  TEST_BLK_PROGRAM  - erase the block, then program it from an image, leaving it inactive
     '  TEST_BLK_ACTIVATE - write a lifecycle into the block
     '  TEST_BLK_CANCEL   - cancel the block
     '  TEST_BLK_CORRUPT  - clear TEST_CORRUPT_BIT in the first byte, so the stored CRC no longer matches
     TEST_BLK_PROGRAM = 1
     TEST_BLK_ACTIVATE = 2
     TEST_BLK_CANCEL = 3
     TEST_BLK_CORRUPT = 4

     TEST_CORRUPT_BIT = %0000_0100                                  ' a reserved bit of the first byte of a block, covered by the block CRC

     TEST_BLOCK_BELOW_FS = -4                                       ' relative block just below the file system: flash sector $07C000, in the boot image area

     ' The counts TEST_setElectionCounts() places in the entries of the lock election:
     '  TEST_COUNT_UNSET  - the count every entry holds at power-up, before any cog has entered the election
     '  TEST_COUNT_LOWEST - the lowest count an entry can hold, the one a cog leaves when getct() read $8000_0000
     TEST_COUNT_UNSET = POSX
     TEST_COUNT_LOWEST = NEGX
     TEST_ELECTION_ENTRIES = 8                                      ' entries of the lock election, one for each cog

DAT { regression testing buffers and such }

   blockForUser         BYTE    0[4096]
   block2ForUser        BYTE    0[4096]


CON { methods supporting regression testing }


PUB TEST_count_file_bytes(p_filename) : bytes_used, bytes_free, block_count | signature

'' TEST METHOD: return information about a file: blocks allocated, bytes used, bytes free
''  forwarding access to internal method: count_file_bytes()
''
'' @param p_filename - address of a zstring containing the filename
'' @returns bytes_used - the number of bytes written to file, E_FILE_NOT_FOUND if the file doesn't exist
'' @returns bytes_free - the number of bytes allocated but not yet written (in the last block)
'' @returns block_count - the number of blocks allocation to this file

' Local Variables:
' @local signature - the block state bits of the block being counted
  'debug("TEST_count_file_bytes() ENTRY")

  ifnot fsMounted
    return (LONG[@errorCode][cogid()] := E_NOT_MOUNTED), 0, 0

  repeat while locktry(fsLock) == 0                                             ' lock for exlusive use

  LONG[@errorCode][cogid()] := SUCCESS
  if signature := get_file_head_signature(p_filename)                           'does file exist?
    'debug("* have signature")
    bytes_used, bytes_free, block_count := count_file_bytes(signature.[19..8], head_data_start_of_format(signature.[19..8], signature.[2] == 0))
  else
    bytes_used := (LONG[@errorCode][cogid()] := E_FILE_NOT_FOUND)
  'debug("TEST_count_file_bytes() EXIT")

  lockrel(fsLock)                                                               ' release the lock, we're done with it


PUB TEST_getHead4kBlock(p_filename) : p_buffer | signature
'' TEST METHOD: Return the named file's head block
''
'' The block is read into a buffer shared by every TEST method that returns a block, so this method is for
'' use by one cog at a time: the returned buffer is valid only until the next such call from any cog.
''
'' @param p_filename - address of a zstring containing the filename
'' @returns p_buffer - address of a 4KB buffer containing the head block, or a negative error code:
'' .. E_NOT_MOUNTED if the file system is NOT mounted, E_FILE_NOT_FOUND if the file doesn't exist

' Local Variables:
' @local signature - temporary storage for a block state bits

    p_buffer := E_NOT_MOUNTED
    if fsMounted
        repeat while locktry(fsLock) == 0                                       ' lock for exlusive use

        p_buffer := @blockForUser
        if signature := get_file_head_signature(p_filename)                     ' if file exists...
            flash_read_block_addr(field[IDToBlock][signature.[19..8]], @blockForUser, $000, $FFF)   'read head block into buffer
        else
            p_buffer := E_FILE_NOT_FOUND
        lockrel(fsLock)                                                         ' release the lock, we're done with it

    if p_buffer < 0
        LONG[@errorCode][cogid()] := p_buffer


PUB TEST_get4kBlockAndNextAtOffset(p_filename, file_position) : p_buffer, p_buffer2, blkAddr1, blkAddr2 | signature, block_id
'' TEST METHOD: Return the file block holding a given file position, and the block that follows it
''
'' The blocks are read into buffers shared by every TEST method that returns a block, so this method is for
'' use by one cog at a time: the returned buffers are valid only until the next such call from any cog.
''
'' @param p_filename - address of a zstring containing the filename
'' @param file_position - byte position within the file
'' @returns p_buffer - address of a 4KB buffer containing the block holding file_position, 0 if the file is not
'' .. found or the file system is NOT mounted (error() then holds E_NOT_MOUNTED)
'' @returns p_buffer2 - address of a 4KB buffer containing the next block, 0 if there is no next block
'' @returns blkAddr1 - block address of the block in p_buffer
'' @returns blkAddr2 - block address of the block in p_buffer2, 0 if there is no next block

' Local Variables:
' @local signature - temporary storage for a block state bits
' @local block_id - ID of the block being read

    p_buffer := 0
    p_buffer2 := 0
    blkAddr1 := 0
    blkAddr2 := 0
    if fsMounted
        repeat while locktry(fsLock) == 0                                       ' lock for exlusive use

        if signature := get_file_head_signature(p_filename)                     ' if file exists...
            p_buffer := @blockForUser
            block_id, _, _ := locate_file_byte(signature.[19..8], file_position) ' locate byte in file
            blkAddr1 := field[IDToBlock][block_id]
            flash_read_block_id(block_id, p_buffer, $000, $FFF)                 ' read lead block into buffer
            if LONG[p_buffer].[0]                                               ' if NOT last block
                p_buffer2 := @block2ForUser
                block_id := LONG[p_buffer].[31..20]
                blkAddr2 := field[IDToBlock][block_id]
                flash_read_block_id(block_id, p_buffer2, $000, $FFF)            ' ..read next block into buffer
        lockrel(fsLock)                                                         ' release the lock, we're done with it
    else
        LONG[@errorCode][cogid()] := E_NOT_MOUNTED


PUB TEST_getTail4kBlock(p_filename) : p_buffer | signature, block_address
'' TEST METHOD: Return the named file's tail block
''
'' The block is read into a buffer shared by every TEST method that returns a block, so this method is for
'' use by one cog at a time: the returned buffer is valid only until the next such call from any cog.
''
'' @param p_filename - address of a zstring containing the filename
'' @returns p_buffer - address of a 4KB buffer containing the tail block, or a negative error code:
'' .. E_NOT_MOUNTED if the file system is NOT mounted, E_FILE_NOT_FOUND if the file doesn't exist

' Local Variables:
' @local signature - temporary storage for a block state bits
' @local block_address - address of the block being read

    p_buffer := E_NOT_MOUNTED
    if fsMounted
        repeat while locktry(fsLock) == 0                                       ' lock for exlusive use

        p_buffer := @blockForUser
        if signature := get_file_head_signature(p_filename)                     ' if file exists...
            ' locate tail
            block_address := field[IDToBlock][signature.[19..8]]                ' get this block address
            if signature.[0]                                                    ' if not last block, walk to the tail
                repeat
                    ifnot signature.[0]                                         ' if last block, exit loop
                        quit
                    block_address := field[IDToBlock][signature.[31..20]]       ' get next block address
                    flash_read_block_addr(block_address, @signature, $000, $003) ' read the first long of the head/body block

            flash_read_block_addr(block_address, @blockForUser, $000, $FFF)     ' read tail block into buffer
            if showRTdebug
                debug("returning: id=", udec_word_(signature.[19..8]), " addr=", uhex_word(block_address))
        else
            p_buffer := E_FILE_NOT_FOUND
        lockrel(fsLock)                                                         ' release the lock, we're done with it

    if p_buffer < 0
        LONG[@errorCode][cogid()] := p_buffer


PUB TEST_getFileBlockSignatures(p_filename, p_sigLong) : sigCount | signature[2], block_address, bIsHeadSig
'' TEST METHOD: copy the named file's block signatures, for the blocks allocated to the file, into a caller's array
''
'' @param p_filename - address of a zstring containing the filename
'' @param p_sigLong - address of a long array of at least MAX_FILE_LEN_IN_BLOCKS * 2 longs to receive the signatures
'' @returns sigCount - the number of longs placed in the array (two per block: signature, data offset),
'' .. 0 if the file doesn't exist or the file system is NOT mounted (error() then holds E_NOT_MOUNTED).
'' .. A chain longer than MAX_FILE_LEN_IN_BLOCKS blocks is listed up to that many; the last block listed
'' .. then still has its more-blocks bit (signature bit 0) set

' Local Variables:
' @local signature - temporary storage for a block state bits
' @local block_address - the block offset within the file system
' @local bIsHeadSig - true while reading the file's head block

    sigCount := 0
    if fsMounted
        repeat while locktry(fsLock) == 0                                       ' lock for exlusive use

        if signature := get_file_head_signature(p_filename)                     ' if file exists...
            block_address := field[IDToBlock][signature.[19..8]]                ' get this block address
            bIsHeadSig := true
            repeat
                flash_read_block_addr(block_address, @signature, $000, $007)    ' read the first long of the head/body block
                LONG[p_sigLong][sigCount++] := bIsHeadSig ? signature : signature[0] ' place this signature in list
                LONG[p_sigLong][sigCount++] := signature[1]                     ' place the dataOffset in list
                ifnot signature.[0]                                             ' if last block, exit loop
                    quit
                if sigCount >= MAX_FILE_LEN_IN_BLOCKS * 2                       ' if filled table, exit loop
                    quit
                bIsHeadSig := false
                block_address := field[IDToBlock][signature.[31..20]]           ' get next block address
        lockrel(fsLock)                                                         ' release the lock, we're done with it
    else
        LONG[@errorCode][cogid()] := E_NOT_MOUNTED


PUB TEST_getCommitBlockSignatures(handle, p_sigLong) : sigCount | pBuff, endPtr, signature[2], block_address, lastSignature[2], lastBlockId
'' TEST METHOD: copy the pending-commit chain signatures for a handle into a caller's array
''
'' @param handle - a handle to an open file
'' @param p_sigLong - address of a long array of at least MAX_FILE_LEN_IN_BLOCKS * 2 longs to receive the signatures
'' @returns sigCount - the number of longs placed in the array (two per block: signature, data offset),
'' .. 0 if the file system is NOT mounted or the handle is not valid (error() then holds E_NOT_MOUNTED or E_BAD_HANDLE).
'' .. A chain longer than MAX_FILE_LEN_IN_BLOCKS blocks is listed up to that many; the last block listed
'' .. then still has its more-blocks bit (signature bit 0) set

' Local Variables:
' @local pBuff - address of the handle's in-memory block buffer
' @local endPtr - end-of-data offset within the handle's tail block
' @local signature - temporary storage for a block state bits
' @local block_address - the block offset within the file system
' @local lastSignature - signature and data offset of the in-memory (tail) block
' @local lastBlockId - ID of the in-memory (tail) block

' NOTE: !!! INTERNAL USE !!!   signature.[4..2] are unused - we use .[3] herein to indicate modified!

    sigCount := 0
    handle := handle_index(handle)                                              'from here on handle is the index in the handle tables
    ifnot fsMounted
        LONG[@errorCode][cogid()] := E_NOT_MOUNTED
    elseif handle < 0 or handle > MAX_FILES_OPEN - 1
        LONG[@errorCode][cogid()] := E_BAD_HANDLE
    else
        repeat while locktry(fsLock) == 0                                       ' lock for exlusive use

        endPtr := hSeekPtr[handle] <> NOT_ENABLED ? hSeekPtr[handle] : hEndPtr[handle]

        pBuff := buffer_pointer(handle)                                         ' get block buffer pointer
        if hChainBlockAddr[handle] == 0
            ' no commit chain (must be single block write)
            ' in this case return signature from in-memory buffer[handle]
            signature[0] := LONG[pBuff]
            signature[0].[3] := hModified[handle] ? 0 : 1                       ' special FLAG for this routine (block is modified)
            signature[1] := LONG[pBuff][1]
            ifnot signature.[0]                                                 ' if is tail block
                signature[0].[31..20] := endPtr
            lastSignature := 0
        else
            ' NOTE: hChainBlockAddr[handle] has block address of head of commit chain
            lastSignature[0] := LONG[pBuff]
            lastSignature[0].[3] := hModified[handle] ? 0 : 1                   ' special FLAG for this routine (block is modified)
            lastSignature[1] := LONG[pBuff][1]
            ifnot lastSignature.[0]                                             ' if is tail block
                lastSignature[0].[31..20] := endPtr
            lastBlockId := lastSignature[0].[19..8]
            flash_read_block_addr(hChainBlockAddr[handle], @signature, $000, $007) ' read first long of block to get ID

        repeat
            LONG[p_sigLong][sigCount++] := signature[0]                         ' place this signature in list
            LONG[p_sigLong][sigCount++] := signature[1]                         ' place this data offset in list
            ifnot signature.[0]                                                 ' if last block, exit loop
                quit
            if sigCount >= MAX_FILE_LEN_IN_BLOCKS * 2                           ' if filled table, exit loop
                quit
            if signature.[0] == 1 and signature.[31..20] == lastBlockId         ' if more block pointing to last in memory block
                LONG[p_sigLong][sigCount++] := lastSignature[0]                 ' place final buffer signature in list
                LONG[p_sigLong][sigCount++] := lastSignature[1]                 ' place final data offset in list
                quit
            block_address := field[IDToBlock][signature.[31..20]]               ' get next block address
            flash_read_block_addr(block_address, @signature, $000, $007)        ' read the first long of the head/body block

        lockrel(fsLock)                                                         ' release the lock, we're done with it


PUB TEST_getBlockAddressForId(blockID, possHandle) : block_address
'' TEST METHOD: Return block address associated with block ID
''
'' @param blockID - the ID of the block
'' @param possHandle - possible handle of file
'' @returns block_address - the address the ID currently maps to, or 0 if block ID is not in use
'' .. or the file system is NOT mounted (error() then holds E_NOT_MOUNTED)

    block_address := 0
    possHandle := handle_index(possHandle)                                      'from here on possHandle is the index in the handle tables
    if fsMounted
        repeat while locktry(fsLock) == 0                                       ' lock for exlusive use

        if field[IDValid][blockID]
            if possHandle >= 0 and hChainBlockID[possHandle] == blockID
                block_address := hChainBlockAddr[possHandle]
            else
                block_address := field[IDToBlock][blockID]
        lockrel(fsLock)                                                         ' release the lock, we're done with it
    else
        LONG[@errorCode][cogid()] := E_NOT_MOUNTED


PUB TEST_freeBlockIdCount() : idCount | blockID
'' TEST METHOD: Return the number of block IDs that are free: not marked valid, so a new block can take one
''
'' @returns idCount - the count of free block IDs, or 0 if the file system is NOT mounted
'' .. (error() then holds E_NOT_MOUNTED)

' Local Variables:
' @local blockID - the ID being checked

    idCount := 0
    if fsMounted
        repeat while locktry(fsLock) == 0                                       ' lock for exlusive use

        repeat BLOCKS with blockID
            ifnot field[IDValid][blockID]
                idCount++
        lockrel(fsLock)                                                         ' release the lock, we're done with it
    else
        LONG[@errorCode][cogid()] := E_NOT_MOUNTED


PUB TEST_getHandleStatusDump(p_buffer, guardBytes) : byteCount
'' TEST METHOD: copy the handle status bytes, and the bytes on each side of them, into a caller's buffer
''
'' The copy holds guardBytes bytes that precede the handle status array, the MAX_FILES_OPEN handle status
'' bytes, then guardBytes bytes that follow them, so a write just outside the array shows as a difference
'' between two dumps. The array is the one of the object instance this method is called through.
''
'' @param p_buffer - address of a buffer of at least (guardBytes * 2) + MAX_FILES_OPEN bytes
'' @param guardBytes - number of bytes to copy on each side of the handle status array
'' @returns byteCount - the number of bytes placed in the buffer, 0 if the file system is NOT mounted
'' .. (error() then holds E_NOT_MOUNTED)

    byteCount := 0
    if fsMounted
        repeat while locktry(fsLock) == 0                                       ' lock for exlusive use

        byteCount := guardBytes + MAX_FILES_OPEN + guardBytes
        bytemove(p_buffer, @hStatus - guardBytes, byteCount)
        lockrel(fsLock)                                                         ' release the lock, we're done with it
    else
        LONG[@errorCode][cogid()] := E_NOT_MOUNTED


PUB TEST_filename_for_handle(handle) : pStr

'' TEST METHOD: return pointer to filename associated with handle
''
'' @param handle - a handle to an open file
'' @returns pStr - pointer to filename string or 0 in which case error() contains:
'' .. E_NOT_MOUNTED if the file system is NOT mounted
'' .. E_BAD_HANDLE if the handle is not valid

  'debug("* TST_fn_for_h() ", sdec(fsMounted))
  handle := handle_index(handle)                                                'from here on handle is the index in the handle tables
  ifnot fsMounted
    LONG[@errorCode][cogid()] := E_NOT_MOUNTED
    return 0
  elseif handle < 0 or handle > MAX_FILES_OPEN - 1
    LONG[@errorCode][cogid()] := E_BAD_HANDLE
    return 0

  LONG[@errorCode][cogid()] := SUCCESS
  pStr := @hFilename + handle * FILENAME_SIZE


PUB TEST_enableRTdebug()

'' Turn on showing of debug for low level routines

   showRTdebug := TRUE

PUB TEST_filename_for_block_addr(block_address, pFilename, maxBytes) : status | BYTE filenameBffr[$088]
'' TEST METHOD: return filename for given head block address
''
'' This reads the block straight from flash and uses none of the driver's tables, so it works whether or
'' not the file system is mounted; the lock is created here if no cog has created it yet.
''
'' @param block_address - address of file head block
'' @param pFilename - address of location to place zstring
'' @param maxBytes - max bytes at target location
'' @returns status - SUCCESS (0) or E_NO_LOCK_AVAIL

' Local Variables:
' @local filenameBffr - the head block's header bytes, which hold the filename

    status := SUCCESS
    if fsLock == -1                                                             ' don't acquire lock if already have it
        status := setup_semaphore()

    if status == SUCCESS
        LONG[@errorCode][cogid()] := SUCCESS                                    ' preset to success
        repeat while locktry(fsLock) == 0                                       ' lock for exlusive use

        flash_read_block_addr(block_address, @filenameBffr, $000, $087)         ' read the head block's header bytes
        strcopy(pFilename, @BYTE[@filenameBffr][8], maxBytes - 1)

        lockrel(fsLock)                                                         ' release the lock, we're done with it


PUB TEST_readBlock(block_address) : p_buffer | status
'' TEST METHOD: read one block of the file system straight from the flash
''
'' This reads the flash directly and uses none of the driver's tables, so it works whether or not the file
'' system is mounted; the lock is created here if no cog has created it yet. The block is read into a buffer
'' shared by every TEST method that returns a block, so this method is for use by one cog at a time: the
'' returned buffer is valid only until the next such call from any cog.
''
'' @param block_address - the block offset within the file system
'' @returns p_buffer - address of a 4KB buffer containing the block, or a negative error code:
'' .. E_TEST_BAD_BLOCK_ARG if block_address is outside 0..BLOCKS-1, E_NO_LOCK_AVAIL if the lock could not be created

' Local Variables:
' @local status - SUCCESS, or the reason the block was not read

    status := SUCCESS
    if block_address < 0 or block_address > BLOCKS - 1                         ' refuse an address outside the file system
        status := E_TEST_BAD_BLOCK_ARG
    elseif fsLock == -1                                                         ' don't acquire lock if already have it
        status := setup_semaphore()

    if status == SUCCESS
        repeat while locktry(fsLock) == 0                                       ' lock for exlusive use

        flash_read_block_addr(block_address, @blockForUser, $000, BLOCK_SIZE - 1) ' read the whole block into the buffer
        lockrel(fsLock)                                                         ' release the lock, we're done with it
        p_buffer := @blockForUser
    else
        p_buffer := status

    LONG[@errorCode][cogid()] := status


PUB TEST_changeBlock(blockOp, block_address, p_source, cycle_bits) : status | BYTE firstByte
'' TEST METHOD: program, activate, cancel or corrupt one block of the file system, straight on the flash
''
'' Only the flash changes: the driver's tables are not updated, so call this while the file system is NOT
'' mounted and let the next can_mount() or mount() read the result. The lock is created here if no cog has
'' created it yet. The block address and the operation are checked before any flash command is sent, so a
'' block address outside 0..BLOCKS-1 never reaches the flash and no call can write below the file system
'' or past its end.
''
'' @param blockOp - the operation: TEST_BLK_PROGRAM erases the block and programs it from p_source with
'' .. cycle_bits installed for the CRC, leaving the block inactive; TEST_BLK_ACTIVATE writes cycle_bits into
'' .. the block; TEST_BLK_CANCEL cancels the block; TEST_BLK_CORRUPT clears TEST_CORRUPT_BIT in the first byte
'' .. of the block, so its stored CRC no longer matches while its lifecycle stays as it was
'' @param block_address - the block offset within the file system
'' @param p_source - address of a 4KB block image, used by TEST_BLK_PROGRAM only; the image is copied, not changed
'' @param cycle_bits - lifeCycle bit-pattern to place into block, used by TEST_BLK_PROGRAM and TEST_BLK_ACTIVATE only
'' A flash wait that times out raises the device fault, and while it is raised every block program is refused;
'' mount() and format() clear it. Called while the file system is mounted, such a call takes the fault exit and
'' returns E_FLASH_TIMEOUT with the file system unmounted.
''
'' @returns status - SUCCESS (0) if the operation was performed, E_TEST_BAD_BLOCK_ARG if block_address is
'' .. outside 0..BLOCKS-1 or blockOp is not one of the operations (nothing is sent to the flash),
'' .. E_FLASH_TIMEOUT if it was called while mounted and the flash failed, or E_NO_LOCK_AVAIL if the lock
'' .. could not be created

' Local Variables:
' @local firstByte - first byte of the block, read for TEST_BLK_CORRUPT

    status := SUCCESS
    if block_address < 0 or block_address > BLOCKS - 1                         ' refuse an address outside the file system
        status := E_TEST_BAD_BLOCK_ARG
    elseifnot lookdown(blockOp : TEST_BLK_PROGRAM, TEST_BLK_ACTIVATE, TEST_BLK_CANCEL, TEST_BLK_CORRUPT)
        status := E_TEST_BAD_BLOCK_ARG                                          ' refuse an operation this method does not have
    elseif fsLock == -1                                                         ' don't acquire lock if already have it
        status := setup_semaphore()

    if status == SUCCESS
        repeat while locktry(fsLock) == 0                                       ' lock for exlusive use

        case blockOp
            TEST_BLK_PROGRAM:
                bytemove(@block2ForUser, p_source, BLOCK_SIZE)                  ' programming installs the lifecycle and CRC in the image it is given
                flash_program_block(block_address, @block2ForUser, cycle_bits)
            TEST_BLK_ACTIVATE:
                flash_activate_block(block_address, cycle_bits)
            TEST_BLK_CANCEL:
                flash_cancel_block(block_address)
            other:
                flash_read_block_addr(block_address, @firstByte, $000, $000)    ' read first byte of block
                flash_program_bit(block_address, firstByte & !TEST_CORRUPT_BIT) ' clear the reserved bit, nothing else
        status := release_lock(status)                                          ' release the lock, we're done with it

    LONG[@errorCode][cogid()] := status


PUB TEST_refusedBlockCount() : refusedCount
'' TEST METHOD: return the number of block programs this object instance has refused
''
'' The count rises by one each time flash_program_block() or flash_program_bit() is given a block address
'' outside 0..BLOCKS-1; a program refused because the device fault is raised is not counted. It belongs to the
'' object instance, so read it through the instance that made the calls.
''
'' @returns refusedCount - block programs refused so far

    refusedCount := fsRefusedBlocks


PUB TEST_readBelowFsCrc() : status, crc
'' TEST METHOD: read the flash sector just below the file system and return its CRC, a read only
''
'' The sector is relative block TEST_BLOCK_BELOW_FS ($07C000), outside the file system. The read command does
'' not change the flash, so this is safe on any board. The CRC is computed as block_crc() computes it, over the
'' first BLOCK_SIZE - 4 bytes. The lock is created here if no cog has created it yet.
''
'' @returns status - SUCCESS (0) if the sector was read, or E_NO_LOCK_AVAIL if the lock could not be created
'' @returns crc - the CRC of the sector, 0 when status is not SUCCESS

    status := SUCCESS
    crc := 0
    if fsLock == -1                                                             ' don't acquire lock if already have it
        status := setup_semaphore()

    if status == SUCCESS
        repeat while locktry(fsLock) == 0                                       ' lock for exlusive use

        flash_read_block_addr(TEST_BLOCK_BELOW_FS, @blockForUser, $000, BLOCK_SIZE - 1) ' read the whole sector into the buffer
        lockrel(fsLock)                                                         ' release the lock, we're done with it
        crc := block_crc(@blockForUser)

    LONG[@errorCode][cogid()] := status


PUB TEST_programBelowFs(blockOp) : status
'' TEST METHOD: hand relative block TEST_BLOCK_BELOW_FS to a flash programming primitive, which must refuse it
''
'' This exists to prove the range check of flash_program_block() and flash_program_bit(): it calls the primitive
'' directly with a block address outside 0..BLOCKS-1, which TEST_changeBlock() never does. Each call that is
'' refused raises TEST_refusedBlockCount() by one.
''
'' A refusal also raises the device fault, as a flash wait that times out does: every block program is then
'' refused until the next mount() or format() clears it. Called while the file system is NOT mounted, the call
'' returns SUCCESS and the fault waits for that mount(). Called while it is mounted, the call takes the fault exit:
'' it returns E_FLASH_TIMEOUT with the file system unmounted, every later call returns E_NOT_MOUNTED, and mount()
'' recovers it.
''
'' @param blockOp - the primitive: TEST_BLK_PROGRAM calls flash_program_block(), TEST_BLK_CORRUPT calls flash_program_bit()
'' @returns status - SUCCESS (0) if the primitive was called with the file system not mounted, E_FLASH_TIMEOUT if
'' .. it was called with the file system mounted, E_TEST_BAD_BLOCK_ARG if blockOp is neither of those, or
'' .. E_NO_LOCK_AVAIL if the lock could not be created

    status := SUCCESS
    if not lookdown(blockOp : TEST_BLK_PROGRAM, TEST_BLK_CORRUPT)
        status := E_TEST_BAD_BLOCK_ARG                                          ' refuse an operation this method does not have
    elseif fsLock == -1                                                         ' don't acquire lock if already have it
        status := setup_semaphore()

    if status == SUCCESS
        repeat while locktry(fsLock) == 0                                       ' lock for exlusive use

        if blockOp == TEST_BLK_PROGRAM
            flash_program_block(TEST_BLOCK_BELOW_FS, @block2ForUser, 0)
        else
            flash_program_bit(TEST_BLOCK_BELOW_FS, 0)
        status := release_lock(status)                                          ' release the lock, we're done with it

    LONG[@errorCode][cogid()] := status


PUB TEST_armFlashFault(waitCount)
'' TEST METHOD: make a later flash wait report a timeout, or disarm one that is armed
''
'' Armed at waitCount, each flash wait counts the countdown down by one, and the waitCount-th wait from now (1 is
'' the next one) reports a timeout without polling the chip: it raises the device fault, as a chip still busy at
'' the bound would, and disarms the countdown. Every flash erase, page program and lifecycle-bit program has one
'' wait. A waitCount of 0, or below, disarms it. The countdown is shared by every cog. The lock is not taken.
''
'' @param waitCount - the flash wait, counted from 1, that reports the timeout, or 0 to disarm

    fsFaultCountdown := waitCount #> FAULT_OFF


PUB TEST_setElectionCounts(countValue)
'' TEST METHOD: place one count in every entry of the election that decides which cog creates the lock
''
'' The election runs only while no cog has created the lock. Each cog that enters it writes getct() into
'' its own entry, then the cog whose entry is lowest creates the lock and the others wait for it to exist
'' (can_acquire_lock(), setup_semaphore()); on a tie the lower cog number wins. So the entries the other
'' cogs hold decide whether a cog wins: with TEST_COUNT_LOWEST in every entry a cog that enters loses to the
'' lowest-numbered other cog (cog 0 alone could tie and win, when getct() reads $8000_0000 as it enters),
'' and with TEST_COUNT_UNSET in every entry the election is as it is at power-up. Nothing else is changed
'' and the lock is not taken.
''
'' @param countValue - the count to place in all TEST_ELECTION_ENTRIES entries

    longfill(@fsCogCts, countValue, TEST_ELECTION_ENTRIES)


PUB TEST_holdLock() : status
'' TEST METHOD: take the driver's lock and return still holding it
''
'' The calling cog keeps the lock until the next locked method it calls returns: a cog's LOCKTRY of a lock it
'' already holds succeeds, so that method takes the lock at once and releases it at its end. Meanwhile every
'' other cog that calls a locked method waits for the lock. Nothing else is changed.
''
'' @returns status - SUCCESS (0) if the lock is held, E_NOT_MOUNTED if the filesystem is not mounted (the
'' .. lock is not taken then)

    ifnot fsMounted                                                             ' the lock exists once a mount() has created it
        status := E_NOT_MOUNTED
    else
        repeat while locktry(fsLock) == 0                                       ' lock for exlusive use
        status := SUCCESS

    LONG[@errorCode][cogid()] := status


PUB TEST_blockStateOf(block_address) : stateBits
'' TEST METHOD: return the block state the driver's table holds for one block, read without taking the lock
''
'' The table is read as it stands, so a call made while another cog builds the tables in mount() or
'' can_mount() sees the table part way through that build. The table exists once the first mount() or
'' can_mount() has built it.
''
'' @param block_address - the block offset within the file system
'' @returns stateBits - B_FREE, B_TEMP, B_HEAD or B_BODY, or E_TEST_BAD_BLOCK_ARG if block_address is
'' .. outside 0..BLOCKS-1 or no table has been built yet

    if block_address < 0 or block_address > BLOCKS - 1                         ' refuse an address outside the file system
        stateBits := E_TEST_BAD_BLOCK_ARG
    elseif BlockState == 0                                                      ' the field pointer is set by the first table build
        stateBits := E_TEST_BAD_BLOCK_ARG
    else
        stateBits := field[BlockState][block_address]

    LONG[@errorCode][cogid()] := stateBits < 0 ? stateBits : SUCCESS


PUB TEST_skipCreateChecks()
'' TEST METHOD: make the next create_file() call skip its free-ID and free-block checks
''
'' create_file() checks that a block ID and every block the file needs are free before it changes anything. The
'' next create_file() call after this one skips both checks, so a file too big for the free space runs out inside
'' the block loop instead. That call clears the skip, whatever it returns.
''

    fsSkipCreateChecks := TRUE


PUB TEST_setTargetBlock(block_address) : status
'' TEST METHOD: name a block that the block allocations take in place of a random pick
''
'' While a block is named, every block allocation whose free-block check passes takes the named block if its
'' state is not B_TEMP: a free named block becomes the new block and stays named, and a B_HEAD/B_BODY named block
'' is moved to a free block, which clears the name. NOT_ENABLED clears the name. The lock is not taken.
''
'' @param block_address - the block offset within the file system, or NOT_ENABLED
'' @returns status - SUCCESS (0) if the name was set or cleared, E_TEST_BAD_BLOCK_ARG if block_address is neither
'' .. NOT_ENABLED nor inside 0..BLOCKS-1 (the name is then left as it was)

    status := SUCCESS
    if block_address <> NOT_ENABLED and (block_address < 0 or block_address > BLOCKS - 1)
        status := E_TEST_BAD_BLOCK_ARG                                          ' refuse an address outside the file system
    else
        fsTargetBlock := block_address

    LONG[@errorCode][cogid()] := status


PUB TEST_dumpMountMap(pFileBlocks, pFragments): fileLen, badLen | bReady, bFileFound, blockCount, blkIdx, block_address, blockTypeBits, badBlockCount, fileCount, LONG signature[2], bad_count, dupe_count, dupeIdCount
'' TEST METHOD: scan the flash as mount would, without changing any block, and list all findings
''
'' The scan rebuilds the driver's block tables from scratch, so it runs only while the file system is NOT
'' mounted. When the file system is mounted nothing is scanned: both lists come back empty and the result
'' is 0, 0 with error() holding SUCCESS. The tables are ready for use only after can_mount() or mount() has run once.
''
'' @param pFileBlocks - address of place to put list of file blocks (3 longs per entry, 0 ends each file's entries and the list)
'' @param pFragments - address of place to put list of bad blocks (those not in files) (3 longs per entry, 0 ends the list)
'' @returns fileLen - number of files found, or E_NO_LOCK_AVAIL if the lock could not be created
'' @returns badLen - number of bad blocks found

' Local Variables:
' @local bReady - true when the file system is not mounted and the lock is available
' @local bFileFound - true when a head block starts a complete file
' @local blockCount - longs placed in the file list for the file just traced
' @local blkIdx - next free long in the list being filled
' @local block_address - the block offset within the file system
' @local blockTypeBits - first byte of the block being checked
' @local badBlockCount - count of blocks in no file
' @local fileCount - count of files found
' @local signature - first two longs of the block being listed
' @local bad_count - bad blocks found by the check of one block
' @local dupe_count - duplicate IDs found by the check of one block
' @local dupeIdCount - count of duplicate ID blocks found

    fileLen := 0
    badLen := 0
    LONG[pFileBlocks][0] := 0                                                   ' empty lists unless the scan below fills them
    LONG[pFragments][0] := 0
    LONG[@errorCode][cogid()] := SUCCESS                                        ' preset to success

    bReady := not fsMounted                                                     ' mounted: the scan would clobber the live tables
    if bReady and fsLock == -1                                                  ' don't acquire lock if already have it
        if setup_semaphore() < 0
            bReady := false
            fileLen := LONG[@errorCode][cogid()]

    if bReady
        repeat while locktry(fsLock) == 0                                       ' lock for exlusive use

        bytefill(@hStatus, 0, MAX_FILES_OPEN)                                   ' clear handles

        wordfill(@IDToBlocks, 0, ID_TO_BLOCKS_SZ)                               ' clear ID-to-block translation table
        bytefill(@IDValids, 0, FLAGS_SIZE)                                      ' clear ID flags
        bytefill(@BlockStates, 0, STATES_SIZE)                                  ' clear block states to B_FREE

        repeat BLOCKS with block_address                                        ' check each block and count any duplicate IDs
            bad_count, dupe_count := check_block_read_only(block_address)
            badBlockCount += bad_count
            dupeIdCount += dupe_count

        if showRTdebug
            debug("dmm: (1) ", udec(dupeIdCount, badBlockCount))

        repeat BLOCKS with block_address                                        ' trace head blocks and cancel any broken files
            if field[BlockState][block_address] == B_TEMP                       ' is this a valid block?
                flash_read_block_addr(block_address, @blockTypeBits, $000, $000) ' yes, read first byte of block
                ifnot blockTypeBits.[1]                                         ' is this a head block?
                    bFileFound, blockCount := TEST_trace_n_set(block_address, true, @LONG[pFileBlocks][blkIdx])
                    ifnot bFileFound                                            ' yes, trace file, set block states to B_HEAD/B_BODY
                        trace_file_set_flags(block_address, false)              ' if error, retrace file, return block states to B_TEMP
                    else
                        fileCount++
                        blkIdx += blockCount

        LONG[pFileBlocks][blkIdx] := 0
        fileLen := fileCount
        if showRTdebug
            debug("dmm: (2) ", udec(fileCount, blkIdx))

        blkIdx := 0
        badBlockCount := 0
        repeat BLOCKS with block_address                                        ' list B_TEMP blocks that didn't become B_HEAD/B_BODY blocks
            if field[BlockState][block_address] == B_TEMP                       ' is this an B_TEMP block?
                flash_read_block_addr(block_address, @signature, $000, $007)    ' if so, read first long of block to get ID
                field[IDValid][signature.[19..8]]~                              ' ..cancel ID flag (bit := 0)
                field[BlockState][block_address] := B_FREE                      ' ..return block state to B_FREE
                badBlockCount++                                                 ' ..count the block as bad
                LONG[pFragments][blkIdx++] := block_address
                LONG[pFragments][blkIdx++] := signature[0]
                LONG[pFragments][blkIdx++] := signature[1]

        LONG[pFragments][blkIdx] := 0
        badLen := badBlockCount

        if showRTdebug
            debug("dmm: (3) ", udec(badBlockCount, blkIdx))

        lockrel(fsLock)                                                         ' release the lock, we're done with it

pri TEST_trace_n_set(block_address, set, pFileBlocks) : valid, lenLongs | signature[2], block_id

' Trace file chain marking (or clearing) block states until end of file is reached (or an error in block sequence is found)
'
' @param block_address - the block offset within the file system for the block to trace
' @param set - true to set block states to B_HEAD/B_BODY, false to set block states to B_TEMP
' @returns valid - true if file is valid, false if file is invalid

' Local Variables:
' @local signature - block state bits of block being checked
' @local block_id - the blockID of the block being checked
  valid := false
  'if set
  '    debug("tfsf() - ENTRY set")
  'else
  '    debug("tfsf() - ENTRY clear")
  flash_read_block_addr(block_address, @signature, $000, $007)                  'read first long of initial block
  field[BlockState][block_address] := set ? B_HEAD : B_TEMP                     'set first block state to (set-pass: B_HEAD or clear-pass: B_TEMP)
  LONG[pFileBlocks][lenLongs++] := block_address
  LONG[pFileBlocks][lenLongs++] := signature[0]
  LONG[pFileBlocks][lenLongs++] := signature[1]

  repeat BLOCKS                                                                 'limit repeat to BLOCKS in order to return false on endless loop
    ifnot signature.[0]                                                         'if last block, file is complete, return true
      'debug("tfsf() - OK complete file")
      LONG[pFileBlocks][lenLongs++] := 0
      valid := true
      return
    block_id := signature.[31..20]                                              'get "next" ID from this full block
    ifnot field[IDValid][block_id]                                              'if ID invalid (bit == 0), error!, return false
      'debug("tfsf() - BAD next ID is bad")
      return
    block_address := field[IDToBlock][block_id]                                 'get address of block having this ID
    flash_read_block_addr(block_address, @signature, $000, $007)                'read first long of "next" block
    ifnot signature.[1]                                                         'if "next" is head block, error!, return false
      'debug("tfsf() - BAD head within file")
      return
    LONG[pFileBlocks][lenLongs++] := block_address
    LONG[pFileBlocks][lenLongs++] := signature[0]
    LONG[pFileBlocks][lenLongs++] := signature[1]
    field[BlockState][block_address] := set ? B_BODY : B_TEMP                   'set block state to (set-pass: B_BODY or clear-pass: B_TEMP)
  'debug("tfsf() - EXIT at end: out of blocks?!")


' ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
'}

CON ' --- Technical Details ---

{

head/last block
------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
000..003    long {EndPtr[11:0], ThisID[11:0], %vvv11100}    'vvv = lifecycle, 00 = head/last
004..007    long {FilenameCRC19[19:0], DataOffset[11:0]}    'crc of filename and data offset
008..087    byte Filename[127+1]                            'filename z-string
088..FFB    byte Data[3956]                                 'data
FFC..FFF    long CRC32                                      'crc32 of 000..FFB


head/more block
------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
000..003    long {NextID[11:0], ThisID[11:0], %vvv11101}    'vvv = lifecycle, 01 = head/more
004..007    long {FilenameCRC19[19:0], DataOffset[11:0]}    'crc of filename and data offset
008..087    byte Filename[127+1]                            'filename z-string
088..FFB    byte Data[3956]                                 'data
FFC..FFF    long CRC32                                      'crc32 of 000..FFB


body/last block
------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
000..003    long {EndPtr[11:0], ThisID[11:0], %vvv11110}    'vvv = lifecycle, 10 = body/last
004..FFB    byte Data[4088]                                 'data
FFC..FFF    long CRC32                                      'crc32 of 000..FFB


body/more block
------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
000..003    long {NextID[11:0], ThisID[11:0], %vvv11111}    'vvv = lifecycle, 11 = body/more
004..FFB    byte Data[4088]                                 'data
FFC..FFF    long CRC32                                      'crc32 of 000..FFB



vvv lifecycle rules
- single-zero ring counter state sequence is 011..101..110..repeat (akin to "rock, paper, scissors")
- the block with the greater state is the valid block between two blocks with identical IDs
- this allows for make-before-break block replacement that can be recovered after unexpected power loss
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
111                 inactive    no zeroes
011/101/110         active      one zero        rock, paper, scissors
001/010/100/000     canceled    two or three zeroes

011 > 110       new > old   rock > scissors
101 > 011       new > old   paper > rock
110 > 101       new > old   scissors > paper

}


